WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:06.040
On the 13th of October, 1989, the town of
Danner, Wisconsin, was shaken by a seismic

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:09.350
event unlike anything they'd ever experienced.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:14.019
This might have been written off as an earthquake,
were it not for one disturbing factor - the

00:00:14.019 --> 00:00:18.970
ground shaking event was accompanied by a
huge spike of radioactivity.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:23.580
With the strange phenomenon happening a month
before the Berlin Wall was torn down, during

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:29.019
a period of the Cold War that historians call
“The Year of Crisis”, it’s easy to understand

00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:32.529
why the people of Danner immediately assumed
the worst.

00:00:32.529 --> 00:00:37.469
But the huge eruption they felt wasn't the
result of a nuclear bomb going off.

00:00:37.469 --> 00:00:41.190
The SCP Foundation was alerted to the event
in Danner when they picked up a series of

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:44.890
radio transmissions coming from just outside
the town.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:50.679
When they arrived, they found something incredible,
like something out of a sci-fi movie.

00:00:50.679 --> 00:00:55.570
Standing at the quake's epicenter, was a creature
that looked to be from another world.

00:00:55.570 --> 00:01:01.249
Standing 2 meters tall and weighing almost
300 kilograms, the being was green and brown

00:01:01.249 --> 00:01:03.480
in color, with a bulky, humanoid body.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:08.070
It’s head was a different story though,
and resembled a gigantic housefly, with a

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:11.600
proboscis and huge, stereoscopic eyes.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:15.930
Surprisingly, the strange creature did not
immediately go on a rampage.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:24.570
Instead, the being - designated SCP-2273 - appeared
to be exhausted, injured, and extremely malnourished.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:30.490
It offered no resistance at all to the Foundation
containment team and it was taken to Site-17

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.490
without conflict.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:36.470
While the SCP Foundation is no stranger to
visitors from other worlds, there was something

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:40.250
especially unusual about this supposed alien
invader.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:44.270
The doctors who examined the creature and
treated its injuries found an appendage that

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:49.810
seemed to function as an organic radio transmitter,
and large open wounds on its shoulder blades

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:53.680
and forearms where further appendages had
been ripped off.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:59.290
Additionally, while its insect-like exoskeleton
was mostly a uniform green and brown pattern,

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:04.350
the creature's upper arms and torso were dotted
with a variety of scars and markings that,

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:08.229
on closer inspection, looked like military
badges.

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:12.200
Was this some kind of wounded intergalactic
soldier who had been stranded on Earth?

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:17.370
If it was, then how were the organic badges
on this alien's exoskeleton a near perfect

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:21.950
match to military badges worn by soldiers
in the Soviet Union?

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:25.980
Even if they did reference a unit that didn’t
officially exist within the Soviet army.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:32.760
The scientists were sure, this alien wasn't
an alien at all… underneath its exoskeleton

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:35.880
was a non-anomalous human being.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:41.280
If that was true, then this was even more
terrifying than an extraterrestrial visitor.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:46.880
The scientists were sure the USSR had developed
a new kind of organic armor, and this anomaly

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:52.390
showing up in Wisconsin was the result of
a test on US soil that had gone wrong.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:57.510
If that was the case, then there was no telling
how many more of these exoskeletons were out

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.170
there and would need to be contained.

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:03.380
The Foundation had to act quickly and find
out more.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:09.040
While SCP-2273 was recovering, they called
in Dr. Friedritch, an on-site psychologist

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.670
who could speak several languages including
Russian.

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:16.900
Dr. Friedritch would be tasked with interrogating
the SCP on his origins and the nature of the

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:17.900
suit.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:22.480
The interview was conducted via AM radio from
a separate observation chamber, as the biological

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:27.980
transmitter seemed to be SCP-2273's only method
of communication.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:35.069
The interview began with Dr. Friedritch speaking
to SCP-2273 in Russian, only for 2273 to respond

00:03:35.069 --> 00:03:39.940
that Dr. Friedritch’s accent was atrocious
and requesting he use German instead.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:46.459
SCP-2273 who, according to the organic military
patches on his body, was named Major Alexei

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:49.599
Belitrov, initially resisted being interviewed.

00:03:49.599 --> 00:03:54.239
He believed that he was a prisoner of war,
being held by the American military.

00:03:54.239 --> 00:03:58.239
According to him, he had been in the middle
of battle, and that the Americans had killed

00:03:58.239 --> 00:04:01.340
his men and left him for dead in the wilderness.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:05.530
Nothing that Dr. Friedritch told him - that
there was no war, or that the Foundation was

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:10.569
not affiliated with the US government - could
convince him otherwise and he refused to talk

00:04:10.569 --> 00:04:11.730
further.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:16.661
Before a second interview was conducted, Belitrov
was given an old copy of the Level 1 Researcher

00:04:16.661 --> 00:04:21.810
General Debrief, as a way of helping him further
understand the nature of the Foundation and

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:23.379
his containment.

00:04:23.379 --> 00:04:26.990
Belitrov was more co-operative after that,
though the realization that he would most

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:31.560
likely be kept in containment for the rest
of his life caused him great distress and

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:35.139
he was unwilling to speak to Dr. Friedritch
for another three days.

00:04:35.139 --> 00:04:40.110
Dr. Friedritch didn’t give up though, and
when Belitrov finally opened up to the doctor,

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:43.389
he began to tell him more and more.

00:04:43.389 --> 00:04:47.699
Belitrov told the doctor that when he was
a child, Russia was hit by an American nuclear

00:04:47.699 --> 00:04:51.289
warhead, and that the Soviet Union immediately
retaliated.

00:04:51.289 --> 00:04:56.759
The resulting nuclear conflict, which Belitrov
called The War to End the World, caused massive

00:04:56.759 --> 00:05:00.819
devastation and left most of the planet dangerously
irradiated.

00:05:00.819 --> 00:05:03.150
That’s why he had the exoskeleton.

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:08.169
It was to shield him from the radiation and
allow him to survive above ground.

00:05:08.169 --> 00:05:13.569
Unfortunately, Belitrov knew very little about
how the suit was made or how it worked, saying

00:05:13.569 --> 00:05:18.210
that it was built by “the engineers”,
and that it grew naturally over a period of

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:19.639
several years.

00:05:19.639 --> 00:05:22.319
But Belitrov hadn’t made the decision himself.

00:05:22.319 --> 00:05:26.740
It was his parents who had volunteered him
as a test subject for the exoskeleton suit

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:31.699
program when he was still young, hoping it
would give him a better chance at survival.

00:05:31.699 --> 00:05:36.419
The process of bonding the exoskeleton to
the human body was extremely painful, but

00:05:36.419 --> 00:05:40.599
according to Belitrov, its advantages far
outweighed the pain.

00:05:40.599 --> 00:05:46.270
The suit not only helped him survive in a
nuclear wasteland, but made him a better soldier.

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:52.430
The suit allowed him to lift and carry up
to 1200 kilograms, gave him stereoscopic vision,

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:57.119
and the organic radio transmitter allowed
him to communicate with other soldiers across

00:05:57.119 --> 00:06:02.250
long distances, as well as listen in on encrypted
enemy transmissions.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:06.490
The wounds on his shoulders and arms, where
it looked like appendages had been ripped

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:11.180
out, were where his weapons and supply packs
had previously been mounted.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:14.611
Belitrov had been stationed with his men in
the area he was discovered when they were

00:06:14.611 --> 00:06:16.430
attacked by American soldiers.

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:21.659
The soldiers had ripped off Belitrov's weapons
and supply pack, and did the same to all of

00:06:21.659 --> 00:06:22.659
his men as well.

00:06:22.659 --> 00:06:27.409
They were all shot, with Belitrov being spared
for the moment only because the Americans

00:06:27.409 --> 00:06:29.960
had identified him as the commanding officer.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:35.110
Suddenly, there was a bright flash of light,
and the American soldiers vanished.

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:40.879
Not only that, but the landscape changed - where
there had been a post-nuclear wasteland before,

00:06:40.879 --> 00:06:43.300
now there were lush green trees.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:48.300
Injured and disoriented, Belitrov began sending
distress signals, only to have those signals

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:49.749
intercepted by the SCP Foundation.

00:06:49.749 --> 00:06:55.930
The most interesting part of Belitrov's story,
as far as the Foundation was concerned, came

00:06:55.930 --> 00:07:00.770
during his fourth interview, when Dr. Friedritch
asked him about the engineers who had designed

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:02.590
the exoskeleton suit.

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:07.059
In Belitrov's own words - “They weren't
truly known to Man until the years of the

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:09.119
Great War and the Revolution.

00:07:09.119 --> 00:07:13.990
The French found them, in buried cities where
the Western Allies were digging their trenches.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:18.430
Eventually, they were made to build weapons
for the war, by both sides.”

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:24.219
By his description, these engineers didn't
sound human, but they were by no means unknown

00:07:24.219 --> 00:07:26.860
to the SCP Foundation.

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:31.479
Belitrov described the engineers as humanoid,
nocturnal, covered in fur, and possessing

00:07:31.479 --> 00:07:35.419
technology and intelligence far beyond that
of any human.

00:07:35.419 --> 00:07:39.279
Those familiar with the Foundation's history
might already know the engineers by their

00:07:39.279 --> 00:07:46.800
Foundation designation of SCP-1000, or their
more commonly known name - Bigfoot.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:52.869
A quick rundown: SCP-1000 are a species of
intelligent humanoid primates that lived alongside

00:07:52.869 --> 00:07:57.990
humanity in highly advanced cities until their
own technology was turned against them.

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:02.360
Not only were their cities wiped off the face
of the earth, but 70 percent of their population

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:07.050
was slaughtered, and the survivors were driven
mad to the point that their mental faculties

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:11.539
were no higher than those of a chimpanzee
or gorilla.

00:08:11.539 --> 00:08:15.809
The SCP Foundation is tasked with keeping
them away from human contact, in fear of what

00:08:15.809 --> 00:08:20.879
the creatures would be able to do to humanity
if they ever regained their memories and full

00:08:20.879 --> 00:08:26.719
mental function and rumors have been spread
about them possessing deadly anomalous properties.

00:08:26.719 --> 00:08:32.860
But evidently, the destruction of the SCP-1000
species never occurred in Belitrov's universe,

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:35.649
or if it did, it wasn't nearly as complete.

00:08:35.649 --> 00:08:41.240
In that timeline, humanity regained contact
with SCP-1000 after discovering their underground

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:43.729
cities sometime during World War One.

00:08:43.729 --> 00:08:48.160
After this discovery, both the Allied and
Axis powers began recruiting them to build

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:52.790
weapons, and their weapons played a role in
both the Russian Revolution and the second

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:53.790
world war.

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:58.430
It was because of these technological advantages
that the Cold War escalated into what would

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:01.490
become the war to end all wars.

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:06.440
Both sides were armed with not only nuclear
warheads, but highly advanced, radiation-proof

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:11.300
exoskeleton armor that allowed the conflict
to continue even after the total destruction

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:12.480
of the planet.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:17.850
While the humans fought above ground, life
continued as normal for SCP-1000 in their

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:19.420
underground cities.

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:24.680
As Belitrov noted, they never wore the armor
themselves, as they had no need to venture

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:25.810
above ground.

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:30.279
“Only soldiers wear armor, and this is not
their war.”

00:09:30.279 --> 00:09:35.620
Belitrov continued to adjust to life in containment
and sitting for regular interviews with Dr.

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:36.620
Friedritch.

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:40.940
He was given the rations provided for humanoid
anomalies, but in much larger quantities,

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:45.930
as the suit required him to eat around 8000
calories a day to keep it functioning.

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:50.250
Belitrov also began taking advantage of his
ability to access the Foundation's library

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:55.910
- he would often read, or listen to classical
music, particularly by the Russian composer

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:56.910
Tchaikovsky.

00:09:56.910 --> 00:10:02.360
He seemed especially fond of reading The Time
Machine by HG Wells, no surprise given he

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:06.930
was able to directly relate to the experience
of living through an apocalypse and being

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:11.319
transported to a strange timeline with no
way to return home.

00:10:11.319 --> 00:10:16.620
But with little else to occupy his time, Belitrov
began to display symptoms consistent with

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:21.410
post-traumatic stress disorder, reporting
in his now regular interviews with Dr. Friedritch

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:25.810
that he was constantly reliving memories of
the battles he'd fought and the lives he had

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:27.350
taken in combat.

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:30.389
The suit was making the problem worse too,
it seemed.

00:10:30.389 --> 00:10:35.660
It was as if he could never forget, as one
of its features was an ability to store and

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:37.190
replay memories.

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:41.639
This feature was intended as a strategic aid
that would allow commanding officers to more

00:10:41.639 --> 00:10:47.149
effectively gather and process information
about their surroundings, but outside of combat,

00:10:47.149 --> 00:10:53.510
this only served to force Belitrov into reliving
his most painful memories again and again.

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:58.210
Every night as he tried to sleep, he would
see the faces of his men, their weapons torn

00:10:58.210 --> 00:11:03.840
from their exoskeletons, laying in the dirt
after being gunned down by the enemy.

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:09.160
Like many veterans, Belitrov was being hit
all at once with the harsh realities of war.

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:13.790
Now that his brain wasn't solely focused on
keeping him alive, it had time to process

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:15.920
all the horrors he'd experienced.

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:21.250
He told Dr. Friedritch- “I trained alongside
these men for years before they put us back

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:24.519
on the surface, since we were all young children.

00:11:24.519 --> 00:11:25.779
We were brothers.

00:11:25.779 --> 00:11:29.900
And I gave the order to surrender, and…
got them killed.

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:32.250
I should have died with them.”

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:40.980
While the story of SCP-2273 ends here, the
story of Alexei Belitrov, SCP-2273-1, continues.

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:47.730
In 2018, Belitrov was allowed passage to Volgograd,
Russia, as part of an Anomaly Reintegration

00:11:47.730 --> 00:11:48.730
program.

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:52.230
While he was unable to secure employment within
the Russian government as he had hoped, he

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:57.000
eventually was taken in by a monastery and
continued to write letters to Dr. Friedritch

00:11:57.000 --> 00:12:00.870
until Friedritch's eventual death from lymphoma-related
complications.

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:05.800
There’s plenty more on the monastery, the
Anomaly Reintegration program, and what happened

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:10.439
to Major Belitrov when he returned to Russia,
but that'll have to be a story for another

00:12:10.439 --> 00:12:11.990
day.

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:18.100
The year was 1857, and the Second Opium War
was raging between China and the combined

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:23.300
forces of the English and French. It was one
of the many bloody colonial wars fought over

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:30.370
resources like tea, sugar, and the intoxicating
opium poppy. It was a war fought by peasants

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:35.560
and noblemen alike. One of these aristocratic
soldiers was the noble Lord Theodore Thomas

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:41.380
Blackwood, the quintessential English gentleman
and explorer. While his fellow soldiers cowered

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:46.480
behind cover, Lord Blackwood charged into
the fray, shouldering his rifle and firing

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:48.899
his pistol into the crowd of opposing soldiers.

00:12:48.899 --> 00:12:54.180
It was the Battle of Canton, one of the most
crucial battles of the entire conflict. The

00:12:54.180 --> 00:12:59.100
French and English were laying siege to the
city of Canton, also known as Guangzhou, to

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:03.600
prove their military dominance and capture
an important Chinese government official.

00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:08.000
Lord Blackwood led the charge on horseback.
Every bullet seemed to find the heart of a

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:15.279
foe. He was a true hero among men; a gentleman
warrior with class, refinement, and style.

00:13:15.279 --> 00:13:19.779
And it would be thanks to his expert leadership
and marksmanship on the field that the allied

00:13:19.779 --> 00:13:23.129
European forces won the battle decisively.

00:13:23.129 --> 00:13:27.079
Lord Theodore Thomas Blackwood is a name that
deserves to be counted among Lord

00:13:27.079 --> 00:13:32.879
Horatio Nelson, Sir Francis Bacon, and Sir
Walter Raleigh. In addition to being a skilled

00:13:32.879 --> 00:13:39.319
and honorable fighter, Lord Blackwood is an
consummate explorer, naturalist, and frontiersman.

00:13:39.319 --> 00:13:43.950
During his heyday, he traveled perhaps further
than any man across the known and unknown

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:49.319
corners of the globe. He made scientific,
biological, and anthropological discoveries

00:13:49.319 --> 00:13:54.870
that should have reset the course of society
forever. And yet, you won’t find any records

00:13:54.870 --> 00:14:00.389
in the history books of Lord Theodore Thomas
Blackwood. Nor will you find any grand oil

00:14:00.389 --> 00:14:03.620
paintings, or dedicated wings in British museums.

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:09.370
This is because Lord Theodore Thomas Blackwood…
is a four and a half inch, telepathic neon

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:15.100
sea slug. And he’s known to the SCP Foundation,
as SCP-1867.

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:22.339
While he would never admit to it, Lord Blackwood
belongs to the species Nembrotha kubaryana,

00:14:22.339 --> 00:14:27.600
also known as the variable neon slug. He’s
kept in a standard aquarium in a Foundation

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:33.480
containment site, and is physically no different
to any other member of his species. What makes

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:39.900
Lord Blackwood unique is his powerful telepathic
abilities - specifically, the power to communicate

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:45.860
by speaking directly into people’s minds.
And what’s more, he’s extremely talkative.

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:52.330
But to what extent is anything that this anomalous
sea slug says true? Or is he just like SCP-082,

00:14:52.330 --> 00:14:57.180
Fernand the Cannibal - a creative and pathological
liar.

00:14:57.180 --> 00:15:01.870
It isn’t committed to record how exactly
the Foundation discovered Lord Blackwood.

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:05.760
Perhaps a local aquarium worker worried they
were going insane when they heard the voice

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:10.509
of a nineteenth century English nobleman ringing
in their ears whenever they were cleaning

00:15:10.509 --> 00:15:16.570
algae out of the tank. Maybe Lord Blackwood
was found by SCP Foundation divers, who are

00:15:16.570 --> 00:15:20.910
constantly combing the ocean for anomalous
creatures and activity. What we do know is

00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:26.540
that Lord Blackwood is an incredibly strange
and mysterious individual. He claims to have

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:32.339
visited locations all around the world, and
encountered rare societies and creatures.

00:15:32.339 --> 00:15:37.040
The Foundation was skeptical about a number
of Lord Blackwood’s more outlandish claims,

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:41.259
on account of him being a sea slug, but he
does appear to have the knowledge to back

00:15:41.259 --> 00:15:46.220
up his supposed experience. Interviews with
Lord Blackwood have shown that he’s extremely

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:52.790
knowledgeable in the areas of geography, zoology,
botany, archaeology, anthropology and linguistics

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:58.490
relating to his claimed regions of exploration,
as well as more esoteric fields such as obscure

00:15:58.490 --> 00:16:04.580
mythology, mysticism, and cryptozoology. In
other words, if Lord Blackwood hadn’t gone

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:08.740
on his escapades around the globe throughout
history, how would he come to possess this

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:10.850
wide variety of information?

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:15.339
The Foundation was getting frustrated, and
began to probe further into the personal life

00:16:15.339 --> 00:16:20.990
of the most interesting gastropod in containment.
Lord Blackwood, under questioning, was always

00:16:20.990 --> 00:16:25.899
polite and amicable with Foundation staff.
He seemed to display no real knowledge of

00:16:25.899 --> 00:16:31.149
the fact that he himself was a sea slug - going
as far to accuse other people of being crazy

00:16:31.149 --> 00:16:35.300
or drunk when they brought the fact up to
him. While none of Lord Blackwood’s tall

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:40.920
tales ever extend past the year 1910, he told
fanciful stories of exploring the Americas,

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:45.180
and of his involvement in the Second Opium
War on the side of the English.

00:16:45.180 --> 00:16:49.959
Naturally, the Foundation wanted proof. When
they pressured Lord Blackwood on this, something

00:16:49.959 --> 00:16:54.870
even stranger happened: He gave it. The Lord
told his interviewers that he would happily

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:59.420
donate his collection to them, if it gave
them cause to believe what he was saying.

00:16:59.420 --> 00:17:04.250
He gave the baffled Foundation researchers
the address of a cottage in England where

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:09.600
they could find the secrets to his bizarre
and mysterious past, and local agents in the

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:11.900
area followed up on the information.

00:17:11.900 --> 00:17:16.920
Upon investigation, Foundation Field Agents
did indeed find the cottage that Lord Blackwood

00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:21.820
had specified. It was being maintained by
an extremely old woman. When questioned about

00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:26.050
her presence there, she said that she was
“keeping the house for Lord Blackwood”,

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:31.830
and gave no more useful information. Incidentally,
it appeared that this singular purpose was

00:17:31.830 --> 00:17:36.760
all that this old woman was living for. She
abruptly passed away from heart failure five

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:41.360
days after the Foundation commandeered the
cottage. Whether anything truly anomalous

00:17:41.360 --> 00:17:44.290
caused this, we still don’t know.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:48.870
At first, the cottage seemed normal, until
the Field Agents discovered a secret basement

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:53.900
housing Lord Blackwood’s “collection.”
They were amazed at what they saw: The basement

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:59.960
consisted of zoological and botanical specimens,
over three thousand artifacts, a library containing

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:06.150
over five thousand items, and a functioning
1800s scientific laboratory. It took around

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:10.310
three weeks for Foundation agents working
round the clock in shifts to remove all the

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:16.670
items from Lord Blackwood’s mysterious collection,
and what they found raised even more questions.

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:22.860
The collection included, but was by no means
limited to: 116 unknown species of plants,

00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:29.780
107 unknown species of insects, 28 unknown
species of lizards, 23 unknown species of

00:18:29.780 --> 00:18:36.110
fish, 14 unknown species of amphibians, 12
unknown species of mammals, Fossils pertaining

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:41.330
to 8 unknown species of dinosaur, Fossils
pertaining to 12 unknown species of prehistoric

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:48.620
mammal, and Artifacts belonging to 29 unknown
indigenous societies. That’s a lot of unknowns!

00:18:48.620 --> 00:18:53.900
But wait, there’s more! His collection also
contained a collection of seemingly unknown

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:58.871
firearms, including three wide-bore muskets
marked as “Dr. B. T. Moth’s Effective

00:18:58.871 --> 00:19:04.340
Particle Destabilizers.” Detailed globes
of Mercury, Venus, Mars, and the Galilean

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:10.730
moons, accompanied by notes detailing possible
paths of surface exploration. A heavily modified

00:19:10.730 --> 00:19:14.890
carriage, containing instruments of unknown
purpose. A note attached to the door reads

00:19:14.890 --> 00:19:19.710
“On the fritz. Speak with Henry.” And
a highly dangerous and seemingly anomalous

00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:24.840
machine that killed four Foundation Field
Agents before it was destroyed on site. And

00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:28.310
when questioned about this little fiasco,
Lord Blackwood responded:

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:32.250
“I did warn you to be careful around my
collection. That bloody thing nearly took

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:34.740
my head off back in ninety-seven when I found
it.”

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:38.900
However, there was one thing recovered from
Lord Blackwood’s collection that was perhaps

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:45.580
more interesting than all the others: 35 hand-written
journals containing recordings of events described

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:50.910
by Lord Blackwood in his grandiose tall tales
to the Foundation researchers. The accounts

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:55.530
are generally identical to the stories he
had told, save for some slight variations

00:19:55.530 --> 00:20:00.760
and exaggerations on the part of Blackwood
in the re-telling. Most interestingly of all,

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:05.150
all of these journals have been dated to the
appropriate time period of the events described

00:20:05.150 --> 00:20:07.130
by Foundation scientists.

00:20:07.130 --> 00:20:11.440
While his stories are too numerous to all
be shared here, there’s one that perfectly

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:17.500
sums them all up: Lord Blackwood’s account
of a possible encounter with SCP - 1000, also

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:21.280
known as Bigfoot, in Seattle during the mid-1800s.

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:25.680
Lord Blackwood, seeking to explore the so-called
“new world” of North America, embarked

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:30.410
with an assistant and an indigenous American
guide to the Pacific Northwest, in search

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:36.400
of the legendary Sasquatch. The trio was headed
for Mount Rainier, then known as Tahoma. During

00:20:36.400 --> 00:20:40.570
the journey, Lord Blackwood found a young
fox caught in a trap that had been set by

00:20:40.570 --> 00:20:46.170
a local tribe. He took sympathy on the animal
and freed it, allowing it to run away to safety.

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:50.330
That night, he and his assistant met up with
the rest of his guide’s tribe, and they

00:20:50.330 --> 00:20:55.100
settled down for the evening. However, things
took a disastrous turn when the camp was raided

00:20:55.100 --> 00:21:00.390
by a rival tribe. Almost everyone was slaughtered
in the process, and Lord Blackwood and his

00:21:00.390 --> 00:21:05.950
two companions were hauled away by the enemy
tribe for a sinister purpose: Sacrifice to

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:08.030
a violent local deity.

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:12.810
As it turns out, the creature that this tribe
worshipped was the very same one Lord Blackwood

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:19.060
and the others were trying to find: A particularly
large and aggressive Sasquatch. Each night,

00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:24.400
a different sacrifice was made to the Sasquatch.
The victim would be placed near a forest clearing

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:28.830
while the tribe played a primal song, and
the Sasquatch would emerge from the trees

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:35.200
to devour its prey. The first night it ate
the assistant, the next night it ate the guide.

00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:40.130
And then, it became time for the sacrifice
of Lord Blackwood himself.

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:45.890
As Blackwood was presented for sacrifice,
he accepted his fate. But instead of the Sasquatch,

00:21:45.890 --> 00:21:51.591
a legion of woodland animals emerged from
the trees - foxes, elks, raccoons, and more

00:21:51.591 --> 00:21:56.360
- themselves painted with tribal symbols.
The animals seemed to be on Lord Blackwood’s

00:21:56.360 --> 00:22:00.580
side, and attacked the tribespeople who had
been holding him captive giving Blackwood

00:22:00.580 --> 00:22:05.390
the chance to flee into the forest during
the chaos. Later, these same animals would

00:22:05.390 --> 00:22:10.100
find Blackwood again, and present him with
the things his captors had stolen from him.

00:22:10.100 --> 00:22:15.300
An elder fox also gave him a letter, proclaiming
him a knight of their people now. He was allowed

00:22:15.300 --> 00:22:19.750
safe passage back to a nearby settlement,
at which point he wrote to his financiers

00:22:19.750 --> 00:22:24.350
back in England, explaining the situation
and asking for more money to perform further

00:22:24.350 --> 00:22:29.670
expeditions into the Tahoma region. The whole
incident had only increased his thirst for

00:22:29.670 --> 00:22:32.330
adventure and exploration.

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:38.170
Whether this tale is actually true, or just
a bizarre, colonial fantasy from the pathological

00:22:38.170 --> 00:22:44.790
mind of a telepathic sea slug, we may never
know - but it doesn’t make it any less interesting.

00:22:44.790 --> 00:22:50.080
To this day, Lord Blackwood continues to be
a perplexing but fascinating anomaly. He may

00:22:50.080 --> 00:22:54.650
not be the most dangerous, and he may not
be the most useful, either, but there’s

00:22:54.650 --> 00:22:59.150
no denying that perhaps we’d all like to
sit next to his tank for a couple hours one

00:22:59.150 --> 00:23:04.290
day, and hear him spin a good yarn over a
warm cup of tea.

00:23:04.290 --> 00:23:05.760
Welcome back, Comrade.

00:23:05.760 --> 00:23:12.740
The case of SCP-2273 - also known as Major
Alexei Belitrov - has sparked your imagination,

00:23:12.740 --> 00:23:14.870
and you need to know more.

00:23:14.870 --> 00:23:19.290
But even if you’re not familiar with the
Major, his story, all you need to know is

00:23:19.290 --> 00:23:23.380
that it’s one of war, tragedy, and alternate
dimensions.

00:23:23.380 --> 00:23:30.410
He first appeared in the town of Danner, Wisconsin,
on the 13th of October, 1989, during an unprecedented

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:31.940
seismic event.

00:23:31.940 --> 00:23:37.030
When he was first discovered, the Foundation
researchers assumed that he was an extraterrestrial

00:23:37.030 --> 00:23:40.730
being, on account of his advanced organic
exoskeleton.

00:23:40.730 --> 00:23:45.790
In a surprising move for such an imposing
creature, Belitrov gave himself up to Foundation

00:23:45.790 --> 00:23:47.860
Agents without a fight.

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:53.460
Major Belitrov was then impounded in Foundation
containment Site 17, where he was interrogated

00:23:53.460 --> 00:23:54.460
thoroughly.

00:23:54.460 --> 00:23:58.640
Over a series of interviews, the Foundation
ascertained that Belitrov came from an alternate

00:23:58.640 --> 00:24:03.490
timeline where Russia and the US are locked
in a so-called “War To End The World”,

00:24:03.490 --> 00:24:07.390
thanks to advanced military technology given
to them by SCP-1000.

00:24:07.390 --> 00:24:13.860
Belitrov had narrowly escaped execution at
the hands of American soldiers, and appeared

00:24:13.860 --> 00:24:14.940
in our timeline.

00:24:14.940 --> 00:24:20.020
Now, he’s a prisoner of the advanced suit
that formerly kept him alive.

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:21.900
But his story isn’t over.

00:24:21.900 --> 00:24:27.080
This last remnant of a cold-war-turned-hot
has plenty left to teach us.

00:24:27.080 --> 00:24:31.170
Something that you need to understand about
the SCP Foundation before we go any further

00:24:31.170 --> 00:24:36.520
is that it doesn’t only exist in every nation
across the globe, it also exists in every

00:24:36.520 --> 00:24:39.150
splinter-reality across the multiverse.

00:24:39.150 --> 00:24:44.630
And these splinter realities offer a countless
multitude of tales - of different places,

00:24:44.630 --> 00:24:46.730
different people, and different times.

00:24:46.730 --> 00:24:51.760
Today’s tale concerns Major Belitrov’s
future, in a universe where the secrecy of

00:24:51.760 --> 00:24:57.350
the Foundation is broken, and the anomalous
world needs to find a way to fit in with our

00:24:57.350 --> 00:24:58.350
own.

00:24:58.350 --> 00:25:00.280
The year was 2018.

00:25:00.280 --> 00:25:05.050
Like many humanoid anomalies that the Foundation
was holding in this timeline, Belitrov was

00:25:05.050 --> 00:25:06.870
released from containment.

00:25:06.870 --> 00:25:12.330
He was no longer an SCP, he was now a mere
Person of Interest, free to move around as

00:25:12.330 --> 00:25:13.330
he pleased.

00:25:13.330 --> 00:25:17.980
But this didn’t mean Belitrov was about
to enjoy a quiet life on easy street - he

00:25:17.980 --> 00:25:22.530
was still an inter dimensional refugee from
a broken alternate world.

00:25:22.530 --> 00:25:27.630
Thankfully, there was a certain group willing
to help: The Manna Charitable Foundation.

00:25:27.630 --> 00:25:32.070
This anomalous charity has been involved in
a number of strange cases investigated by

00:25:32.070 --> 00:25:37.120
the Foundation before, and now, they were
going to lend a hand to Major Belitrov.

00:25:37.120 --> 00:25:42.390
Thanks to their Anomaly Reintegration Project,
Manna was able to transport Belitrov back

00:25:42.390 --> 00:25:44.670
to his home of Volgograd in Russia.

00:25:44.670 --> 00:25:50.170
There, he became something of a national celebrity,
making headlines across the country, sitting

00:25:50.170 --> 00:25:55.670
down for interviews on every Russian talk
show, and even being offered book deals.

00:25:55.670 --> 00:26:00.450
But as a former military man, Belitrov was
eager to return to government life and run

00:26:00.450 --> 00:26:01.840
for a government position.

00:26:01.840 --> 00:26:04.650
However, this ambition didn’t go far.

00:26:04.650 --> 00:26:09.730
Belitrov was rejected by all the government
bodies he applied to: Even Vladimir Putin

00:26:09.730 --> 00:26:15.350
wasn’t eccentric enough to want an insectoid
cyborg from another dimension in his cabinet.

00:26:15.350 --> 00:26:18.610
Belitrov endured a rough two years in Volgograd.

00:26:18.610 --> 00:26:23.111
He was treated more like a sideshow freak
than a human being - people didn’t want

00:26:23.111 --> 00:26:27.940
to rent apartments to him, and he was never
able to find permanent employment.

00:26:27.940 --> 00:26:30.540
Even entry level jobs rejected him.

00:26:30.540 --> 00:26:35.010
Nobody wanted to get food served to them by
what looked to be a seven foot monster, and

00:26:35.010 --> 00:26:40.190
he seemed equally ill-suited to helping Russian
women find the right perfume in department

00:26:40.190 --> 00:26:41.190
stores.

00:26:41.190 --> 00:26:44.880
In April of 2020, Belitrov had finally had
enough.

00:26:44.880 --> 00:26:49.710
He contacted the Manna Charitable Foundation
once again and asked to be relocated.

00:26:49.710 --> 00:26:55.110
They told him that some religious institutions
in the area, including the Eastern Clockwork

00:26:55.110 --> 00:26:59.550
Orthodox Church, were accepting and housing
anomalous refugees.

00:26:59.550 --> 00:27:04.980
Not long after this, Belitrov truly fell off
of the SCP Foundation’s radar.

00:27:04.980 --> 00:27:09.810
But one former Foundation operative was well
aware of Major Belitrov’s fate.

00:27:09.810 --> 00:27:11.230
It’s 2021.

00:27:11.230 --> 00:27:16.660
Dr. Friedrich, the Site-17 Anomaly Psychologist
who’d conducted all the initial interviews

00:27:16.660 --> 00:27:22.340
with Belitrov all the way back in 1989, started
receiving letters from him.

00:27:22.340 --> 00:27:26.770
There was no indication as to his true location,
and they appeared to have been handled by

00:27:26.770 --> 00:27:31.360
a Manna Charitable Foundation Mail Carrier
in Russia, but Dr. Friedrich was happy to

00:27:31.360 --> 00:27:33.750
hear from an old friend nonetheless.

00:27:33.750 --> 00:27:38.860
Due to a career of working near highly radioactive
anomalies like Belitrov, Dr. Friedrich was

00:27:38.860 --> 00:27:41.110
suffering from terminal lymphoma.

00:27:41.110 --> 00:27:45.630
It seemed almost like an act of divine providence
that Belitrov’s letters would come to him

00:27:45.630 --> 00:27:47.380
so close to the end.

00:27:47.380 --> 00:27:51.930
The two began a correspondence, and it was
only after Dr. Friedrich’s eventual death

00:27:51.930 --> 00:27:55.570
that the letters came to the SCP Foundation’s
attention.

00:27:55.570 --> 00:28:00.500
It was from this final correspondence that
the Foundation was able to answer the big

00:28:00.500 --> 00:28:04.310
question: Whatever happened to Major Alexei
Belitrov?

00:28:04.310 --> 00:28:08.440
In his first letter to Dr. Friedrich, Belitrov
thanked him profusely.

00:28:08.440 --> 00:28:13.450
He knew that Dr. Friedrich had been a crucial
part of him gaining freedom from the Foundation,

00:28:13.450 --> 00:28:18.340
and credited the therapeutic techniques taught
to him by Dr. Friedrich with keeping him alive,

00:28:18.340 --> 00:28:21.060
and sane, to this day.

00:28:21.060 --> 00:28:26.900
Belitrov expressed a mix of amazement at this
brave new world and a sense of profound weariness.

00:28:26.900 --> 00:28:32.450
As a man eternally locked into a weapon of
war, he felt unsuited to a world in peacetime.

00:28:32.450 --> 00:28:36.710
He almost missed the scorched, irradiated
Russia of his home dimension.

00:28:36.710 --> 00:28:39.690
But most of all, he missed Site-17.

00:28:39.690 --> 00:28:41.100
He missed Dr. Friedrich.

00:28:41.100 --> 00:28:47.800
He missed some of his fellow anomalies, like
SCP-507, the Teleporting Man, and SCP-163,

00:28:47.800 --> 00:28:48.890
the Space Crab.

00:28:48.890 --> 00:28:52.340
He even missed the simplicity of being contained.

00:28:52.340 --> 00:28:54.860
He hoped that Dr. Friedrich would write back.

00:28:54.860 --> 00:28:59.650
In his second letter, Belitrov began detailing
his experience with the Eastern Clockwork

00:28:59.650 --> 00:29:00.880
Orthodox Church.

00:29:00.880 --> 00:29:05.840
Despite growing up in a highly atheistic Communist
environment, Belitrov became enamored with

00:29:05.840 --> 00:29:07.110
the ways of the Church.

00:29:07.110 --> 00:29:12.080
He found them to be highly accepting of him,
in spite of his unfortunate circumstances.

00:29:12.080 --> 00:29:16.860
They displayed a freedom in their faith that
Belitrov had never encountered before, and

00:29:16.860 --> 00:29:18.780
he was eager to be a part of it.

00:29:18.780 --> 00:29:23.510
With the help of Dr. Friedrich, Belitrov was
also sending letters to some of his fellow

00:29:23.510 --> 00:29:24.510
freed anomalies.

00:29:24.510 --> 00:29:30.150
He signed off by saying that he had even started
praying - something he’d never even considered

00:29:30.150 --> 00:29:31.150
before.

00:29:31.150 --> 00:29:35.050
The next letter, sent in 2027, struck a much
more somber tone.

00:29:35.050 --> 00:29:39.440
It was sent shortly after Belitrov discovered
Dr. Friedrich’s diagnosis.

00:29:39.440 --> 00:29:44.230
He wanted to return and see the doctor one
more time, but the Manna Charitable Foundation

00:29:44.230 --> 00:29:49.330
wouldn’t allow him to return to Site-17
- believing he had been abused during his

00:29:49.330 --> 00:29:50.330
time there.

00:29:50.330 --> 00:29:55.530
Belitrov gave Friedrich his prayers and well-wishes,
and asked for a number through which he could

00:29:55.530 --> 00:29:58.100
contact his ailing old friend.

00:29:58.100 --> 00:30:02.800
By the time the next letter arrived in 2034,
Belitrov had become a fully-fledged member

00:30:02.800 --> 00:30:05.540
of the Eastern Clockwork Orthodox Church.

00:30:05.540 --> 00:30:09.270
He referred to the other monks at the monastery
as his brothers and sisters.

00:30:09.270 --> 00:30:14.700
He seemed to have finally found a true home
there, and the others fondly referred to him

00:30:14.700 --> 00:30:17.040
by the nickname “Father Anvil.”

00:30:17.040 --> 00:30:21.780
But the true heart of the letter is Belitrov’s
deep concern for Dr. Friedrich’s health.

00:30:21.780 --> 00:30:26.700
Notably, in this letter, he often refers to
Dr. Friedrich by his first name, Thomas, as

00:30:26.700 --> 00:30:29.940
though to emphasize the urgency of the message.

00:30:29.940 --> 00:30:33.990
After the deaths of several of the anomalies
that Belitrov considered friends, he stated

00:30:33.990 --> 00:30:36.280
that he couldn’t handle losing anyone else.

00:30:36.280 --> 00:30:38.720
His letter ends with a poignant passage:

00:30:38.720 --> 00:30:42.580
“You may be unmarried, Doctor Friedrich,
but you are not unloved.

00:30:42.580 --> 00:30:44.560
You have to be strong for me.

00:30:44.560 --> 00:30:46.230
You have to be strong for yourself.

00:30:46.230 --> 00:30:50.840
If you're ever worried that you cannot find
the strength to continue, think of the garden

00:30:50.840 --> 00:30:52.290
you'll plant this spring.

00:30:52.290 --> 00:30:55.210
I'd like to share gardening photos with you
again.

00:30:55.210 --> 00:31:00.210
Not many of my brothers and sisters here appreciate
the simple beauty of a flower bed or the effort

00:31:00.210 --> 00:31:02.500
that goes into growing a patch of vegetables.

00:31:02.500 --> 00:31:05.060
It's a beauty I'd like to continue to share.

00:31:05.060 --> 00:31:10.250
Trust in the power of our Lord, Thomas, and
trust in the power of modern medicine.

00:31:10.250 --> 00:31:11.670
God is smiling on you.

00:31:11.670 --> 00:31:13.340
Please, be strong.

00:31:13.340 --> 00:31:16.110
With Love and Prayers,
Alexei Belitrov”

00:31:16.110 --> 00:31:19.780
This letter arrived on the 15th of February,
2034.

00:31:19.780 --> 00:31:23.270
Sadly, Dr. Friedrich had already passed away
four days earlier.

00:31:23.270 --> 00:31:26.240
He never got to see Alexei’s final letter.

00:31:26.240 --> 00:31:31.560
And it truly was his final letter - with nobody
left for him in the world, Major Belitrov

00:31:31.560 --> 00:31:33.660
stopped sending any correspondence.

00:31:33.660 --> 00:31:39.250
What we know about the final years of Belitrov’s
life all comes from a few scattered journal

00:31:39.250 --> 00:31:42.100
entries, translated from Russian after his
passing.

00:31:42.100 --> 00:31:46.810
They provide clues as to the kind of life
he lived during the 29 years the Foundation

00:31:46.810 --> 00:31:50.040
could not account for his whereabouts and
actions.

00:31:50.040 --> 00:31:55.700
The first entry, written on January 7th, 2035,
paints a grim picture of Belitrov feeling

00:31:55.700 --> 00:31:58.760
broken and isolated inside the monastery.

00:31:58.760 --> 00:31:59.760
He wrote:

00:31:59.760 --> 00:32:02.910
“Today is the day that our monastery celebrates
the birth of our Lord.

00:32:02.910 --> 00:32:05.800
However, I feel no desire to celebrate.

00:32:05.800 --> 00:32:08.460
All of my friends in this world are dead.

00:32:08.460 --> 00:32:13.290
My brothers and sisters are partaking in some
celebration outside my dormitory; all of the

00:32:13.290 --> 00:32:18.610
required ceremonies are complete, and neither
they nor whatever is happening out there now

00:32:18.610 --> 00:32:20.060
will lighten my mood.”

00:32:20.060 --> 00:32:24.360
Belitrov also wrote about losing the comfort
he once had in his faith, and his doubts about

00:32:24.360 --> 00:32:27.220
whether he would ever be able to recapture
that comfort.

00:32:27.220 --> 00:32:32.690
But he had survived greater traumas than this,
and he would continue to press on.

00:32:32.690 --> 00:32:37.250
As the months turned to years and the years
turned to decades, Belitrov climbed through

00:32:37.250 --> 00:32:39.210
the ranks of the monastery.

00:32:39.210 --> 00:32:44.040
Seeing as the Eastern Clockwork Orthodox Church
practically worshipped the concepts of industrialization

00:32:44.040 --> 00:32:49.100
and mechanization, the fact that Belitrov
was permanently encased in a biomechanical

00:32:49.100 --> 00:32:54.080
exoskeleton probably made him seem even more
pious to his holy brethren.

00:32:54.080 --> 00:32:58.470
The final piece of evidence collected by the
Foundation into the life and times of Alexei

00:32:58.470 --> 00:33:03.560
Belitrov came just over twenty years later,
in a final address written to comfort his

00:33:03.560 --> 00:33:07.090
followers in preparation for his own death.

00:33:07.090 --> 00:33:12.290
Belitrov recounted the details of his own
life: Being born into a world of fire, death,

00:33:12.290 --> 00:33:13.790
and mushroom clouds.

00:33:13.790 --> 00:33:19.530
Then his life being suddenly saved by forces
beyond his control, only to place him into

00:33:19.530 --> 00:33:21.840
containment for almost thirty years.

00:33:21.840 --> 00:33:26.510
It was only after accepting the teachings
of the Church, and accepting the Clockwork

00:33:26.510 --> 00:33:30.210
Goddess, that he felt he was truly free from
his past.

00:33:30.210 --> 00:33:35.730
In this final note, Belitrov lays out some
of the teachings of his new religion: The

00:33:35.730 --> 00:33:40.270
belief in a great mechanized Goddess who planned
all of reality.

00:33:40.270 --> 00:33:46.520
According to Belitrov, everything in her design
fits together perfectly like cogs in a machine,

00:33:46.520 --> 00:33:50.530
turning and twisting in unison to create an
ideal world.

00:33:50.530 --> 00:33:55.690
He hoped to be forgiven for the many violent
sins he committed in his military life, and

00:33:55.690 --> 00:33:59.450
that his contributions to this new world were
valuable.

00:33:59.450 --> 00:34:02.460
At the very end of his final address, Belitrov
wrote:

00:34:02.460 --> 00:34:06.760
“I do not believe that my time in this world
is much longer.

00:34:06.760 --> 00:34:11.419
Brothers and Sisters, when my time of Judgment
comes, do not mourn me.

00:34:11.419 --> 00:34:17.410
I would rather you remember these words: the
Goddess is most pleased with those who seek

00:34:17.410 --> 00:34:23.159
kind, non-violent resolution to their problems,
because a machine whose gears grind against

00:34:23.159 --> 00:34:26.270
each other is a machine that cannot work.

00:34:26.270 --> 00:34:28.990
Seek truth, but also compassion.

00:34:28.990 --> 00:34:30.490
The Words are only words.

00:34:30.490 --> 00:34:34.570
Seek out the Truth within them.

00:34:34.570 --> 00:34:35.720
God bless you all.

00:34:35.720 --> 00:34:36.720
Father Anvil.”

00:34:36.720 --> 00:34:42.270
A month after authoring this statement, records
indicate that Alexei Belitrov was found dead

00:34:42.270 --> 00:34:46.370
in his room, having passed away peacefully
in his sleep from natural causes.

00:34:46.370 --> 00:34:51.290
He lived a warrior’s life but died a humble
priest’s death.

00:34:51.290 --> 00:34:56.430
The true tragedy in the strange life of Major
Alexei Belitrov is how little choice he had

00:34:56.430 --> 00:35:01.721
in his circumstances, but thanks to this tale,
we know that he did what he could with the

00:35:01.721 --> 00:35:03.410
life he was given.

00:35:03.410 --> 00:35:08.190
His remains lay within the graveyard at the
Eastern Clockwork Orthodoxy monastery where

00:35:08.190 --> 00:35:10.690
he spent the last years of his life.

00:35:10.690 --> 00:35:24.270
With a life as difficult as his own, we can
only imagine he’s glad to finally rest.

00:35:24.270 --> 00:35:28.850
Some of the anomalies the SCP Foundation deals
with are dangerous, with the most powerful

00:35:28.850 --> 00:35:32.660
able to end all life and even reality as we
know it.

00:35:32.660 --> 00:35:37.030
Others pose no threat at all, and seem content
to simply exist.

00:35:37.030 --> 00:35:39.610
Still others are something else entirely.

00:35:39.610 --> 00:35:46.100
SCP-4999 is a humanoid entity, though its
appearance seems to fluctuate between manifestations,

00:35:46.100 --> 00:35:51.040
with the only unchanging detail being that
it is always dressed in dark formalwear.

00:35:51.040 --> 00:35:56.600
Originally thought by many to be an urban
legend, local tales of SCP-4999 are what initially

00:35:56.600 --> 00:36:00.600
tipped the Foundation off to its existence,
and further research indicates that there

00:36:00.600 --> 00:36:06.440
are accounts that may be referring to the
appearance of 4999 throughout recorded history.

00:36:06.440 --> 00:36:11.150
Strangest of all though, is the consistency
with which it appears, or rather the consistent

00:36:11.150 --> 00:36:14.090
situations and types of people it appears
to.

00:36:14.090 --> 00:36:20.330
From the data available, it seems that SCP-4999
only appears to people in a very specific

00:36:20.330 --> 00:36:21.330
type of need.

00:36:21.330 --> 00:36:27.220
As you’ll see in the case of a subject named
Alex Hereford and the fateful night he experienced.

00:36:27.220 --> 00:36:29.960
The road was slippery, and Alex was driving
too fast.

00:36:29.960 --> 00:36:34.890
He knew this of course, but it's a different
matter altogether to know a thing, and to

00:36:34.890 --> 00:36:35.890
care about it.

00:36:35.890 --> 00:36:40.840
Rain hammered on the front windshield, the
weak headlights of his 2005 Honda Civic barely

00:36:40.840 --> 00:36:43.750
punching into the thick, black night ahead
of him.

00:36:43.750 --> 00:36:48.500
Winding through the mountain side, the road
was mostly empty, save for the very occasional

00:36:48.500 --> 00:36:52.060
twin beams of light blazing past him due to
his high speed.

00:36:52.060 --> 00:36:56.450
It was hard to hear the honking of angry horns
over the heavy pounding of the rain.

00:36:56.450 --> 00:36:57.680
Then, it happened.

00:36:57.680 --> 00:37:00.400
In a way, Alex knew it was inevitable.

00:37:00.400 --> 00:37:05.020
His tread-worn wheels finally lost contact
with the ground, thick layer of rainwater

00:37:05.020 --> 00:37:10.920
between them and asphalt betraying his speeding
vehicle's grip on the road and sending it

00:37:10.920 --> 00:37:12.281
careening out of control.

00:37:12.281 --> 00:37:15.310
He had expected fear, but instead felt...
nothing really.

00:37:15.310 --> 00:37:21.260
A slight sense of anticipation, like wincing
right before a punch lands in that childhood

00:37:21.260 --> 00:37:23.370
game of hitting each other on the arm.

00:37:23.370 --> 00:37:27.760
It wasn't that the world had slowed down,
but perhaps his brain was simply working at

00:37:27.760 --> 00:37:32.710
a much greater velocity now, recognizing its
own impending death.

00:37:32.710 --> 00:37:37.040
His speed of thought seemed magnified to the
point of slowing his perception down.

00:37:37.040 --> 00:37:41.820
He'd heard of soldiers in war zones experiencing
the same phenomenon as they felt sure that

00:37:41.820 --> 00:37:44.930
in the next few seconds, they'd be dead.

00:37:44.930 --> 00:37:47.140
Alex wondered, would he smash into a tree?

00:37:47.140 --> 00:37:48.420
Go over a cliff's edge?

00:37:48.420 --> 00:37:53.640
He could hardly see the forest or the terrain
beyond in the thick rain and dark of the mountain.

00:37:53.640 --> 00:37:58.220
Though he'd traveled this road a million times
before, he had no idea where he actually was

00:37:58.220 --> 00:37:59.220
tonight.

00:37:59.220 --> 00:38:01.900
He supposed it wouldn't really matter which
it was.

00:38:01.900 --> 00:38:03.940
As usual, his thoughts turned to her.

00:38:03.940 --> 00:38:08.530
Or rather, they had simply run their course
and returned to the one place they always

00:38:08.530 --> 00:38:09.530
did.

00:38:09.530 --> 00:38:13.110
It wasn't like there were many other people
to think about in Alex's mostly empty life.

00:38:13.110 --> 00:38:18.830
There was, and always had been since the moment
he'd met her, mostly just her.

00:38:18.830 --> 00:38:22.980
But even Alex's heightened state of mind couldn't
delay the inevitable for long.

00:38:22.980 --> 00:38:27.540
It would be a cliff after all, Alex thought
curiously, catching a glimpse of town lights

00:38:27.540 --> 00:38:29.310
far away and below.

00:38:29.310 --> 00:38:35.210
The car spun 180 degrees out into empty air,
then came crashing down with a horrible roar

00:38:35.210 --> 00:38:39.350
of shattered glass and tearing metal as it
tumbled down the hillside.

00:38:39.350 --> 00:38:44.300
Even over the torrential downpour the noise
of Alex's crash was significant- had anyone

00:38:44.300 --> 00:38:46.350
been around to hear it.

00:38:46.350 --> 00:38:51.080
Finally, after over a hundred feet down a
steep incline, the car smashed into a single

00:38:51.080 --> 00:38:54.710
thick oak tree, bringing the disaster to an
end.

00:38:54.710 --> 00:38:58.170
As if on cue, the rain began to let up.

00:38:58.170 --> 00:39:03.180
Slowly at first, then all of the sudden in
that peculiar way that Northwest torrential

00:39:03.180 --> 00:39:08.930
downpours tend to do, as if the sky had at
last finished emptying itself all at once.

00:39:08.930 --> 00:39:12.650
Inside the shattered vehicle, Alex was- incredibly-
alive.

00:39:12.650 --> 00:39:15.320
At least for the time being.

00:39:15.320 --> 00:39:19.570
The airbag deployment had spared his face
the worst of it, and the sturdy aluminum frame

00:39:19.570 --> 00:39:24.760
of the vehicle had given its all in protecting
Alex's body from the downhill crash.

00:39:24.760 --> 00:39:27.980
But even post-modern vehicle engineering has
its limits.

00:39:27.980 --> 00:39:34.490
His breath came in slow, ragged gasps, difficult
at first but gradually steadying.

00:39:34.490 --> 00:39:39.170
Not an improvement in his condition, but rather
his body dedicating the rapidly dwindling

00:39:39.170 --> 00:39:45.210
resources at its disposal into keeping vital
functions going as long as possible.

00:39:45.210 --> 00:39:49.920
Opening his eyes, Alex was surprised to find
himself right side up, less surprised to look

00:39:49.920 --> 00:39:53.770
down at the shattered mess his limbs and lower
body had become.

00:39:53.770 --> 00:39:59.140
Gradually, Alex's thoughts cleared, his sense
of self returning after the bone-jarring drop

00:39:59.140 --> 00:40:02.690
down the steep incline and sudden stop at
the end.

00:40:02.690 --> 00:40:06.860
Looking to his right, he could see the trunk
of the tree that had stopped his out of control

00:40:06.860 --> 00:40:07.960
tumble.

00:40:07.960 --> 00:40:11.710
Despite himself, Alex laughed- a weak, gurgling
chuckle.

00:40:11.710 --> 00:40:14.860
So, it was the cliff and a tree after all.

00:40:14.860 --> 00:40:19.820
He focused on breathing, letting the waves
of pain wash over him until his brain eventually

00:40:19.820 --> 00:40:24.619
canceled them out by injecting his broken
body with adrenaline and chemicals.

00:40:24.619 --> 00:40:29.560
Everything was quiet and still after the crash
and the rain, but to his surprise he realized

00:40:29.560 --> 00:40:31.040
he could hear... something.

00:40:31.040 --> 00:40:36.230
It was faint at first, just a soft crunch
of footsteps on gravel, but the sound grew

00:40:36.230 --> 00:40:41.600
louder and louder until at last, it came to
a stop outside Alex's window.

00:40:41.600 --> 00:40:46.550
With every ounce of effort, Alex turned his
head towards the sound- a rescuer?

00:40:46.550 --> 00:40:48.150
No, impossible.

00:40:48.150 --> 00:40:52.119
Nobody was up on this mountain, and nobody
could possibly have reached him here so quickly

00:40:52.119 --> 00:40:53.930
even if there had been.

00:40:53.930 --> 00:40:57.990
He supposed he should have been surprised,
yet almost from the moment that his eyes fell

00:40:57.990 --> 00:41:03.760
on the tall, handsome figure with the casual,
yet fashionably cut black suit, Alex accepted

00:41:03.760 --> 00:41:05.500
him for what he was.

00:41:05.500 --> 00:41:11.300
There was no shock, no confusion, for the
second time tonight, just a calm sense of

00:41:11.300 --> 00:41:12.300
acceptance.

00:41:12.300 --> 00:41:16.900
The man, probably somewhere in his mid thirties,
leaned down to peer in through the window.

00:41:16.900 --> 00:41:20.610
He said nothing as he casually observed the
extent of Alex's injuries.

00:41:20.610 --> 00:41:24.020
Satisfied, he laid a hand on Alex's shoulder.

00:41:24.020 --> 00:41:29.200
The grip was firm, but not painfully so, just
strong enough to communicate, “I am here

00:41:29.200 --> 00:41:30.200
with you.

00:41:30.200 --> 00:41:31.200
Things'll be alright.”.

00:41:31.200 --> 00:41:36.330
After a slight squeeze, the figure reached
inside his jacket and produced a pack of cigarettes,

00:41:36.330 --> 00:41:40.730
packing the tobacco with swift taps against
his palm before removing two cigarettes and

00:41:40.730 --> 00:41:42.619
offering one to Alex.

00:41:42.619 --> 00:41:47.530
Alex nodded his head, a very small motion
that exploded pain across his shattered body.

00:41:47.530 --> 00:41:50.510
“Nah, thank you, but that stuff will kill
you.”

00:41:50.510 --> 00:41:51.510
Alex smiled.

00:41:51.510 --> 00:41:56.080
The man paused for a moment, the ghost of
a smile showing on his face for just a moment

00:41:56.080 --> 00:41:57.690
before disappearing.

00:41:57.690 --> 00:42:01.860
Returning the offered cigarette, the man took
his own and lit it, giving Alex a good look

00:42:01.860 --> 00:42:04.710
at his face in the light of his cigarette
lighter.

00:42:04.710 --> 00:42:08.890
Alex had been right, the man appeared to be
somewhere in his mid to late thirties.

00:42:08.890 --> 00:42:13.119
Handsome, but not cover model so, just pleasing
to the eyes.

00:42:13.119 --> 00:42:18.450
He sported short hair, carefully combed and
perfectly neat, completely unaffected by the

00:42:18.450 --> 00:42:20.530
slight drizzle that still fell.

00:42:20.530 --> 00:42:25.110
The more Alex looked at him though, the less
he could remember about the man's exact features.

00:42:25.110 --> 00:42:29.800
It wasn't that they changed in any way, but
rather that he simply couldn't hold on to

00:42:29.800 --> 00:42:31.980
any details for more than a few seconds.

00:42:31.980 --> 00:42:34.100
“I'm dying, aren't I?”.

00:42:34.100 --> 00:42:39.810
The figure didn't speak, nor did it nod or
make any form of verbal or bodily communication.

00:42:39.810 --> 00:42:42.670
He simply looked, and Alex understood.

00:42:42.670 --> 00:42:47.660
Alex had never been particularly religious
or spiritual, but in that look he understood

00:42:47.660 --> 00:42:52.630
that there was a world beyond, and one that
he would very quickly be entering into.

00:42:52.630 --> 00:42:58.610
It was as if for the first time in his life,
he was able to probe that world, reality peeling

00:42:58.610 --> 00:43:02.090
away just enough to glimpse what was beyond.

00:43:02.090 --> 00:43:07.340
Twisting paths though planes of shadow and
light both, shuffling figures along each,

00:43:07.340 --> 00:43:11.340
and at the very center of it all- a light?

00:43:11.340 --> 00:43:12.820
No, a feeling.

00:43:12.820 --> 00:43:13.820
Love.

00:43:13.820 --> 00:43:16.630
Pulsing forth like the beating heart of it
all.

00:43:16.630 --> 00:43:18.290
The saints had their angels.

00:43:18.290 --> 00:43:19.570
The wicked, their demons.

00:43:19.570 --> 00:43:23.560
But everyone else in between the two, they
had him.

00:43:23.560 --> 00:43:27.600
A guide, someone to watch over them on the
final journey.

00:43:27.600 --> 00:43:28.600
Alex coughed.

00:43:28.600 --> 00:43:29.610
It was ending soon.

00:43:29.610 --> 00:43:33.810
The man took a drag from his cigarette and
removed a handkerchief from another hidden

00:43:33.810 --> 00:43:39.500
pocket, carefully dabbing away the blood around
Alex's chin, then returned to his silent smoking.

00:43:39.500 --> 00:43:44.210
His vision was beginning to dim around the
edges, the noises of the forest growing more

00:43:44.210 --> 00:43:45.770
and more distant.

00:43:45.770 --> 00:43:50.220
Alex knew it wouldn't be long now, but he
had just one final thing to do.

00:43:50.220 --> 00:43:55.290
As he always knew they would, his thoughts
returned to her here, at the end.

00:43:55.290 --> 00:44:00.290
Once more he turned his head towards the passenger's
side seat, pain exploding across his body

00:44:00.290 --> 00:44:01.880
with the motion.

00:44:01.880 --> 00:44:07.040
There, just on the far edge of the seat as
his phone, having miraculously survived the

00:44:07.040 --> 00:44:08.040
crash.

00:44:08.040 --> 00:44:09.040
It was no good though.

00:44:09.040 --> 00:44:13.300
Even if he'd been able to move his shattered
right arm, he could never reach it with his

00:44:13.300 --> 00:44:14.300
fading strength.

00:44:14.300 --> 00:44:18.230
The smoking man took one final pull of his
cigarette, putting it out on the side of the

00:44:18.230 --> 00:44:20.501
vehicle and pocketing the stub.

00:44:20.501 --> 00:44:24.110
Then he reached in through the broken driver's
side window, Alex catching a slight whiff

00:44:24.110 --> 00:44:28.440
of cigarette smoke blended with an unrecognizable,
but pleasant cologne.

00:44:28.440 --> 00:44:32.970
The man reached across Alex and grabbed the
phone, pulling back and looking down at Alex's

00:44:32.970 --> 00:44:34.590
shattered right hand.

00:44:34.590 --> 00:44:38.220
After a moment, he reached down once more
and put the phone in Alex's left hand.

00:44:38.220 --> 00:44:39.220
“Thank you.”

00:44:39.220 --> 00:44:41.890
The words were barely a whisper.

00:44:41.890 --> 00:44:47.570
He had to concentrate now, willing the pressing
darkness to part just long enough for one

00:44:47.570 --> 00:44:48.700
final task.

00:44:48.700 --> 00:44:53.880
The man once more placed his hand reassuringly
on Alex's shoulder, and the darkness parted

00:44:53.880 --> 00:44:57.450
slightly- just enough for what Alex needed
to do.

00:44:57.450 --> 00:45:01.940
He worked the phone awkwardly with his left
hand, gritting his teeth through the pain

00:45:01.940 --> 00:45:03.700
of broken fingers.

00:45:03.700 --> 00:45:06.680
Opening a new message, he scrolled down his
contacts...

00:45:06.680 --> 00:45:15.190
G...H...I...J... finally, K. He found her
name at last, then began typing out a message.

00:45:15.190 --> 00:45:17.750
I still think about you every time it rains.

00:45:17.750 --> 00:45:23.600
He moved his thumb to press send, but that's
when Alex's body failed him at last, the phone

00:45:23.600 --> 00:45:25.110
tumbling out of his grasp.

00:45:25.110 --> 00:45:29.840
But the man was there to catch it, moving
blindly fast he snatched the falling phone

00:45:29.840 --> 00:45:34.060
up and held it carefully up to Alex's yes
before pressing Send.

00:45:34.060 --> 00:45:39.721
He held the phone there for Alex to see through
his fading vision, until at last, Message

00:45:39.721 --> 00:45:42.740
Sent confirmed successful delivery.

00:45:42.740 --> 00:45:47.950
The rain began once more, temperamental as
it always is in the Pacific Northwest.

00:45:47.950 --> 00:45:52.490
Fat, heavy rain drops fell on the scene of
a terrible accident, the victim seemingly

00:45:52.490 --> 00:45:54.541
having died on impact.

00:45:54.541 --> 00:46:00.110
On his lap though lay his phone, and somewhere
far away and far below this dark mountain

00:46:00.110 --> 00:46:05.180
side, a message notification chirped on a
distant phone.

00:46:05.180 --> 00:46:10.830
SCP-4999 manifests to only one person at a
time and only when they are alone.

00:46:10.830 --> 00:46:15.030
All subjects to date have been in the final
stages of a terminal illness, suffering from

00:46:15.030 --> 00:46:18.060
a life threatening injury, or otherwise on
their deathbed.

00:46:18.060 --> 00:46:23.950
It also appears that all subjects have personalities
and lives that could be described as nondescript,

00:46:23.950 --> 00:46:27.130
insignificant, or otherwise unremarkable.

00:46:27.130 --> 00:46:32.500
No testing of SCP-4999 has been authorized
by the Foundation due to both the difficulty

00:46:32.500 --> 00:46:36.750
in predicting where it will appear as well
as the fact that observation seems to prevent

00:46:36.750 --> 00:46:38.400
the anomaly from appearing.

00:46:38.400 --> 00:46:44.211
There are also ethical concerns, since many
in the Foundation feel that SCP-4999 is providing

00:46:44.211 --> 00:46:49.480
an important service to humanity, even if
it is only for those on the margins of society,

00:46:49.480 --> 00:46:53.710
and it is debated whether this should be one
anomalous creature that is allowed to continue

00:46:53.710 --> 00:46:58.280
its existence, and its work, without interference.

00:46:58.280 --> 00:47:00.130
What makes someone a hero?

00:47:00.130 --> 00:47:03.160
There is never just one answer to that question.

00:47:03.160 --> 00:47:07.960
Some will tell you that it’s selflessness,
putting other people before oneself that makes

00:47:07.960 --> 00:47:09.840
someone heroic.

00:47:09.840 --> 00:47:14.700
Others believe that heroism takes someone
with a clear sense of morality, the ability

00:47:14.700 --> 00:47:18.660
to tell right from wrong with absolute certainty.

00:47:18.660 --> 00:47:23.460
Perhaps a hero should also be a symbol, a
paragon of hope and virtue for all of society

00:47:23.460 --> 00:47:26.530
to look up to and aspire to be.

00:47:26.530 --> 00:47:31.460
And then there are those who would argue that
a person can’t possibly be a hero, unless

00:47:31.460 --> 00:47:33.760
they possess one key trait.

00:47:33.760 --> 00:47:39.230
Whether that comes as the result of a freak
accident, gamma radiation exposure, or mutated

00:47:39.230 --> 00:47:44.650
genes, being blessed with extraordinary powers
and the will to use them for good might just

00:47:44.650 --> 00:47:50.640
be what elevates a moral, selfless and symbolic
hero into something more.

00:47:50.640 --> 00:47:52.280
A superhero.

00:47:52.280 --> 00:47:57.660
It is rare that the SCP Foundation encounters
an anomalous creature or entity that it considers

00:47:57.660 --> 00:47:59.170
to be harmless.

00:47:59.170 --> 00:48:04.580
There are, of course, exceptions, but perhaps
even more of a rarity is an SCP that seeks

00:48:04.580 --> 00:48:09.109
to go out of its way and use its anomalous
abilities to do good.

00:48:09.109 --> 00:48:14.100
So many of the creatures and entities kept
contained by the Foundation have malicious

00:48:14.100 --> 00:48:19.380
intent, like damage-regenerating reptiles
with contempt for humanity and eldritch beings

00:48:19.380 --> 00:48:22.440
with desires to take over this dimension.

00:48:22.440 --> 00:48:28.610
But then there is SCP-2800, or as he prefers
to call himself, “Cactusman, the Spiked

00:48:28.610 --> 00:48:29.610
Menace.”

00:48:29.610 --> 00:48:36.341
Partially human, and part succulent plant,
SCP-2800 is one of a rare breed of SCPs: one

00:48:36.341 --> 00:48:41.990
that aims to help people, rather than killing
them, enslaving them, or wiping reality as

00:48:41.990 --> 00:48:43.869
we know it from existence.

00:48:43.869 --> 00:48:48.850
And you might be surprised to learn that this
superhero known as Cactusman, began life as

00:48:48.850 --> 00:48:52.780
one Daniel MacIntyre, an average guy from
Scotland.

00:48:52.780 --> 00:48:55.070
Little is known about Daniel’s “origin
story.”

00:48:55.070 --> 00:49:00.340
All superheroes have one, of course, but as
far as Foundation researchers are aware, Cactusman

00:49:00.340 --> 00:49:04.580
wasn’t jettisoned in a pod from his dying
homeworld to the safety of Earth.

00:49:04.580 --> 00:49:09.730
It is also safe to assume he didn’t get
pricked by a radioactive cactus, or have his

00:49:09.730 --> 00:49:13.210
DNA infused with a plant during a genetic
experiment.

00:49:13.210 --> 00:49:17.420
He was first encountered by the SCP Foundation
whilst they were trying to contain another

00:49:17.420 --> 00:49:22.300
SCP, a reality warping object that had somehow
breached containment.

00:49:22.300 --> 00:49:26.350
What Foundation staff tracking the object
witnessed was Cactusman attempting to assault

00:49:26.350 --> 00:49:30.130
the escaped SCP, to little success.

00:49:30.130 --> 00:49:34.580
Following this encounter, Foundation personnel
convinced Cactusman to allow them to contain

00:49:34.580 --> 00:49:35.580
him.

00:49:35.580 --> 00:49:40.840
He complied, was designated as SCP-2800, and
researchers began investigating the nature

00:49:40.840 --> 00:49:43.680
of this strange, would-be superhero.

00:49:43.680 --> 00:49:47.940
According to Daniel, one day his powers just
“happened”, with little understanding

00:49:47.940 --> 00:49:52.020
as to how, why, or what had caused the transformation.

00:49:52.020 --> 00:49:56.090
When asked about how he acquired his powers
during an interview with SCP Foundation researcher

00:49:56.090 --> 00:50:00.190
Dr L'oeuf, Daniel said:
“To be honest, doc, I dunno.

00:50:00.190 --> 00:50:03.290
I woke up one day, and boom, cactus powers.

00:50:03.290 --> 00:50:05.070
Thought that I might as well use them for
good, right?

00:50:05.070 --> 00:50:07.640
I always grew up reading a lot of comic books.

00:50:07.640 --> 00:50:10.650
Always loved the X-Men as a little kid, so
I thought I was one of them.

00:50:10.650 --> 00:50:11.650
Heh.

00:50:11.650 --> 00:50:15.120
I thought I was the luckiest guy in the world,
ending up with superpowers.

00:50:15.120 --> 00:50:17.910
Doesn't every kid wish that they could be
a superhero?”

00:50:17.910 --> 00:50:22.520
Analysis by Foundation research staff revealed
that Daniel’s DNA had somehow merged with

00:50:22.520 --> 00:50:27.100
a genome of a Carnegiea gigantea plant, or
saguaro cactus.

00:50:27.100 --> 00:50:32.640
This plant is usually what most people picture
if they were to imagine a typical cactus,

00:50:32.640 --> 00:50:38.110
and is known to be native to the Sonoran Desert,
as well as the Mexican state of Sonora.

00:50:38.110 --> 00:50:42.320
How one became a part of Daniel McIntyre’s
genetic makeup is baffling.

00:50:42.320 --> 00:50:46.920
It seems highly unlikely that a saguaro cactus
would grow naturally in Scotland, given that

00:50:46.920 --> 00:50:51.750
the country has a far damper and colder climate
than the scorching hot deserts that saguaros

00:50:51.750 --> 00:50:53.760
normally thrive in.

00:50:53.760 --> 00:50:58.590
Regardless of exactly how Daniel became fused
with a cactus, his body shares a number of

00:50:58.590 --> 00:51:01.100
the same physical properties of the plant.

00:51:01.100 --> 00:51:05.860
Pointed spines protrude from his skin, which
can grow to just over an inch in length.

00:51:05.860 --> 00:51:11.670
It seems that SCP-2800 can either remove these
spikes manually with little pain, or will

00:51:11.670 --> 00:51:16.830
eventually shed them naturally over time,
allowing more to regrow in their place.

00:51:16.830 --> 00:51:23.359
As well as outwardly looking like an anthropomorphic
cactus, SCP-2800 also shares various biological

00:51:23.359 --> 00:51:25.210
traits with his cacti counterparts.

00:51:25.210 --> 00:51:30.200
Daniel’s body no longer functions in the
same way as that of an ordinary human being

00:51:30.200 --> 00:51:31.840
in a number of different ways.

00:51:31.840 --> 00:51:36.760
Firstly, he is able to perform photosynthesis,
deriving the necessary nutrients he requires

00:51:36.760 --> 00:51:38.150
from direct sunlight.

00:51:38.150 --> 00:51:43.310
This negates the need for him to consume any
food, and prevents him from feeling hunger

00:51:43.310 --> 00:51:46.030
or the fatigue this can often bring.

00:51:46.030 --> 00:51:50.720
Additionally, his altered biology allows Cactusman
to store more water than would normally be

00:51:50.720 --> 00:51:52.390
possible for the average human.

00:51:52.390 --> 00:51:55.450
And he requires less of it too.

00:51:55.450 --> 00:52:00.330
SCP-2800 is able to keep himself hydrated
with a third of the required fluids for an

00:52:00.330 --> 00:52:01.860
average person.

00:52:01.860 --> 00:52:06.780
Daniel can also adapt to more arid environments,
with drier climates and above average levels

00:52:06.780 --> 00:52:10.330
of heat having little impact on his abilities.

00:52:10.330 --> 00:52:15.930
Speaking of abilities, SCP-2800 is not just
a man with the physical and biological traits

00:52:15.930 --> 00:52:23.000
of a saguaro cactus - he also has superpowers
that seem, well let’s say inspired by a

00:52:23.000 --> 00:52:24.000
cactus.

00:52:24.000 --> 00:52:27.750
While perhaps not as flashy as being faster
than a speeding bullet, more powerful than

00:52:27.750 --> 00:52:32.900
a locomotive, or able to leap tall buildings
in a single bound, Cactusman does possess

00:52:32.900 --> 00:52:36.230
his own unique set of superhuman abilities.

00:52:36.230 --> 00:52:42.840
Derived, like his other traits, from his part-saguaro
DNA, SCP-2800 has the power to empathically

00:52:42.840 --> 00:52:45.150
communicate with other plant life.

00:52:45.150 --> 00:52:50.490
Unlike telepathy and the ability to communicate
solely through thoughts, empaths like Cactusman

00:52:50.490 --> 00:52:56.140
are able to influence or interpret the emotions
or moods of others, so similar but a little

00:52:56.140 --> 00:52:58.010
more subtle in its effectiveness.

00:52:58.010 --> 00:53:03.610
Cactusman might have superhuman powers, altered
DNA, and a mysterious origin, but another

00:53:03.610 --> 00:53:10.030
part of a hero’s journey is their struggle
and SCP-2800 is no exception to this either.

00:53:10.030 --> 00:53:15.210
Despite his desire to do good, he harbors
a lot of unrest under that prickly exterior.

00:53:15.210 --> 00:53:19.950
After extensive psychological examination
by the researchers at the SCP Foundation,

00:53:19.950 --> 00:53:23.290
Daniel was diagnosed with two distinct mental
disorders.

00:53:23.290 --> 00:53:27.820
The first of these is dysthymia, or chronic
depression, with the other being a condition

00:53:27.820 --> 00:53:30.800
colloquially known as “hero syndrome.”

00:53:30.800 --> 00:53:36.000
Hero syndrome, as its name suggests, is often
characterized by an unstoppable, pathological

00:53:36.000 --> 00:53:41.140
urge to help other people, usually ignoring
any risks to oneself in the pursuit of assisting

00:53:41.140 --> 00:53:43.230
even total strangers.

00:53:43.230 --> 00:53:47.310
Some with this disorder will even attempt
to manufacture dangerous scenarios in order

00:53:47.310 --> 00:53:52.300
to act like the hero, and earn themselves
recognition and praise for reacting heroically

00:53:52.300 --> 00:53:55.210
to the danger they secretly caused.

00:53:55.210 --> 00:54:00.010
Like committing arson so they can save people
from a burning building.

00:54:00.010 --> 00:54:05.500
SCP-2800 has never attempted anything like
this so far, but Cactusman does express an

00:54:05.500 --> 00:54:10.710
extreme willingness to help people, and try
to intervene in any situation that he thinks

00:54:10.710 --> 00:54:12.050
he can assist with.

00:54:12.050 --> 00:54:17.980
The problem is, SCP-2800 is hardly an experienced
crimefighter, and this has put him on the

00:54:17.980 --> 00:54:21.580
receiving end of his fair share of injuries.

00:54:21.580 --> 00:54:25.530
During his first outing as “Cactusman, the
Spiked Menace”, Daniel encountered a group

00:54:25.530 --> 00:54:29.840
engaging in the sale of illicit substances
and attempted to apprehend them.

00:54:29.840 --> 00:54:34.610
While he was able to deal a cactus-spine-filled
blow to one of their faces, the group quickly

00:54:34.610 --> 00:54:39.730
overpowered Cactusman and beat him until local
law enforcement arrived to save him.

00:54:39.730 --> 00:54:43.470
Determined to prove himself a hero, though,
Daniel returned to patrolling the streets

00:54:43.470 --> 00:54:47.080
soon after, but met the same result.

00:54:47.080 --> 00:54:51.940
Even weak, petty criminals seemed like they
were too much for Cactusman to handle.

00:54:51.940 --> 00:54:57.230
While his hero syndrome compels SCP-2800 to
want to do good and set a good example, it

00:54:57.230 --> 00:55:00.970
is also directly linked to his other condition:
His dysthymia.

00:55:00.970 --> 00:55:06.640
By attempting and failing to be heroic, Cactusman
becomes chronically depressed, yet still has

00:55:06.640 --> 00:55:10.910
the urges brought on by his hero syndrome
to put himself in harm’s way for the sake

00:55:10.910 --> 00:55:11.910
of others.

00:55:11.910 --> 00:55:15.600
And when he is unable to provide help, Daniel
falls back into depression.

00:55:15.600 --> 00:55:18.800
It’s a very difficult cycle.

00:55:18.800 --> 00:55:23.119
In the hopes of counteracting some of Daniel’s
struggles, the SCP Foundation have gifted

00:55:23.119 --> 00:55:25.530
him a pair of potted cacti.

00:55:25.530 --> 00:55:31.300
These occupy SCP-2800’s cell with him, both
oxygenating his room as well as boosting his

00:55:31.300 --> 00:55:32.300
morale.

00:55:32.300 --> 00:55:36.570
Although, he has remarked that cacti don’t
say much to him beyond “I'm thirsty” and

00:55:36.570 --> 00:55:41.220
“I am a cactus”, Daniel has affectionately
named his potted plants.

00:55:41.220 --> 00:55:46.890
They’re now known as Cactilad and Spikigirl,
his sidekicks in the never ending battle against

00:55:46.890 --> 00:55:47.960
evil.

00:55:47.960 --> 00:55:52.320
During interviews with Foundation researcher
Dr L'oeuf, Daniel admitted that he was the

00:55:52.320 --> 00:55:54.740
victim of bullying throughout much of his
childhood.

00:55:54.740 --> 00:55:58.880
From a young age he often found himself in
physical altercations with bullies that singled

00:55:58.880 --> 00:56:01.210
him out and picked on him at school.

00:56:01.210 --> 00:56:05.750
Cactusman said that his experiences encouraged
him to “give back”, and that despite having

00:56:05.750 --> 00:56:12.109
suffered at the hands of bullies, it made
SCP-2800 determined to help others in need.

00:56:12.109 --> 00:56:17.380
In his own words, Daniel didn’t want what
had happened to him to happen to anybody else

00:56:17.380 --> 00:56:21.720
and it is highly likely that these experiences
from his youth are at least part of the cause

00:56:21.720 --> 00:56:23.220
of his hero syndrome.

00:56:23.220 --> 00:56:28.340
However, another incident may also be linked
to SCP-2800’s condition.

00:56:28.340 --> 00:56:32.880
Despite not often prevailing against petty
criminals, there is CCTV surveillance footage

00:56:32.880 --> 00:56:36.990
of Cactusman from before his containment by
the SCP Foundation.

00:56:36.990 --> 00:56:41.000
The footage in question was taken at a subway
close to where Daniel “patrolled” and

00:56:41.000 --> 00:56:43.020
looked for criminals to apprehend.

00:56:43.020 --> 00:56:47.230
In the surveillance tape, a woman and her
child can be seen waiting at the subway station

00:56:47.230 --> 00:56:48.850
near a support pillar.

00:56:48.850 --> 00:56:52.660
From behind the pillar, an assailant in a
mask appeared, wielding what looked to be

00:56:52.660 --> 00:56:53.660
a knife.

00:56:53.660 --> 00:56:58.020
The woman, cowering and trying to protect
her child, was made to open her purse, as

00:56:58.020 --> 00:57:00.510
the attacker threatened her with his knife.

00:57:00.510 --> 00:57:02.940
But then, Cactusman appears behind the man.

00:57:02.940 --> 00:57:06.720
He walked up to him and punched him in his
lower back and chest.

00:57:06.720 --> 00:57:12.180
A number of SCP-2800’s sharp cacti spines
end up lodged in the man’s skin, causing

00:57:12.180 --> 00:57:14.250
him to drop his knife in pain.

00:57:14.250 --> 00:57:20.300
During the ensuing scuffle, SCP-2800 was able
to tie the man up, thus saving the woman and

00:57:20.300 --> 00:57:21.380
her child.

00:57:21.380 --> 00:57:25.170
The woman then thanked Cactusman, shaking
his hand and embracing him.

00:57:25.170 --> 00:57:31.109
Her child also expressed gratitude, with SCP-2800
kneeling down to face them and appearing to

00:57:31.109 --> 00:57:34.200
get emotional at receiving recognition.

00:57:34.200 --> 00:57:38.050
After signing an autograph for the child,
Cactusman then disappeared from the scene

00:57:38.050 --> 00:57:40.170
before police arrived.

00:57:40.170 --> 00:57:44.800
Cacti have the tenacity to grow in barren
desert environments, surviving on very little

00:57:44.800 --> 00:57:45.800
water.

00:57:45.800 --> 00:57:50.700
It is for that reason, that to some, these
plants have come to symbolize strength, resilience,

00:57:50.700 --> 00:57:52.490
and endurance.

00:57:52.490 --> 00:57:56.790
This one encounter captured in this surveillance
footage may well have been one of the few

00:57:56.790 --> 00:58:02.400
times Cactusman ever succeeded at being heroic,
but perhaps it is all he needed to encourage

00:58:02.400 --> 00:58:03.660
him to keep trying.

00:58:03.660 --> 00:58:09.910
To seek out wrongdoings time and time again,
even if it led to him being injured.

00:58:09.910 --> 00:58:14.610
Maybe knowing that just once he had succeeded
in saving a woman and her child, was enough

00:58:14.610 --> 00:58:18.900
to convince him that he would one day be able
to do so again.

00:58:18.900 --> 00:58:25.190
And maybe that is what makes someone a true
hero: The power to endure.

00:58:25.190 --> 00:58:28.869
A tangled mass of yarn and ribbon sounds more
like what you’d find in the back room of

00:58:28.869 --> 00:58:33.770
a craft store or a forgotten closet than a
mysterious creature worthy of investigation.

00:58:33.770 --> 00:58:40.130
And yet that’s exactly what SCP-066 appeared
to be, or at least it did at first glance.

00:58:40.130 --> 00:58:45.510
But the SCP Foundation doesn’t contain and
study just anything, and there was - and still

00:58:45.510 --> 00:58:53.070
is - something incredibly strange just below
the surface of SCP-066, also known as “Eric’s

00:58:53.070 --> 00:58:54.070
Toy.”

00:58:54.070 --> 00:58:58.400
At first, Eric’s Toy seemed to be completely
harmless and even helpful, a knot of string

00:58:58.400 --> 00:59:01.320
that produced strange but harmless items and
effects.

00:59:01.320 --> 00:59:05.440
But, the Foundation soon discovered a dark
side to SCP-066.

00:59:05.440 --> 00:59:10.850
While it may be referred to as a toy, this
is no mere plaything.

00:59:10.850 --> 00:59:15.880
SCP-066 weighs only about one kilogram and
appears to be a braided bunch of yarn and

00:59:15.880 --> 00:59:16.880
ribbon.

00:59:16.880 --> 00:59:21.270
Though there is no apparent musical capability
within the strands of yarn and ribbon themselves,

00:59:21.270 --> 00:59:25.260
music can be produced by moving individual
strands one at a time.

00:59:25.260 --> 00:59:30.619
When it was first being studied, this SCP
was composed of multicolored strings and ribbons,

00:59:30.619 --> 00:59:35.220
but it has since undergone a transformation
and now presents an appearance somewhat different

00:59:35.220 --> 00:59:37.040
from its initial description.

00:59:37.040 --> 00:59:43.520
The strands of yarn and ribbon can be used
to play the notes of a diatonic scale - C-D-E-F-G-A-B

00:59:43.520 --> 00:59:49.720
- though the research has not been able to
determine just how SCP-066 produces music,

00:59:49.720 --> 00:59:51.730
or any sound at all.

00:59:51.730 --> 00:59:57.200
SCP-066 was thought to be completely benign
at first and was classified as Safe, but following

00:59:57.200 --> 01:00:04.000
an incident known as Incident 066-2, its classification
was adjusted to a subcategory of Euclid: Euclid-impetus.

01:00:04.000 --> 01:00:10.970
Euclid is a classification given to SCPs that
are more difficult to contain than those classified

01:00:10.970 --> 01:00:12.020
as “Safe.”

01:00:12.020 --> 01:00:18.140
Impetus, in Latin, means “attack” and
specifies that SCP-066 is not only Euclid

01:00:18.140 --> 01:00:20.300
class, but on the more aggressive side.

01:00:20.300 --> 01:00:26.349
While 066 is not always aggressive toward
humans, the events of Incident 066-2 proved

01:00:26.349 --> 01:00:29.910
that it is highly unpredictable, and should
not be provoked.

01:00:29.910 --> 01:00:35.530
Like many SCPs, it proved that underestimating
its capabilities can be a dangerous mistake.

01:00:35.530 --> 01:00:41.540
Before the incident, SCP-066 displayed only
charming, if unusual, behavior.

01:00:41.540 --> 01:00:45.740
Various researchers spent their time playing
random assortments of notes using its strings,

01:00:45.740 --> 01:00:50.580
curious about what would happen and determined
to record anything this unusual ball of string

01:00:50.580 --> 01:00:51.810
had to offer.

01:00:51.810 --> 01:00:55.990
They did not yet know that the creature was
capable of any hostility, and went about their

01:00:55.990 --> 01:00:58.910
work with a lighthearted, carefree spirit.

01:00:58.910 --> 01:01:02.940
After playing an improvised six-note melody
with the strands, a researcher was thrilled

01:01:02.940 --> 01:01:06.710
to find that SCP-066 was capable of shapeshifting.

01:01:06.710 --> 01:01:11.200
Its appearance changed to resemble a small
calico kitten for seventeen minutes.

01:01:11.200 --> 01:01:14.760
The kitten was incredibly friendly, rubbing
its head against the researcher’s gloved

01:01:14.760 --> 01:01:16.500
hand and purring loudly.

01:01:16.500 --> 01:01:20.780
Ironically enough, the kitten also spent time
playing with a piece of string.

01:01:20.780 --> 01:01:26.250
After the seventeen minutes were up, the kitten
transformed back into SCP-066’s original

01:01:26.250 --> 01:01:27.250
form.

01:01:27.250 --> 01:01:31.030
A few days later, another researcher played
a different melody on the strands, and was

01:01:31.030 --> 01:01:35.510
surprised to find that, when they stopped,
the music continued on its own.

01:01:35.510 --> 01:01:39.930
The sound of an acoustic guitar kicked in,
accompanied by vocals, with no visible source

01:01:39.930 --> 01:01:41.619
for either sound.

01:01:41.619 --> 01:01:46.250
The SCP then played a four-minute song with
lyrics warning against the use of sharp objects

01:01:46.250 --> 01:01:49.750
without the supervision of a parent, especially
scissors.

01:01:49.750 --> 01:01:53.290
After the song ended, the SCP was silent for
the rest of the day.

01:01:53.290 --> 01:01:58.440
The following week, a research assistant used
the strands of SCP-066 to play the opening

01:01:58.440 --> 01:02:02.770
notes of “Happy Birthday,” and a chocolate
cupcake with a lit birthday candle appeared

01:02:02.770 --> 01:02:05.190
from within the braided strings.

01:02:05.190 --> 01:02:08.109
Against the warnings of his peers, the assistant
ate the cupcake.

01:02:08.109 --> 01:02:12.640
In response, the SCP played the rest of “Happy
Birthday,” and the assistant suffered no

01:02:12.640 --> 01:02:15.200
adverse effects from the cupcake.

01:02:15.200 --> 01:02:19.420
All of this fun was brought to a swift end
when one scientist suggested that a portion

01:02:19.420 --> 01:02:25.710
of SCP-066’s yarn body be cut off and removed
so that the specimen could be tested.

01:02:25.710 --> 01:02:32.560
On April 18, 2008, the event that would become
known as Incident 066-2 took place.

01:02:32.560 --> 01:02:39.670
A young man known only as D-066-4437, or D,
was assigned to the task.

01:02:39.670 --> 01:02:43.750
Naturally, he was a member of the highly disposable
D Class personnel.

01:02:43.750 --> 01:02:48.970
But D was grateful for the opportunity, as
most experiments of a similar nature involved

01:02:48.970 --> 01:02:50.690
quite a bit more obvious risk.

01:02:50.690 --> 01:02:56.061
It was a simple enough job: take a pair of
scissors, snip off some yarn, and bring it

01:02:56.061 --> 01:02:58.390
back to the lab for further study.

01:02:58.390 --> 01:03:04.280
It was hardly on the level of supervising
173 or being 682’s latest chew toy.

01:03:04.280 --> 01:03:09.590
He entered the containment room, where SCP-066
was lying dormant and still, and approached

01:03:09.590 --> 01:03:11.181
it with the scissors.

01:03:11.181 --> 01:03:13.820
He grabbed a small handful of string, and
started to cut.

01:03:13.820 --> 01:03:18.250
As soon as the scissors began to cut through
the fabric, the SCP rolled out of his grasp.

01:03:18.250 --> 01:03:23.030
It came to a stop one meter away, where it
started to make a high-pitched squeaking sound

01:03:23.030 --> 01:03:25.250
resembling the cry of a frightened rabbit.

01:03:25.250 --> 01:03:29.630
Unsure what to do and unprepared for this
scenario, D approached the entity again.

01:03:29.630 --> 01:03:34.520
He snagged another fistful of yarn and cut,
only for 066 to curl into a ball and roll

01:03:34.520 --> 01:03:37.040
away from him again, even faster this time.

01:03:37.040 --> 01:03:41.120
Once it was safely on the other side of the
room and away from the scissors it stopped

01:03:41.120 --> 01:03:42.120
moving.

01:03:42.120 --> 01:03:44.050
Only this time it didn't squeak.

01:03:44.050 --> 01:03:49.210
Instead, for the very first time since its
containment, it spoke in a deep, uncannily

01:03:49.210 --> 01:03:52.980
human voice and asked: “Are you Eric?”

01:03:52.980 --> 01:03:57.040
After recovering from his initial shock at
hearing a voice come out of a mass of string,

01:03:57.040 --> 01:03:59.440
D responded “No, I’m not.”

01:03:59.440 --> 01:04:05.240
This answer set something off in SCP-066,
and its form began to shift and change.

01:04:05.240 --> 01:04:09.950
The string wriggled around on the floor, unbraiding
and wrapping around itself into a mound.

01:04:09.950 --> 01:04:15.970
The colors, previously a rainbow of shades,
shifted until every strand was blood red.

01:04:15.970 --> 01:04:19.849
Much to D’s horror, the transformation was
not yet complete.

01:04:19.849 --> 01:04:24.000
Small bumps began to emerge from the spaces
between the strands of yarn, popping out all

01:04:24.000 --> 01:04:25.700
over the bright red mass.

01:04:25.700 --> 01:04:31.140
If that wasn’t terrifying enough, suddenly
all together as one, they blinked open, revealing

01:04:31.140 --> 01:04:34.280
themselves to be over a dozen small eyes.

01:04:34.280 --> 01:04:39.530
Every single eye was focused at D, studying
him, staring him down.

01:04:39.530 --> 01:04:44.460
SCP-066 then began to produce loud, abrupt,
dissonant notes like someone banging on the

01:04:44.460 --> 01:04:45.990
keys of a piano.

01:04:45.990 --> 01:04:46.990
D had seen enough.

01:04:46.990 --> 01:04:50.080
He abandoned his task and fled the containment
room.

01:04:50.080 --> 01:04:55.110
After this failed attempt to extract a sample,
SCP-066’s behavior and its treatment of

01:04:55.110 --> 01:04:58.380
personnel who interacted with it began to
change dramatically.

01:04:58.380 --> 01:05:03.530
Before the incident, the SCP was largely dormant,
only becoming active if a melody was played

01:05:03.530 --> 01:05:05.010
using its strands.

01:05:05.010 --> 01:05:10.180
Following the incident, and its change of
form, 066 began to move on its own.

01:05:10.180 --> 01:05:14.410
Long strands of its yarn body would move like
tentacles, writhing and wriggling around at

01:05:14.410 --> 01:05:15.410
a high speed.

01:05:15.410 --> 01:05:20.310
It no longer needed human interaction in order
to produce sound, or to produce any other

01:05:20.310 --> 01:05:21.310
effects.

01:05:21.310 --> 01:05:25.940
At the sight of any human, regardless of the
human’s behavior, the SCP would begin to

01:05:25.940 --> 01:05:28.990
react with sound and effect within six seconds.

01:05:28.990 --> 01:05:33.350
The first of these effects was noted by a
research assistant who entered the SCP’s

01:05:33.350 --> 01:05:38.330
containment facility a week after the incident
with D. As she approached 066 to take notes

01:05:38.330 --> 01:05:42.790
about its current state and its new ability
to move, a bee appeared out of nowhere.

01:05:42.790 --> 01:05:46.680
It stung the assistant and flew away before
it could be captured.

01:05:46.680 --> 01:05:51.270
Weeks later, a team of eleven personnel were
monitoring the SCP when it suddenly burst

01:05:51.270 --> 01:05:53.800
into a rendition of Beethoven’s second symphony.

01:05:53.800 --> 01:05:58.869
It produced this music at a volume of over
140 decibels, permanently deafening three

01:05:58.869 --> 01:06:02.369
of the personnel, and causing permanent hearing
damage in the other eight.

01:06:02.369 --> 01:06:08.160
It was theorized that the SCP did this as
an act of retribution for its perceived mistreatment.

01:06:08.160 --> 01:06:12.270
These personnel refused to work with SCP-066
again.

01:06:12.270 --> 01:06:16.160
When a new team was assigned to monitor the
entity, everything seemed to be going well

01:06:16.160 --> 01:06:17.160
at first.

01:06:17.160 --> 01:06:21.480
It was moving around, flailing its tentacles
of yarn at nothing in particular, and staring

01:06:21.480 --> 01:06:25.880
at the personnel with its many eyes, but otherwise
was on its best behavior.

01:06:25.880 --> 01:06:31.030
Then, suddenly, every light in the room went
dark, and there was a complete loss of visibility.

01:06:31.030 --> 01:06:35.460
The lights were unable to be turned on for
five hours, and any attempt at an alternate

01:06:35.460 --> 01:06:38.440
light source such as a flashlight was unsuccessful.

01:06:38.440 --> 01:06:42.380
It was as if the darkness in the room swallowed
any and all light right up.

01:06:42.380 --> 01:06:47.370
It was similar to the oppressive darkness
within SCP – 087, or the unlimited black

01:06:47.370 --> 01:06:50.660
of SCP – 3001’s shadow dimension.

01:06:50.660 --> 01:06:54.590
The personnel in the room later reported hearing
the sound of loud, labored breathing just

01:06:54.590 --> 01:06:59.339
behind their shoulders, though when they searched
for a source of the sound, they could find

01:06:59.339 --> 01:07:00.339
nothing.

01:07:00.339 --> 01:07:03.740
There have been no recent anomalies reported,
or any additional hostile behavior.

01:07:03.740 --> 01:07:09.530
Instead, whenever it sees a new human, SCP-066
repeats the name “Eric” again and again

01:07:09.530 --> 01:07:11.680
in that same deep voice.

01:07:11.680 --> 01:07:12.680
Who is Eric?

01:07:12.680 --> 01:07:16.930
No one at the facility knows, or, if they
do, they have not reported it to any official

01:07:16.930 --> 01:07:17.990
channels.

01:07:17.990 --> 01:07:23.010
It is possible that the SCP was once owned
by someone named Eric and perhaps, given the

01:07:23.010 --> 01:07:28.740
circumstances under which SCP-066 first said
the name, Eric attempted to cut the threads

01:07:28.740 --> 01:07:31.339
of the entity while it was in his care.

01:07:31.339 --> 01:07:36.900
Unfortunately, there are no official records
of how SCP-066 was discovered, or why it was

01:07:36.900 --> 01:07:39.260
brought to the foundation in the first place.

01:07:39.260 --> 01:07:43.130
Its origins remain murky and as mysterious
as everything else about it.

01:07:43.130 --> 01:07:49.720
All that is known is that, whoever Eric is,
SCP-066 is determined to find him.

01:07:49.720 --> 01:07:53.830
Once the SCP’s class was changed from Safe
to Euclid, its containment procedures had

01:07:53.830 --> 01:07:54.830
to be adjusted.

01:07:54.830 --> 01:07:59.710
While it was previously kept in a simple room,
it is now contained in a tungsten carbide

01:07:59.710 --> 01:08:03.349
box at its site’s high-value item storage
facility.

01:08:03.349 --> 01:08:08.460
Once a month, the box is inspected for damage
to its interior, due to the SCP’s tendency

01:08:08.460 --> 01:08:13.200
to use its appendages to wear down the walls
of the box over time.

01:08:13.200 --> 01:08:19.259
If there is any damage, SCP-066 is to be moved
to a new box using a robotic arm that performs

01:08:19.259 --> 01:08:22.079
this transfer in less than three seconds.

01:08:22.079 --> 01:08:26.589
The Foundation has attempted to place recording
devices in the box with the entity in order

01:08:26.589 --> 01:08:29.749
to monitor its behavior when there are no
humans present.

01:08:29.749 --> 01:08:35.179
But the SCP destroys every recording device
placed inside of its containment box and any

01:08:35.179 --> 01:08:40.609
attempts to record its behavior when it is
not being observed by humans have been unsuccessful.

01:08:40.609 --> 01:08:44.630
Whatever it’s doing when there is no one
around it wants to keep a secret.

01:08:44.630 --> 01:08:49.589
On the surface, SCP-066 is one of the less
frightening finds contained within the walls

01:08:49.589 --> 01:08:50.859
of the SCP Foundation.

01:08:50.859 --> 01:08:57.119
It does not have claws, or teeth, or the ability
to cause mass deaths, but it has incredible,

01:08:57.119 --> 01:09:01.579
unpredictable capabilities, and seems very
capable of holding a grudge.

01:09:01.579 --> 01:09:06.160
There is so much that is unknown about it,
from its origins, to its form, to its ability

01:09:06.160 --> 01:09:10.779
to manifest matter from nothing, and there
is something deeply unsettling about this

01:09:10.779 --> 01:09:16.019
SCP’s unpredictable behavior and increased
hostility toward being observed.

01:09:16.019 --> 01:09:20.089
We do not know what it has done, and we do
not know what it will do next.

01:09:20.089 --> 01:09:21.670
All we can do is wonder.

01:09:21.670 --> 01:09:28.630
As we ponder the nature of SCP-066, it does
nothing but sit, staring with unblinking eyes,

01:09:28.630 --> 01:09:30.369
waiting for Eric to come back.

01:09:30.369 --> 01:09:32.719
Are you sitting comfortably?

01:09:32.719 --> 01:09:35.049
We know a good chair is hard to find.

01:09:35.049 --> 01:09:39.349
Maybe you’re watching this on your phone
while you lie in bed, or maybe you’re watching

01:09:39.349 --> 01:09:42.329
it at your desk, sitting in an office chair.

01:09:42.329 --> 01:09:45.670
Maybe you’re even watching it while you’re
in the bathroom; it’s fine, we’re not

01:09:45.670 --> 01:09:46.690
here to judge.

01:09:46.690 --> 01:09:52.829
For our money, you just can’t beat a nice,
classic wooden chair, with soft leather upholstery.

01:09:52.829 --> 01:09:58.260
Call us old-fashioned, but some things just
never go out of style.

01:09:58.260 --> 01:10:01.989
Take a chair like SCP-1609, for example.

01:10:01.989 --> 01:10:06.640
This fine piece of mahogany was once a chair
that simply couldn’t be beat in its quest

01:10:06.640 --> 01:10:11.869
to bring its users a little dose of comfort
and refinement in their daily life.

01:10:11.869 --> 01:10:16.630
Tell us, have you ever been on your feet all
day, just walking and walking and walking,

01:10:16.630 --> 01:10:20.929
and at a certain point, you’re just begging
for a nice, comfy chair that’ll let you

01:10:20.929 --> 01:10:23.080
take the weight off your feet for a little
while?

01:10:23.080 --> 01:10:27.179
You would have been SCP-1609’s favorite
kind of person.

01:10:27.179 --> 01:10:32.249
After all, it was the only chair that literally
sought out weary travelers, and even did you

01:10:32.249 --> 01:10:34.150
the courtesy of tucking itself in.

01:10:34.150 --> 01:10:37.360
That’s not a metaphor, either.

01:10:37.360 --> 01:10:42.480
SCP-1609 could literally teleport to nearby
people who needed to sit down and didn’t

01:10:42.480 --> 01:10:44.639
have a chair to fulfill that desire.

01:10:44.639 --> 01:10:49.699
It was nothing but a nice, helpful anomaly
that wanted to help people rest when they

01:10:49.699 --> 01:10:50.869
needed it most.

01:10:50.869 --> 01:10:55.369
The more observant members of you may have
noticed that we’ve been using the past tense

01:10:55.369 --> 01:10:56.369
so far.

01:10:56.369 --> 01:11:02.669
That’s because, while SCP-1609 is still
an active anomaly, it isn’t a chair anymore

01:11:02.669 --> 01:11:09.510
- and this transformation wasn’t something
that SCP-1609 planned, anticipated, or even

01:11:09.510 --> 01:11:10.510
wanted.

01:11:10.510 --> 01:11:15.199
The story of 1609’s transformation even
strikes to the core of one of the Foundation’s

01:11:15.199 --> 01:11:19.090
oldest and most bitterly held rivalries with
another group of interest.

01:11:19.090 --> 01:11:24.469
It’s the tale of how a helpful piece of
anomalous furniture became a paranoid killer.

01:11:24.469 --> 01:11:28.130
But first, we need to talk about containment
procedures.

01:11:28.130 --> 01:11:33.219
Like a word you see so often that it starts
to lose meaning, containment and specific

01:11:33.219 --> 01:11:39.070
containment procedures are concepts so integral
to the very existence of the SCP Foundation

01:11:39.070 --> 01:11:42.229
that it’s easy to overlook or forget about
them.

01:11:42.229 --> 01:11:47.210
They’re one of the three core pillars of
the Foundation’s mission statement - Secure,

01:11:47.210 --> 01:11:49.570
Contain, Protect.

01:11:49.570 --> 01:11:53.809
Because of the centrality of containment to
the Foundation’s core principles, one of

01:11:53.809 --> 01:11:59.349
the most valuable roles on the SCP Foundation
payroll is that of the Containment Specialist:

01:11:59.349 --> 01:12:05.989
A vast team of experts who work with researchers
to figure out the best way to keep every anomaly

01:12:05.989 --> 01:12:09.770
contained, based on their unique abilities
and attributes.

01:12:09.770 --> 01:12:16.340
They’re zookeepers, archivists, guards,
security and intelligence experts, magicians,

01:12:16.340 --> 01:12:20.579
practitioners of ritual, scientists, and so
much more.

01:12:20.579 --> 01:12:24.659
In short, they’re anything they need to
be in order to adapt to the ever-evolving

01:12:24.659 --> 01:12:28.699
containment needs of the anomalies they keep
under lock and key.

01:12:28.699 --> 01:12:31.010
And containment isn’t easy.

01:12:31.010 --> 01:12:37.050
Aside from the rare Safe-class SCPs, which
require incredibly minimal containment resources,

01:12:37.050 --> 01:12:43.610
the containment of most SCPs extracts some
kind of cost, whether that be financial, time,

01:12:43.610 --> 01:12:48.760
effort, or in some particularly dark cases,
human life.

01:12:48.760 --> 01:12:56.699
Some SCPs, like SCP-974 and SCP-2845, require
the sacrifice of human children to prevent

01:12:56.699 --> 01:12:59.420
worse fates befalling many others.

01:12:59.420 --> 01:13:06.190
Other SCPs, like the infamous SCP-231, require
the Foundation to do horrifying things to

01:13:06.190 --> 01:13:12.300
the SCP itself to prevent it from manifesting
some even more horrifying anomalous traits.

01:13:12.300 --> 01:13:19.790
And a third but equally inconvenient kind
of SCP, like SCP-682 and SCP-076, require

01:13:19.790 --> 01:13:24.860
huge numbers of heavily armed guards with
powerful weapons to keep their deadly prisoners

01:13:24.860 --> 01:13:29.389
locked away, often at massive risk to their
own lives.

01:13:29.389 --> 01:13:34.179
Containment isn’t easy, but it’s ultimately
the very thing that makes the SCP Foundation

01:13:34.179 --> 01:13:36.329
the organization it is.

01:13:36.329 --> 01:13:40.090
If they were instead on a quest to kill and
destroy every anomaly they could get their

01:13:40.090 --> 01:13:46.249
hands on, then, they’d be the Global Occult
Coalition - the UN’s answer to the SCP Foundation

01:13:46.249 --> 01:13:52.179
that prefers to seek, disable, and destroy
rather than Secure, Contain, and Protect.

01:13:52.179 --> 01:13:57.420
It’s the primary characteristic that differentiates
these two titans of the anomalous world who

01:13:57.420 --> 01:14:03.960
regularly come to blows, and right at the
heart of that difference is SCP-1609.

01:14:03.960 --> 01:14:09.809
As we mentioned earlier, SCP-1609 went through
a transformation that changed everything,

01:14:09.809 --> 01:14:14.940
but the SCP Foundation never actually knew
about the anomaly prior to that transformation

01:14:14.940 --> 01:14:16.260
taking place.

01:14:16.260 --> 01:14:21.110
It first came to their attention when it literally
manifested within a containment cell in Storage

01:14:21.110 --> 01:14:27.420
Site-08, making the rare move of willingly
submitting itself to Foundation containment.

01:14:27.420 --> 01:14:31.130
But what showed up in that cell certainly
wasn’t a chair.

01:14:31.130 --> 01:14:36.479
When 1609 appeared all it looked like was
a pile of trash - specifically, splinters,

01:14:36.479 --> 01:14:41.249
wood chippings, furniture nails, and scraps
of bleached leather and fabric.

01:14:41.249 --> 01:14:45.730
Anything that suddenly infiltrates a secure
Foundation containment site is a cause for

01:14:45.730 --> 01:14:51.449
concern, even a bunch of wood scraps, so the
Site Director sent in an armed guard to investigate

01:14:51.449 --> 01:14:54.209
the mysterious pile of debris.

01:14:54.209 --> 01:14:58.150
Researchers watching over a surveillance feed
were surprised when the guard suddenly entered

01:14:58.150 --> 01:15:00.280
a state of heightened distress.

01:15:00.280 --> 01:15:05.059
He fell to his knees, coughing and spluttering
until he expelled a considerable amount of

01:15:05.059 --> 01:15:07.239
blood from his mouth and nose.

01:15:07.239 --> 01:15:11.250
He then collapsed onto the ground next to
the pile of debris, dead.

01:15:11.250 --> 01:15:16.309
An investigation following this incident found
that the guard had died after a sudden influx

01:15:16.309 --> 01:15:22.590
of jagged metal and wood had teleported inside
of him, tearing his lungs apart from the inside

01:15:22.590 --> 01:15:26.510
and causing the guard to die a painful and
horrific death.

01:15:26.510 --> 01:15:30.710
Naturally, the site personnel were somewhat
concerned by this development.

01:15:30.710 --> 01:15:35.300
They sent in a D-Class to investigate further,
but were surprised to find that the D-Class

01:15:35.300 --> 01:15:37.949
in question was somehow completely fine.

01:15:37.949 --> 01:15:44.059
The pile of debris that would soon be designated
SCP-1609 made no attempt to harm the D-Class

01:15:44.059 --> 01:15:48.940
as it had the guard, and finding out why this
was the case came as a side effect of figuring

01:15:48.940 --> 01:15:51.150
out exactly what had happened to SCP-1609.

01:15:51.150 --> 01:15:58.130
Through a rigorous investigation, involving
more than one secret Foundation mole, they

01:15:58.130 --> 01:16:03.849
discovered that SCP-1609 had previously been
in the possession of - you guessed it - the

01:16:03.849 --> 01:16:05.659
Global Occult Coalition.

01:16:05.659 --> 01:16:10.619
Back then, it was just the helpful chair you
once knew and loved, until the GOC had the

01:16:10.619 --> 01:16:15.809
bright idea of forcing it into a woodchipper
in order to destroy it due to its connection

01:16:15.809 --> 01:16:18.489
to someone called The Carpenter.

01:16:18.489 --> 01:16:23.929
But all the GOC’s attempt actually succeeded
in doing was altering its form, and completely

01:16:23.929 --> 01:16:26.039
changing its personality.

01:16:26.039 --> 01:16:32.409
To put it in simple terms, SCP-1609 is now
a pile of possibly-sentient, teleporting wood

01:16:32.409 --> 01:16:36.800
and metal chippings that suffers from a nasty
case of PTSD.

01:16:36.800 --> 01:16:42.570
The incident with the wood chipper traumatized
SCP-1609, and its anxiety is triggered by

01:16:42.570 --> 01:16:47.659
anything that reminds it of the GOC or the
wood chipper incident - this includes wearing

01:16:47.659 --> 01:16:53.969
formal clothing, lab coats, protective clothing,
jumpsuits, and particularly body armor, but

01:16:53.969 --> 01:16:59.889
also includes anyone carrying weapons, appearing
outwardly aggressive, using common GOC lingo,

01:16:59.889 --> 01:17:03.719
or even mentioning the GOC in SCP-1609’s
proximity.

01:17:03.719 --> 01:17:10.290
If any of this happens, it’s extremely likely
that SCP-1609 will resort to its only natural

01:17:10.290 --> 01:17:15.249
defense mechanism, which is teleporting its
debris into the lungs of anyone it considers

01:17:15.249 --> 01:17:16.639
to be a threat.

01:17:16.639 --> 01:17:22.050
The guard had received this grisly punishment
because his clothes, weapon, and overall manner

01:17:22.050 --> 01:17:27.519
caused SCP-1609 to regard him as a threat
and react accordingly.

01:17:27.519 --> 01:17:31.830
You may think this is overkill on 1609’s
part, but if you were just trying to help

01:17:31.830 --> 01:17:36.350
out the chairless people of the world and
someone fed you into a wood chipper, you’d

01:17:36.350 --> 01:17:38.880
probably be a little jumpy too.

01:17:38.880 --> 01:17:42.849
Since these early days, the Foundation has
learned to apply a more tender touch when

01:17:42.849 --> 01:17:48.650
it comes to dealing with SCP-1609, and the
brilliant containment specialists even figured

01:17:48.650 --> 01:17:55.060
out a way to keep 1609 happily contained…
by placing it in a flower bed inside its containment

01:17:55.060 --> 01:18:00.199
chamber where its wood chips get to serve
as mulch for a variety of flowers and plants.

01:18:00.199 --> 01:18:04.940
All attending researchers and guards dress
in plain clothes, and adopt a loose, pleasant

01:18:04.940 --> 01:18:06.880
attitude while inside.

01:18:06.880 --> 01:18:10.650
Whenever they’re around, they make a point
of saying how beautiful the flower bed is,

01:18:10.650 --> 01:18:15.269
so that the disfigured anomaly that only ever
wanted to be helpful can still feel like it’s

01:18:15.269 --> 01:18:17.040
doing something nice.

01:18:17.040 --> 01:18:22.730
Because of these containment procedures, breaches
involving SCP-1609 have remained in the single

01:18:22.730 --> 01:18:23.730
digits.

01:18:23.730 --> 01:18:28.780
It’s a perfect example of less really being
more when it comes to containment.

01:18:28.780 --> 01:18:35.059
The head researcher on the SCP-1609 case,
Dr. Sievert, released an internal document,

01:18:35.059 --> 01:18:38.499
permanently affixed to the file like a kind
of cautionary signpost.

01:18:38.499 --> 01:18:43.340
It’s a clear expression of exasperation
and rage at the actions of the Global Occult

01:18:43.340 --> 01:18:45.489
Coalition, reading:

01:18:45.489 --> 01:18:50.550
“SCP-1609 represents a perfect example of
the flaws inherent in the operating procedure

01:18:50.550 --> 01:18:56.250
of the GOC, and serves as a cautionary tale
for any members of the Foundation who disagree

01:18:56.250 --> 01:18:59.579
with our practices on containing dangerous
objects.

01:18:59.579 --> 01:19:04.360
Prior to the Coalition getting their hands
on this, it was perfectly harmless.

01:19:04.360 --> 01:19:08.610
A chair which teleports to you when you need
a seat is normal compared to most of the stuff

01:19:08.610 --> 01:19:11.080
that we deal with on a regular basis.

01:19:11.080 --> 01:19:15.860
When they put it through a woodchipper, it
got hurt, scared and angry, so it lashed out

01:19:15.860 --> 01:19:16.860
at them.

01:19:16.860 --> 01:19:20.929
By trying to 'protect the world' by destroying
it, they inadvertently made the situation

01:19:20.929 --> 01:19:22.940
a whole lot worse.

01:19:22.940 --> 01:19:28.020
SCP-1609 went from being harmless to deadly
in the space of a few minutes because of the

01:19:28.020 --> 01:19:30.790
GOC, and we had to clean up the mess.

01:19:30.790 --> 01:19:34.949
Thankfully, SCP-1609 is pretty simple for
us to deal with.

01:19:34.949 --> 01:19:39.889
So long as we don't do anything stupid around
it, it won't fight back and it won't try to

01:19:39.889 --> 01:19:40.889
leave.

01:19:40.889 --> 01:19:42.479
Even if it does, it usually comes back.

01:19:42.479 --> 01:19:44.349
I think I've worked out why.

01:19:44.349 --> 01:19:48.219
It came to us because it was afraid of the
people who had hurt it.

01:19:48.219 --> 01:19:49.710
That's why it always comes back.

01:19:49.710 --> 01:19:54.639
It's afraid of the rest of the world now,
and it's looking to us for protection.

01:19:54.639 --> 01:20:00.969
This is why we have Special Containment Procedures
instead of Special Destruction Procedures.

01:20:00.969 --> 01:20:03.329
If you break something, it's broken forever.

01:20:03.329 --> 01:20:07.679
When you try to destroy an anomaly, you can't
take back your mistakes.

01:20:07.679 --> 01:20:11.139
That's what SCP-1609 has to tell us.

01:20:11.139 --> 01:20:14.449
This is why we're right and the GOC is wrong,
people.”

01:20:14.449 --> 01:20:18.929
But of course, there are two sides to every
story, and it’s important to understand

01:20:18.929 --> 01:20:21.679
the GOC’s perspective on this whole mess.

01:20:21.679 --> 01:20:29.679
To them, this has never been SCP-1609, it’s
KTE-0937-Velveteen, aka The Sixth Chair.

01:20:29.679 --> 01:20:34.510
It was labeled as the “sixth” because
for the GOC, this chair was merely one part

01:20:34.510 --> 01:20:36.360
of a wider investigation.

01:20:36.360 --> 01:20:41.860
It belonged to a six piece furniture set created
by a dangerous, anomalous person of interest

01:20:41.860 --> 01:20:44.630
named The Carpenter for a classified customer.

01:20:44.630 --> 01:20:49.619
The GOC was able to intercept this deal, and
kill the Carpenter and his customer in the

01:20:49.619 --> 01:20:50.719
process.

01:20:50.719 --> 01:20:54.989
After that, all that was left was to eliminate
the anomalous objects and five of them were

01:20:54.989 --> 01:20:56.780
incinerated without incident.

01:20:56.780 --> 01:21:01.820
However, before they could do the same to
the Sixth Chair, they experienced an incinerator

01:21:01.820 --> 01:21:03.119
malfunction.

01:21:03.119 --> 01:21:07.679
Rather than waiting for the incinerator to
be fixed, a member of GOC personnel decided

01:21:07.679 --> 01:21:10.780
to rush the job and run the chair through
the woodchipper.

01:21:10.780 --> 01:21:15.639
It was at this point that its pieces first
lashed out, invading the lungs of this negligent

01:21:15.639 --> 01:21:19.010
GOC member along with five others, killing
them all.

01:21:19.010 --> 01:21:25.039
It was shortly after that that SCP-1609 manifested
in Foundation containment.

01:21:25.039 --> 01:21:30.119
Much like Dr. Sievert did for the Foundation,
Assistant Director Kipling, one of the GOC’s

01:21:30.119 --> 01:21:35.969
legion of middle managers, affixed a note
to the profile on KTE-0937-Velveteen that

01:21:35.969 --> 01:21:36.969
reads:

01:21:36.969 --> 01:21:41.869
“KTE-0937-Velveteen is an object lesson
in the importance of following proper operating

01:21:41.869 --> 01:21:43.010
procedures.

01:21:43.010 --> 01:21:47.409
Due to the lack of vigilance by the agent
on the scene, the object's threat level was

01:21:47.409 --> 01:21:52.619
escalated, the object itself was not successfully
disposed of, and it has since fallen into

01:21:52.619 --> 01:21:54.719
the hands of a hostile agency.

01:21:54.719 --> 01:21:59.659
A single failure by a single operative resulted
in the deaths of six.

01:21:59.659 --> 01:22:01.869
Remember this the next time you think about
cutting corners.”

01:22:01.869 --> 01:22:04.199
And that’s a good lesson for everyone.

01:22:04.199 --> 01:22:08.489
Whether you’re trying to destroy an anomalous
piece of furniture or keeping its remains

01:22:08.489 --> 01:22:13.969
happy so that they don’t try to kill you,
cutting corners is always a fast track to

01:22:13.969 --> 01:22:14.969
failure.

01:22:14.969 --> 01:22:21.289
In June of 1985, Mark Johnson and his wife
of ten years, Sophie, were on vacation in

01:22:21.289 --> 01:22:23.499
Myrtle Beach having a great time.

01:22:23.499 --> 01:22:28.119
While they relaxed on the sand, Sophie decided
to take a picture of her husband for their

01:22:28.119 --> 01:22:33.159
scrapbook, so she pulled out the Polaroid
Supercolor 645 that she'd bought specifically

01:22:33.159 --> 01:22:34.260
for the trip.

01:22:34.260 --> 01:22:38.929
She pressed the button, waited for the picture
to print, pulled it out, and shook it.

01:22:38.929 --> 01:22:42.929
What she expected to see was a shot of Mark
lying on his beach towel.

01:22:42.929 --> 01:22:48.289
What she got, was a picture of her husband
in the arms of his secretary.

01:22:48.289 --> 01:22:53.449
They say that a picture speaks a thousand
words, but this particular camera takes pictures

01:22:53.449 --> 01:22:55.659
that are worth even more than that.

01:22:55.659 --> 01:23:00.309
When developed, the pictures taken with this
normal-looking polaroid camera reveal the

01:23:00.309 --> 01:23:03.780
innermost desires of the person being photographed.

01:23:03.780 --> 01:23:09.789
Welcome to the story of SCP - 978 - The Desire
Camera.

01:23:09.789 --> 01:23:15.809
The main reason the foundation keeps SCP 978
under wraps is due to its use as an easy form

01:23:15.809 --> 01:23:17.120
of blackmail.

01:23:17.120 --> 01:23:21.999
All anyone with access to the camera would
have to do is snap a few covert photos and

01:23:21.999 --> 01:23:25.289
they'd have instant dirt on the world's most
powerful people.

01:23:25.289 --> 01:23:29.769
To further stop this camera from falling into
the wrong hands, the containment guidelines

01:23:29.769 --> 01:23:35.099
strictly forbid the use of the camera for
anything other than simple documentation,

01:23:35.099 --> 01:23:38.349
and all uses of it must be thoroughly logged
and checked.

01:23:38.349 --> 01:23:43.729
So, now that you know what the camera does,
it’s time to look at what kinds of strange

01:23:43.729 --> 01:23:46.329
and mysterious photos it’s taken.

01:23:46.329 --> 01:23:50.519
After all, who doesn't want a chance to gain
insight into the minds of the Foundation's

01:23:50.519 --> 01:23:53.309
most famous and dangerous inmates?

01:23:53.309 --> 01:23:58.309
First, to serve as a control the team took
a photo of a blue office chair.

01:23:58.309 --> 01:24:04.499
No change was recorded, proving that the camera
didn't work on non-anomalous inanimate objects.

01:24:04.499 --> 01:24:08.440
Some of the earliest tests of the camera were
the photos that the research team took of

01:24:08.440 --> 01:24:09.440
each other.

01:24:09.440 --> 01:24:14.539
One by one, the doctors and their assistants
were photographed in neutral poses, smiling

01:24:14.539 --> 01:24:19.159
as if for a completely normal photo, then
they waited while the photos developed like

01:24:19.159 --> 01:24:20.939
normal polaroids.

01:24:20.939 --> 01:24:24.469
Most of the research team had minimal changes
in their photos.

01:24:24.469 --> 01:24:27.639
One was shown slouched in his chair, drinking
from a flask.

01:24:27.639 --> 01:24:32.260
One was shown in her civilian clothes, getting
ready to go home from work.

01:24:32.260 --> 01:24:36.429
One doctor was in the exact same pose, but
with a different colored tie on.

01:24:36.429 --> 01:24:40.989
The last assistant photographed, however,
had their picture come out wildly different

01:24:40.989 --> 01:24:42.810
than how they were posed.

01:24:42.810 --> 01:24:47.789
Their desire revealed by the camera was so
shocking that it had to be redacted, and the

01:24:47.789 --> 01:24:51.670
assistant was placed on temporary psychiatric
leave.

01:24:51.670 --> 01:24:55.539
Following this first successful test, the
doctor in charge of the project ordered a

01:24:55.539 --> 01:25:00.739
second round of tests to be conducted, this
time on a series of D-class personnel.

01:25:00.739 --> 01:25:05.179
A picture of one D-class, who was photographed
while eating in the cafeteria, showed up as

01:25:05.179 --> 01:25:08.250
scuba diving on vacation with his wife and
child.

01:25:08.250 --> 01:25:10.789
He was allowed to keep the picture afterwards.

01:25:10.789 --> 01:25:15.349
Another had a similar result - he was photographed
in a neutral pose like the members of the

01:25:15.349 --> 01:25:19.289
research team had been, and when the picture
developed, the D-Class was seen holding a

01:25:19.289 --> 01:25:23.689
smiling baby whom he identified as his one-year-old
daughter.

01:25:23.689 --> 01:25:29.559
After that, the results of the SCP - 978 tests
started to get a little… well, weird.

01:25:29.559 --> 01:25:35.719
A notoriously twisted D-class known as 7294
was photographed in his cell, and when the

01:25:35.719 --> 01:25:40.810
polaroid developed, he was in the same cell,
playing a cello made out of a dismembered

01:25:40.810 --> 01:25:42.380
mannequin.

01:25:42.380 --> 01:25:50.389
D-217-017, was a late stage victim of SCP-217,
a virus that turns organic matter into metal.

01:25:50.389 --> 01:25:55.140
You would assume that her innermost desire
would be to be cured of her disease, but when

01:25:55.140 --> 01:26:00.900
she was photographed in her cell, the resulting
polaroid showed her completely made of metal,

01:26:00.900 --> 01:26:04.090
kneeling and praying at the base of a black
obelisk.

01:26:04.090 --> 01:26:09.260
One D-class, who had been rendered comatose
and was on life support, was photographed

01:26:09.260 --> 01:26:10.849
in their hospital room.

01:26:10.849 --> 01:26:15.119
Their picture showed them as only a limp,
deflated skin in their photo.

01:26:15.119 --> 01:26:19.539
The photograph of another D-class, who had
become increasingly listless and apathetic

01:26:19.539 --> 01:26:24.510
since their integration into the D-class program,
resulted in a picture that was exactly the

01:26:24.510 --> 01:26:29.889
same as they appeared in reality, except the
light in their cell was slightly dimmer.

01:26:29.889 --> 01:26:34.179
Intrigued by these results, the research team
wanted to see how the camera would react to

01:26:34.179 --> 01:26:38.861
SCP-148, a type of metal that blocks the psychic
properties of other SCPs.

01:26:38.861 --> 01:26:44.699
A helmet was made from the material, and placed
on a D-class who was given an adult magazine

01:26:44.699 --> 01:26:47.010
to read while his photo was taken.

01:26:47.010 --> 01:26:50.469
When the photo was developed, it was extremely
blurry.

01:26:50.469 --> 01:26:55.360
Upon close analysis, the figure of the D-class
reading the magazine could still be made out,

01:26:55.360 --> 01:26:59.389
and around him the faint images of several
nude people could also be seen.

01:26:59.389 --> 01:27:03.039
The research team next wanted to see if the
results were the same when the camera was

01:27:03.039 --> 01:27:04.829
used on animals.

01:27:04.829 --> 01:27:09.030
Photos of the lab mice and rabbits showed
them eating or mating in their respective

01:27:09.030 --> 01:27:10.030
polaroids.

01:27:10.030 --> 01:27:14.429
A zebra finch was shown escaping its cage,
while a guard dog and its handler were shown

01:27:14.429 --> 01:27:16.329
playing fetch in the park.

01:27:16.329 --> 01:27:20.760
When cockroaches were photographed, there
was no difference visible between the picture

01:27:20.760 --> 01:27:21.760
and reality.

01:27:21.760 --> 01:27:27.679
But the most exciting test results came when
the camera was tested on other SCPs.

01:27:27.679 --> 01:27:32.400
For a few of the SCPs tested, there was no
visible difference between the picture and

01:27:32.400 --> 01:27:33.400
reality.

01:27:33.400 --> 01:27:41.789
This was the case for SCP-173 the Sculpture,
SCP-343 nicknamed God, SCP-014 - an immortal

01:27:41.789 --> 01:27:49.409
man who is, over time, being turned into concrete,
and SCP-063 - the world's best toothbrush.

01:27:49.409 --> 01:27:55.559
When SCP-035 - better known as the Possessive
Mask - was photographed in its glass case,

01:27:55.559 --> 01:28:00.679
the picture showed an unidentified individual
wearing the mask, sitting on a throne and

01:28:00.679 --> 01:28:03.900
surrounded by three masked corpses.

01:28:03.900 --> 01:28:09.939
The team took a picture of SCP-043 - a haunted
copy of The White Album that was being interrogated

01:28:09.939 --> 01:28:11.469
while on a turntable.

01:28:11.469 --> 01:28:14.719
In the picture, the album was being returned
to its sleeve.

01:28:14.719 --> 01:28:19.739
They then photographed SCP-049, the Plague
Doctor, standing in his cell.

01:28:19.739 --> 01:28:24.320
In the picture, the plague doctor is hugging
an unidentified small child, and surrounded

01:28:24.320 --> 01:28:28.440
by instances of SCP-049-2.

01:28:28.440 --> 01:28:34.570
When they took a picture of SCP-050 - a mischievous
statue of a monkey reading a book - the result

01:28:34.570 --> 01:28:38.979
was predictably playful, given that SCP's
history of pulling pranks.

01:28:38.979 --> 01:28:43.429
The photo that came out of the camera showed
the camera itself, with another picture of

01:28:43.429 --> 01:28:45.949
itself coming out of the developing slot.

01:28:45.949 --> 01:28:51.579
Microscopic analysis revealed that this recursive
photography kept going until the cameras in

01:28:51.579 --> 01:28:55.329
the pictures of the other cameras were too
small to see.

01:28:55.329 --> 01:29:01.079
The team next photographed SCP-053, the young
girl and the photo was taken as the young

01:29:01.079 --> 01:29:03.639
girl was drawing with crayons in her cell.

01:29:03.639 --> 01:29:09.719
In the picture, she was riding through a sunny
field on the back of her friend SCP-682.

01:29:09.719 --> 01:29:17.809
SCP-053 and SCP-682 were even wearing matching
bows, dresses, and pink nail polish.

01:29:17.809 --> 01:29:24.139
When they took a picture of SCP-096 - the
Shy Guy though, the picture showed SCP-096's

01:29:24.139 --> 01:29:26.459
cell with nothing in it.

01:29:26.459 --> 01:29:32.059
SCP-085 - the living 2D sketch known as Cassy
- was photographed tinkering with a drawn

01:29:32.059 --> 01:29:33.059
car.

01:29:33.059 --> 01:29:37.840
In the developed photo, Cassy was engaged
in the same activity, but both she and the

01:29:37.840 --> 01:29:39.840
car were now 3-dimensional.

01:29:39.840 --> 01:29:45.920
The team took a photo of SCP-106, the Old
Man, emerging from a wall within his cell.

01:29:45.920 --> 01:29:51.229
When the photo developed, it showed the old
man roaming a wheat field near an old farmhouse.

01:29:51.229 --> 01:29:57.539
From the porch of the farm house, an older
woman is greeting SCP-106 with open arms.

01:29:57.539 --> 01:30:03.650
They also took a photo of SCP-168 - a sentient
calculator - sitting on a table in its containment

01:30:03.650 --> 01:30:04.650
cell.

01:30:04.650 --> 01:30:09.389
In the picture, a teenage boy is seen doing
complex math homework using the calculator.

01:30:09.389 --> 01:30:14.209
Next to him on the table are thick textbooks
with titles like "Complicated Math", "Difficult

01:30:14.209 --> 01:30:17.219
Math", and "Math You Need Your Calculator
For".

01:30:17.219 --> 01:30:23.229
The photo of SCP-261 - a vending machine that
dispenses snack products from alternate universes

01:30:23.229 --> 01:30:29.440
- showed the SCP in its usual hallway, almost
completely buried in coins.

01:30:29.440 --> 01:30:35.639
SCP-507, an otherwise normal man who unwillingly
teleports between dimensions, was photographed

01:30:35.639 --> 01:30:37.510
while eating in the cafeteria.

01:30:37.510 --> 01:30:41.660
The developed picture showed him dressed as
a Foundation researcher, talking to other

01:30:41.660 --> 01:30:42.660
researchers.

01:30:42.660 --> 01:30:48.519
When SCP-682 was photographed, floating in
its containment tank, the resulting picture

01:30:48.519 --> 01:30:54.369
showed the SCP surrounded by the corpses of
all of the Foundation staff and mauling the

01:30:54.369 --> 01:30:56.360
person who had taken the photo.

01:30:56.360 --> 01:31:00.849
A researcher’s note accompanying this photo
reads “Well, that was predictable.”

01:31:00.849 --> 01:31:01.849
Yes.

01:31:01.849 --> 01:31:03.260
Yes it was.

01:31:03.260 --> 01:31:07.729
Just for fun of it, the team also tested the
camera's effects on a few other Foundation

01:31:07.729 --> 01:31:08.739
personnel.

01:31:08.739 --> 01:31:12.429
They took a photo of Dr. Bright while he was
arguing with Dr. Clef.

01:31:12.429 --> 01:31:17.999
The picture that came out showed a tombstone
engraved with the words "Jack Bright, Resting

01:31:17.999 --> 01:31:19.030
at Last."

01:31:19.030 --> 01:31:24.690
The team also took a photo of Dr. Clef as
he stormed out in a huff following the argument.

01:31:24.690 --> 01:31:29.239
Given that Clef's face cannot be photographed,
they were curious as to what the results would

01:31:29.239 --> 01:31:30.239
be.

01:31:30.239 --> 01:31:34.179
The picture showed little difference compared
to reality, save for the fact that Clef's

01:31:34.179 --> 01:31:38.670
head was replaced by an image of a hand making
a rude gesture.

01:31:38.670 --> 01:31:42.449
Upon closer examination of the photo, the
team also realized that there was a young

01:31:42.449 --> 01:31:47.320
girl in the background who, strangely, has
cloven hooves instead of feet.

01:31:47.320 --> 01:31:50.489
A young SCP-166 perhaps?

01:31:50.489 --> 01:31:54.350
The team then took a photo of Dr. Fisher holding
his pet hamster.

01:31:54.350 --> 01:32:00.260
Contrary to expectation, the picture revealed
not Dr. Fisher's desires, but the hamster's,

01:32:00.260 --> 01:32:05.769
showing the hamster sleeping peacefully in
its cage… with Dr. Fisher nowhere to be

01:32:05.769 --> 01:32:06.769
seen.

01:32:06.769 --> 01:32:12.320
As you can see from these test logs, the effects
of the camera are, well, inconsistent.

01:32:12.320 --> 01:32:17.519
With some photos showing very immediate, simple
whims, and others showing the subject's deepest

01:32:17.519 --> 01:32:19.590
and most secret desires.

01:32:19.590 --> 01:32:24.030
While the researchers working with SCP-978
seemed like they had a lot of fun getting

01:32:24.030 --> 01:32:29.119
to peek into the minds of all their coworkers
and test subjects, there's no telling what

01:32:29.119 --> 01:32:33.980
kind of pandemonium could be unleashed if
someone on the outside ever got a chance to

01:32:33.980 --> 01:32:34.980
use it.

01:32:34.980 --> 01:32:39.960
Thankfully the camera, which has been classified
as safe for obvious reasons, is kept securely

01:32:39.960 --> 01:32:43.790
in security locker H-J-12 at site 17.

01:32:43.790 --> 01:32:47.999
Which means none of us have to worry about
our own pictures taken by the Desire Camera

01:32:47.999 --> 01:32:49.249
leaking out.

01:32:49.249 --> 01:32:55.369
But if someone did get the camera out and
took your picture, what do you think they’d

01:32:55.369 --> 01:32:56.369
see?

01:32:56.369 --> 01:33:00.959
SCP-682 had escaped containment, and it was
all hands on deck at the SCP Foundation to

01:33:00.959 --> 01:33:03.619
try and stop the creature's rampage.

01:33:03.619 --> 01:33:08.889
All unarmed personnel were running to escape
before 682 had a chance to rip them apart,

01:33:08.889 --> 01:33:13.769
as the security team bravely fought to incapacitate
the hard-to-destroy reptile long enough to

01:33:13.769 --> 01:33:20.320
return him to his acid tank. 682 was on an
all-out offensive, stomping through the SCP's

01:33:20.320 --> 01:33:24.329
item gallery and spewing acid at anyone who
came within range.

01:33:24.329 --> 01:33:30.030
People, items, and parts of the room alike
were melting and sizzling as 682 attacked.

01:33:30.030 --> 01:33:34.130
It was an absolute bloodbath, and you'd have
to have been insane to try and fight back

01:33:34.130 --> 01:33:40.441
against it. However, one being remained unfazed
by the chaos, and stood proud in the face

01:33:40.441 --> 01:33:45.889
of the omnicidal monster. It was another SCP,
one who had been broken free from its glass

01:33:45.889 --> 01:33:49.989
display case in the commotion.
“Who dares to disturb the Prime Minister

01:33:49.989 --> 01:33:53.909
Sinister?” It said, in a high tinny voice.
“I shall rip your eyes from their sockets

01:33:53.909 --> 01:33:55.840
and force you to eat them!”

01:33:55.840 --> 01:34:00.630
SCP 682 stopped to see who had threatened
him. It was almost laughable that this thing

01:34:00.630 --> 01:34:05.449
had dared to make such a violent threat, because
there was no way that this little thing would

01:34:05.449 --> 01:34:11.110
be able to stand up to the unkillable 682.
But its size didn't stop it from trying to

01:34:11.110 --> 01:34:16.030
pick a fight all the same.
The SCP was a tiny robot made from junk, which

01:34:16.030 --> 01:34:19.900
looked more like a sculpture made from scrap
that was found on the side of the road than

01:34:19.900 --> 01:34:24.570
a functional automaton. Its head was made
of an upside down voltmeter, giving it the

01:34:24.570 --> 01:34:30.489
appearance of a smiling face, and its arms
were made of wrenches. It was capable of walking

01:34:30.489 --> 01:34:34.739
around, though it seemed to have difficulty
moving, as it was very top heavy.

01:34:34.739 --> 01:34:40.699
It shook its rusty fist at SCP 682 and continued
to threaten him, shouting - "You do not know

01:34:40.699 --> 01:34:44.389
the fury you have unleashed! RoboLord the
Destructor will end you!"

01:34:44.389 --> 01:34:50.730
SCP 682 swiped at the robot, annoyed by its
continued attempts to antagonize him. The

01:34:50.730 --> 01:34:56.099
robot toppled over and struggled to stand
again, but when it did, it ran for 682's feet.

01:34:56.099 --> 01:35:02.110
It started to grab at 682's toes, hitting
them with its wrench hands. As you might expect,

01:35:02.110 --> 01:35:09.570
this had almost no effect on 682.
"You do realize…you are…weak…pathetic"

01:35:09.570 --> 01:35:13.909
said 682, raising his claw to get a better
look at the annoying little robot.

01:35:13.909 --> 01:35:19.570
It responded- "Lies and slander! The Mayor
of Mayhem is the most powerful being in existence!"

01:35:19.570 --> 01:35:24.050
before promptly losing its grip on 682's claw
and falling to the floor.

01:35:24.050 --> 01:35:29.469
Now 682 was really getting tired of this thing.
He prepared to swipe at it again, this time

01:35:29.469 --> 01:35:34.480
using his full strength, which would certainly
smash the robot to pieces. But, luckily for

01:35:34.480 --> 01:35:40.239
the robot, its pestering had distracted 682
just long enough for Foundation security to

01:35:40.239 --> 01:35:41.820
sneak up on him.

01:35:41.820 --> 01:35:46.460
Before 682 had a chance to smash the robot,
the Foundation fired on him with a volley

01:35:46.460 --> 01:35:52.539
of rockets, reducing him to a misshapen lump.
The security team collected up 682's remains,

01:35:52.539 --> 01:35:57.519
ready to put them into a backup acid tank,
but the task was made slightly more difficult

01:35:57.519 --> 01:36:02.320
by the fact that the robot was running around
underfoot, trying in vain to now attack them

01:36:02.320 --> 01:36:03.810
instead.

01:36:03.810 --> 01:36:10.100
What was this strange little robot that thought
it could attack the unkillable lizard, 682?

01:36:10.100 --> 01:36:16.840
Meet SCP-1370, appropriately nicknamed “The
Pesterbot” by Foundation personnel. Pesterbot

01:36:16.840 --> 01:36:21.110
is a small robot made of junk that displays
sentience and the ability to move despite

01:36:21.110 --> 01:36:23.400
having no power source.

01:36:23.400 --> 01:36:29.400
Everything about SCP-1370 defies common sense.
The voltmeter that serves as its head contains

01:36:29.400 --> 01:36:34.820
no sensors, but it seems unable to see if
the voltmeter is covered. Its arms and legs

01:36:34.820 --> 01:36:39.150
are made of wrenches and its wooden torso
contains a speaker which it communicates through

01:36:39.150 --> 01:36:41.079
in a tinny, monotone voice.

01:36:41.079 --> 01:36:49.460
Pesterbot lives in SCP Gallery 27, in a glass
display case which is 125 cm tall, 50 cm wide,

01:36:49.460 --> 01:36:55.699
and 75 cm long. Level 2 personnel and higher
are allowed to remove the robot from containment

01:36:55.699 --> 01:37:00.010
at their discretion, but penalties will be
incurred for anyone who doesn't return to

01:37:00.010 --> 01:37:01.060
its case.

01:37:01.060 --> 01:37:06.539
Due to its impractical, top-heavy design,
Pesterbot falls over frequently when it walks

01:37:06.539 --> 01:37:10.690
around. This led the foundation to believe
that he was created as an art project and

01:37:10.690 --> 01:37:15.880
was later somehow imbued with anomalous properties,
rather than being made with the intent of

01:37:15.880 --> 01:37:17.409
being sentient.

01:37:17.409 --> 01:37:21.679
Pesterbot has demonstrated a high capacity
for learning, having been taught how to speak

01:37:21.679 --> 01:37:26.380
in English, French, and Latin. However, the
major factor hampering attempts to further

01:37:26.380 --> 01:37:30.760
test its intelligence has nothing to do with
its robotic processing power.

01:37:30.760 --> 01:37:33.539
No, it’s because of its poor attitude.

01:37:33.539 --> 01:37:39.630
Pesterbot's encounter with SCP-682 and the
cockiness it expressed in the moment wasn’t

01:37:39.630 --> 01:37:44.940
an aberration, this SCP really believes it's
a killing machine, and as a result, it will

01:37:44.940 --> 01:37:50.749
pick a fight with anyone and anything that
moves. This even includes its own reflection

01:37:50.749 --> 01:37:55.840
- and as a result the glass of its container
must be made as non-reflective as possible

01:37:55.840 --> 01:38:01.290
to prevent the robot from damaging the case
or itself in attempts to fight its mirror

01:38:01.290 --> 01:38:02.290
self.

01:38:02.290 --> 01:38:07.400
Though its most commonly used nickname in
the Foundation is Pesterbot, SCP-1370 also

01:38:07.400 --> 01:38:13.709
goes by a variety of self-given epithets,
including Doom Bot 2000, Robolord the Destructor,

01:38:13.709 --> 01:38:18.949
and Darth Claw Killflex. It can be made to
add new names to this list through encouragement

01:38:18.949 --> 01:38:23.790
by staff, and over time they have managed
to add the name Pesterbot, as well as the

01:38:23.790 --> 01:38:28.709
even more ridiculous “Patheticon the Garglemost”,
to its lexicon of names.

01:38:28.709 --> 01:38:34.160
As you may have surmised, Pesterbot is classified
as Safe and is treated by most SCP foundation

01:38:34.160 --> 01:38:39.050
employees as a humorous oddity rather than
a legitimate threat. Many tests have been

01:38:39.050 --> 01:38:43.400
done on Pesterbot, and they've all conclusively
determined that the robot is incapable of

01:38:43.400 --> 01:38:46.309
inflicting any damage to its opponents.

01:38:46.309 --> 01:38:50.959
In fact, Pesterbot is more of a danger to
itself than to anything around it. Both because

01:38:50.959 --> 01:38:56.099
it's incredibly clumsy and awkward, and because
it frequently picks fights with other SCPs

01:38:56.099 --> 01:38:58.719
who are far more powerful than it.

01:38:58.719 --> 01:39:03.230
One such scenario that could've gone far worse
for Pesterbot than it did was its encounter

01:39:03.230 --> 01:39:10.499
with SCP-846, also known as Robo-Dude, one
of the many Dr. Wondertainment products currently

01:39:10.499 --> 01:39:16.360
kept in Foundation containment. Robo-Dude
is an ordinary-looking toy robot that, upon

01:39:16.360 --> 01:39:22.939
request, can produce up to 350 “robo-accessories”
that function as real weapons.

01:39:22.939 --> 01:39:27.449
Robo-Dude can deploy everything from a rocket
launcher to a flamethrower to a gun that shoots

01:39:27.449 --> 01:39:32.610
out an unknown species of insect that can
chew through wood. However, Robo-Dude seems

01:39:32.610 --> 01:39:38.260
to not be sentient, and is unable to use these
weapons unless asked to. That ultimately worked

01:39:38.260 --> 01:39:40.039
out in the favor of Pesterbot.

01:39:40.039 --> 01:39:45.800
During another SCP-682 escape, the two robots
were brought into contact as they both had

01:39:45.800 --> 01:39:50.739
been broken out of their respective containment
spaces during the brouhaha. Robo-Dude, searching

01:39:50.739 --> 01:39:56.300
for a Robo-Pal to play with, came upon Pesterbot,
who immediately started spouting its usual

01:39:56.300 --> 01:39:57.550
overdramatic threats.

01:39:57.550 --> 01:40:03.059
“I am the Crushmaster, doom to all I survey.”
Pesterbot said. “Gaze upon my might and

01:40:03.059 --> 01:40:07.540
weep. Identify yourself, that I might know
whose destruction I shall sow.”

01:40:07.540 --> 01:40:12.059
Robo-Dude, not programmed to know how to respond
to such a statement, simply responded by asking

01:40:12.059 --> 01:40:14.309
Pesterbot if it wanted to play.

01:40:14.309 --> 01:40:19.179
Pesterbot continued to trash-talk Robo-Dude,
until Robo-Dude decided the best way to play

01:40:19.179 --> 01:40:22.449
with its new pal was to engage in its Robo-Dance
mode.

01:40:22.449 --> 01:40:27.770
Pesterbot accepted the challenge, saying “Activate
all that you wish, but your fate is sealed.

01:40:27.770 --> 01:40:33.709
The Kill-o-tron can not be defeated. I shall
render you unto dust with my mad dancing skills."

01:40:33.709 --> 01:40:38.439
The two robots proceeded to engage in a dance
battle, which the awkwardly shaped Pesterbot

01:40:38.439 --> 01:40:44.179
failed miserably at. While Robo-Dude was a
competent dancer, Pesterbot could only gyrate

01:40:44.179 --> 01:40:48.739
pathetically, before it fell over and rolled
around on the ground, hopelessly out of time

01:40:48.739 --> 01:40:51.540
to the music coming from Robo-Dude's speakers.

01:40:51.540 --> 01:40:56.489
The song ended, and Robo-Dude declared - “Robo-dance
is complete, Robo-pal.”

01:40:56.489 --> 01:41:01.999
Pesterbot was unable to accept its failure,
and replied- "Ha. Pathetic one, you have been

01:41:01.999 --> 01:41:06.760
schooled in the art of the dance by none other
than Mechanobasher, Scourge of a Thousand

01:41:06.760 --> 01:41:10.630
Worlds. Kneel before me before I end your
worthless existence."

01:41:10.630 --> 01:41:15.699
Robo-Dude, unimpressed with Pesterbot's poor
sportsmanship, deployed its hydrogen cannon,

01:41:15.699 --> 01:41:20.760
which it was programmed to do whenever it
detected a sore loser. Fortunately for Pesterbot,

01:41:20.760 --> 01:41:24.540
”hydrogen cannon” was just the name for
Robo-Dude's water pistol.

01:41:24.540 --> 01:41:29.159
While Pesterbot will attempt to fight anything
that moves, the truth is, this robot will

01:41:29.159 --> 01:41:34.360
attack virtually anything it perceives as
being even slightly alive. This is perhaps

01:41:34.360 --> 01:41:39.030
best illustrated by one of the tests of Pesterbot's
abilities that involved putting a small speaker

01:41:39.030 --> 01:41:43.150
at the base of a potted houseplant and speaking
through it from another room.

01:41:43.150 --> 01:41:47.749
The plant was placed across from Pesterbot
in the testing chamber and the interaction

01:41:47.749 --> 01:41:52.300
was monitored by researchers from outside.
Researcher Davies spoke through the speaker

01:41:52.300 --> 01:41:57.320
in the plant pot. He asked Pesterbot if it
could hear him, and it answered - “Who dares.

01:41:57.320 --> 01:42:02.229
All souls will burn. You will feel the sharp
sting of my wrath. Identify yourself so that

01:42:02.229 --> 01:42:05.179
I may sing damnation upon you as you die.”

01:42:05.179 --> 01:42:09.790
The robot began approaching the plant. Davies,
speaking as the plant, identified himself,

01:42:09.790 --> 01:42:14.880
“I am a split-leaf philodendron, a semi-woody
shrub with large glossy leaves.”

01:42:14.880 --> 01:42:19.479
At this point, he had to try very hard not
to laugh at the absurdity of this test, and

01:42:19.479 --> 01:42:20.829
the robot's reaction.

01:42:20.829 --> 01:42:24.499
He continued “These leaves can grow up to
three feet long.”

01:42:24.499 --> 01:42:28.639
Pesterbot used its wrench arms to try and
wrestle with the leaves, but was bested by

01:42:28.639 --> 01:42:34.050
the mighty plant and unable to cause any damage.
Enraged by its failure, it said “Your mockery

01:42:34.050 --> 01:42:38.780
spells your doom. I have arrived. You will
be crushed betwixt my digits.”

01:42:38.780 --> 01:42:43.760
Pesterbot then fell over and was unable to
right itself. It struggled and spent 6 minutes

01:42:43.760 --> 01:42:48.579
trying to stand before its flailing knocked
over the plant, which did nothing to help

01:42:48.579 --> 01:42:52.619
and in fact pinned the robot to the ground.
It was at this point that the researchers,

01:42:52.619 --> 01:42:57.119
who had taken time to compose themselves after
several laughing fits, entered the chamber

01:42:57.119 --> 01:43:02.159
and removed Pesterbot in order to place it
back in its containment case.

01:43:02.159 --> 01:43:06.869
Despite how non-threatening Pesterbot is,
there is actually one situation in the Foundation's

01:43:06.869 --> 01:43:10.519
history where it has actually posed a somewhat
serious threat.

01:43:10.519 --> 01:43:16.090
When Mobile Task Forces were sent in to rescue
survivors of the events at Site-13, also known

01:43:16.090 --> 01:43:21.469
as SCP-1730, they were attacked by alternate
universe versions of a variety of creatures

01:43:21.469 --> 01:43:23.869
kept in Foundation containment.

01:43:23.869 --> 01:43:28.419
One of these creatures was Pesterbot, who
had in that universe somehow gained control

01:43:28.419 --> 01:43:33.690
of a larger mechanical body constructed of
discarded pieces of machinery. It threw other

01:43:33.690 --> 01:43:38.170
pieces of metal scrap at the task force members
as they tried to leave the site, shouting

01:43:38.170 --> 01:43:44.170
in a much deeper and more intimidating voice
- “I am reborn to breathe devastation upon

01:43:44.170 --> 01:43:51.939
this fetid Earth. Pitiful humans. You will
feel the dark sting of my neverending torment.”

01:43:51.939 --> 01:43:57.219
Members of the task force could see the original
Pesterbot body on top of the larger metal

01:43:57.219 --> 01:43:59.590
construct, waving its arms madly.

01:43:59.590 --> 01:44:04.590
The task force opened fire, to little effect.
Pesterbot tossed another piece of scrap at

01:44:04.590 --> 01:44:09.409
them, just narrowly missing. One task force
member threw a frag grenade at the robot,

01:44:09.409 --> 01:44:11.739
which it caught, blowing up its hand.

01:44:11.739 --> 01:44:16.179
Another one was able to jump into the air
and reach the tiny robot atop the larger body,

01:44:16.179 --> 01:44:18.639
knocking it against the wall and shattering
it.

01:44:18.639 --> 01:44:23.920
Even in the reality where Pesterbot was able
to build itself a larger body, it still ultimately

01:44:23.920 --> 01:44:29.349
wasn't able to put up that much of a fight.
Poor Pesterbot. Doomed to be a failure in

01:44:29.349 --> 01:44:32.869
this, and apparently, every other reality.

01:44:32.869 --> 01:44:38.239
That's the story of SCP 1370, also known as
the Pesterbot, one of the most hilariously

01:44:38.239 --> 01:44:43.070
harmless anomalous entities that the foundation
currently has in containment. Perhaps one

01:44:43.070 --> 01:44:47.809
day he’ll achieve his goal of conquering
the universe, he just has to figure out how

01:44:47.809 --> 01:44:50.659
to conquer his toy box first.

01:44:50.659 --> 01:44:57.639
It was the year 2000 and Seven-year-old Xenia
Chau was like a lot of children her age - bright,

01:44:57.639 --> 01:44:58.639
but ignored.

01:44:58.639 --> 01:45:03.519
She had a youthful enthusiasm for knowledge
and learning, and with the right encouragement,

01:45:03.519 --> 01:45:09.150
it was obvious she’d go on to do great things,
but her parents were both working two jobs

01:45:09.150 --> 01:45:14.550
apiece to make ends meet, so outside of school
hours, little Xenia spent a lot of her time

01:45:14.550 --> 01:45:15.659
alone.

01:45:15.659 --> 01:45:20.309
She learned to cook and clean for herself
since it would often be way past her bedtime

01:45:20.309 --> 01:45:22.830
when her parents finally got home from work.

01:45:22.830 --> 01:45:26.829
They communicated largely through the sticky
notes left for her on the fridge before they

01:45:26.829 --> 01:45:28.829
left for work in the morning.

01:45:28.829 --> 01:45:34.010
It would be easy for someone like Xenia to
fall through the cracks, her potential wasted,

01:45:34.010 --> 01:45:37.999
and get forced into the same endless rat race
as her parents.

01:45:37.999 --> 01:45:43.550
And that probably would have happened, if
her brush with SCP-5094 hadn’t changed the

01:45:43.550 --> 01:45:46.090
course of her life forever.

01:45:46.090 --> 01:45:49.829
Like a lot of parents who couldn’t spend
as much time with their children as they’d

01:45:49.829 --> 01:45:55.099
like, Mr. And Mrs. Chau gave Xenia occasional
gifts as a way to try and make up for their

01:45:55.099 --> 01:45:56.099
absence.

01:45:56.099 --> 01:46:00.999
Mostly, they gave Xenia new books to add to
her growing collection, but their two-bedroom

01:46:00.999 --> 01:46:03.570
apartment only had so much space for books.

01:46:03.570 --> 01:46:08.810
A year ago, the family had bought a new desktop
computer to share.

01:46:08.810 --> 01:46:13.130
These days, this would be the answer to a
lonely bookworm’s prayers, but the Internet

01:46:13.130 --> 01:46:16.020
was still in its infancy back then.

01:46:16.020 --> 01:46:20.849
Everything changed when her parents bought
her a copy of the Miss J's Whiz Kidz Schoolhouse

01:46:20.849 --> 01:46:21.849
CD-ROM.

01:46:21.849 --> 01:46:25.739
Miss J's Whiz Kidz Schoolhouse was never a
popular program.

01:46:25.739 --> 01:46:30.780
Produced by Shoot the Moons Software in 1999,
the game sold poorly on the CD-ROM market

01:46:30.780 --> 01:46:34.469
for five years until the company filed for
bankruptcy in 2004.

01:46:34.469 --> 01:46:37.039
But that didn’t matter to Xenia.

01:46:37.039 --> 01:46:41.820
As far as she was concerned, receiving a copy
of Miss J's Whiz Kidz Schoolhouse was nothing

01:46:41.820 --> 01:46:45.699
short of a miracle - and she was far more
right than she knew.

01:46:45.699 --> 01:46:50.900
She didn’t have just any piece of primitive
educational software on her hands.

01:46:50.900 --> 01:46:54.499
Xenia Chau was playing with magic.

01:46:54.499 --> 01:46:58.889
After the software loaded, a cheerful figure
appeared on Xenia’s monitor.

01:46:58.889 --> 01:47:05.099
This was Miss J, a stylized 2D teacher in
a low-res but colorful 3D classroom.

01:47:05.099 --> 01:47:06.800
What can you learn from Miss J?

01:47:06.800 --> 01:47:08.229
Well, pretty much anything.

01:47:08.229 --> 01:47:13.800
And Xenia as a lonely kid without many friends
had all the time in the world.

01:47:13.800 --> 01:47:18.849
She spent days on end learning from Miss J
and soon Xenia went from a bright child to

01:47:18.849 --> 01:47:21.099
a bonafide child genius.

01:47:21.099 --> 01:47:25.789
Her largely absent parents barely even noticed
when their child started demonstrating an

01:47:25.789 --> 01:47:30.669
advanced knowledge of mechanical engineering
and a newfound fluency in Swahili.

01:47:30.669 --> 01:47:38.050
And not only did Miss J, now known to Xenia
as Miss Joyce, teach her students with supernatural

01:47:38.050 --> 01:47:41.240
effectiveness, she also seemed almost like
she was alive.

01:47:41.240 --> 01:47:48.960
She was a warm, calm, encouraging figure who
took a genuine, personal enthusiasm in the

01:47:48.960 --> 01:47:53.999
education and happiness of her students, more
than many real teachers, even.

01:47:53.999 --> 01:47:57.659
But sadly, not all good things last forever.

01:47:57.659 --> 01:48:02.550
When Xenia turned twelve, her family bought
a new computer, and the old Miss J's Whiz

01:48:02.550 --> 01:48:07.780
Kidz Schoolhouse CD-ROM was no longer compatible
with the new operating system.

01:48:07.780 --> 01:48:12.349
The disk gathered dust in a closet while Xenia
passed through high school and then got into

01:48:12.349 --> 01:48:14.239
a prestigious college.

01:48:14.239 --> 01:48:19.349
She received her PhD several years earlier
than expected and showed such promise in her

01:48:19.349 --> 01:48:23.419
scientific field that a certain organization
took notice.

01:48:23.419 --> 01:48:26.639
You guessed it: The SCP Foundation.

01:48:26.639 --> 01:48:31.719
The Foundation is only interested in adding
the best and brightest to their ranks, and

01:48:31.719 --> 01:48:36.239
thanks to the tutoring from Miss J, Xenia
Chau certainly fit the bill.

01:48:36.239 --> 01:48:41.400
She was assigned the role of Junior Researcher,
and little did she know, she was about to

01:48:41.400 --> 01:48:44.939
run into an old friend in her new line of
work.

01:48:44.939 --> 01:48:49.889
The Foundation first discovered evidence of
Miss J’s anomalous qualities while researching

01:48:49.889 --> 01:48:53.909
a series of strange forum posts in 2012.

01:48:53.909 --> 01:48:58.229
On a thread discussing abandonware, which
is software for which official support is

01:48:58.229 --> 01:49:03.489
no longer available, there were multiple reports
of a so-called “living character” in an

01:49:03.489 --> 01:49:06.840
old CD-ROM many of them had owned as children.

01:49:06.840 --> 01:49:11.889
Seeing as the technology to use the CD-ROM
was obsolete, Shoot the Moons had reported

01:49:11.889 --> 01:49:17.059
extremely low sales for the title, and nobody
on the forum had kept their copy, the Foundation

01:49:17.059 --> 01:49:20.550
classified this apparent anomaly as “neutralized.”

01:49:20.550 --> 01:49:21.729
No problem.

01:49:21.729 --> 01:49:28.090
That was, until then Junior Researcher Xenia
Chau was briefed on this particular SCP ten

01:49:28.090 --> 01:49:29.440
years later.

01:49:29.440 --> 01:49:34.599
She remembered exactly what the forum posters
were talking about, and what’s more, she

01:49:34.599 --> 01:49:37.050
still had her old copy at home.

01:49:37.050 --> 01:49:39.689
The senior Foundation researchers were astounded.

01:49:39.689 --> 01:49:45.429
An opportunity to study this forgotten anomaly
had just fallen into their laps, and it was

01:49:45.429 --> 01:49:48.599
all thanks to their brilliant new Junior Researcher.

01:49:48.599 --> 01:49:54.090
Xenia’s superiors ordered her to bring in
her copy of the Miss J's Whiz Kidz Schoolhouse

01:49:54.090 --> 01:49:58.199
CD-ROM, and then, real testing began.

01:49:58.199 --> 01:50:03.940
And after rigorous examination of the software,
it appears, by all accounts, that Miss J really

01:50:03.940 --> 01:50:09.189
is the world’s greatest teacher - in spite
of the fact she’s a collection of pixels

01:50:09.189 --> 01:50:13.679
on a basic CD-ROM program from the tail end
of the 1990s.

01:50:13.679 --> 01:50:17.460
What Miss J seemed to specialize in was intensive
courses.

01:50:17.460 --> 01:50:22.519
She had the ability to make students certifiable
experts in almost any subject through courses

01:50:22.519 --> 01:50:28.249
that can last upwards of 30 hours, and spread
out over just a few days.

01:50:28.249 --> 01:50:32.159
But this isn’t a “students become so enraptured
in learning that they forget accounting for

01:50:32.159 --> 01:50:36.340
their most basic needs and experience a decline
in the process” story.

01:50:36.340 --> 01:50:41.269
Miss J’s lesson plans account for regular
bathroom, meal, and even recreation breaks

01:50:41.269 --> 01:50:42.530
for students.

01:50:42.530 --> 01:50:48.050
Her talents easily account for Xenia Chau’s
remarkable academic success, the same success

01:50:48.050 --> 01:50:51.159
that got her picked up by the SCP Foundation.

01:50:51.159 --> 01:50:56.360
Naturally, if they had a technology on their
hands that could reliably create experts and

01:50:56.360 --> 01:51:02.530
geniuses with seemingly no negative consequences,
the Foundation knew that Miss J and what she

01:51:02.530 --> 01:51:08.489
had to teach could be immensely valuable in
their mission to effectively secure, contain,

01:51:08.489 --> 01:51:10.119
and protect other anomalies.

01:51:10.119 --> 01:51:15.420
But we’re not talking about the Chaos Insurgency
here: The Foundation would never start to

01:51:15.420 --> 01:51:19.269
use an anomaly for their own benefit without
proper testing.

01:51:19.269 --> 01:51:21.610
So, that’s exactly what they did.

01:51:21.610 --> 01:51:28.269
The experiments on SCP-5094 began at Site
- 15, and after ascertaining that Miss J posed

01:51:28.269 --> 01:51:33.289
no real threat to her students, they recruited
a local elementary school to provide human

01:51:33.289 --> 01:51:37.429
test subjects closer to Miss J’s intended
demographic.

01:51:37.429 --> 01:51:41.619
The Foundation found that there were a few
constants between every lesson given by Miss

01:51:41.619 --> 01:51:43.650
J to one of her students.

01:51:43.650 --> 01:51:47.960
Before teaching the really mind-blowingly
complex stuff, she would always begin with

01:51:47.960 --> 01:51:53.380
a basic primer on letters, colors, and numbers
to make sure she and her students were all

01:51:53.380 --> 01:51:55.610
on the same page.

01:51:55.610 --> 01:52:00.380
Another constant was that all her students
would refer to her as some variation of “Miss

01:52:00.380 --> 01:52:05.899
J” with examples including the names "Miss
Julie", "Miss Jenny", and "Miss Joy".

01:52:05.899 --> 01:52:10.909
One experiment was performed on Amy Myers,
a little girl from the third grade.

01:52:10.909 --> 01:52:16.289
Her academic record showed that she was a
bright and eager student, but she was described

01:52:16.289 --> 01:52:19.149
by her teachers as being especially shy.

01:52:19.149 --> 01:52:24.289
Amy referred to Miss J as “Miss Janie”,
and asked to be given a lesson on her favorite

01:52:24.289 --> 01:52:26.090
animal - cats.

01:52:26.090 --> 01:52:31.479
Of course, Miss J gladly obliged, and gave
Amy a fifteen hour lesson split over the course

01:52:31.479 --> 01:52:34.999
of two days which the Foundation closely observed.

01:52:34.999 --> 01:52:40.959
By the time the lesson was completed, the
results were truly astonishing: Amy demonstrated

01:52:40.959 --> 01:52:47.439
knowledge of feline behavior, diet, and physiology
on the level of professional animal behavioral

01:52:47.439 --> 01:52:48.439
scientists.

01:52:48.439 --> 01:52:52.709
She became upset when the session ended and
the program was switched off, having become

01:52:52.709 --> 01:52:57.149
attached to Miss J. No further anomalous effects
were reported.

01:52:57.149 --> 01:53:01.269
The next subject was a student from the second
grade named Devon Williams.

01:53:01.269 --> 01:53:07.429
Devon had a poor academic record, and behavioral
issues stemming from several learning disabilities.

01:53:07.429 --> 01:53:12.189
In the past, teachers had reported Devon having
real difficulty engaging with their lessons,

01:53:12.189 --> 01:53:17.550
and the Foundation wanted to see if Miss J’s
supernatural teaching abilities fared any

01:53:17.550 --> 01:53:18.550
better.

01:53:18.550 --> 01:53:23.000
Devon chose to be educated on the subject
of trains, and was given a fifteen hour course

01:53:23.000 --> 01:53:25.579
on the subject spread over two days.

01:53:25.579 --> 01:53:31.630
Devon had no difficulty engaging with these
lessons, and after their conclusion, he displayed

01:53:31.630 --> 01:53:36.540
a level of knowledge on railway engineering
comparable to a graduate-level education on

01:53:36.540 --> 01:53:37.540
the subject.

01:53:37.540 --> 01:53:42.729
Devon was so engaged in his lessons that he
had to be physically removed from the room

01:53:42.729 --> 01:53:47.929
once the course had completed, because he’d
become so attached to his new teacher.

01:53:47.929 --> 01:53:52.780
The Foundation were feeling extremely optimistic
about the prospect of using Miss J to train

01:53:52.780 --> 01:53:59.219
potential recruits, seeing as she seemed to
be able to teach even the most difficult juvenile

01:53:59.219 --> 01:54:00.219
subjects.

01:54:00.219 --> 01:54:05.369
However, the Foundation needed to prove that
Miss J could be just as effective in teaching

01:54:05.369 --> 01:54:06.369
adults.

01:54:06.369 --> 01:54:12.929
For this next test they recruited D-14417,
a 24 year old member of D-Class personnel

01:54:12.929 --> 01:54:18.059
who described himself as a poor student, and
tested poorly on pre-screening attentiveness

01:54:18.059 --> 01:54:19.570
and focus evaluations.

01:54:19.570 --> 01:54:23.949
He was the perfect candidate for the first
adult test of Miss J.

01:54:23.949 --> 01:54:29.400
To the delight of the Foundation higher-ups,
D-14417 excelled.

01:54:29.400 --> 01:54:34.770
Miss J made him a verifiable expert in Law,
and he was able to pass a mock bar exam with

01:54:34.770 --> 01:54:37.479
a grade of 310 after his course.

01:54:37.479 --> 01:54:42.999
Much like the children, he felt intense sadness
once the experiment ended - stating that Miss

01:54:42.999 --> 01:54:45.750
J was the best teacher he’d ever had.

01:54:45.750 --> 01:54:50.270
He’s since been selectively anesthetized,
released, and is pursuing a degree in criminal

01:54:50.270 --> 01:54:52.290
law with his new knowledge.

01:54:52.290 --> 01:54:54.969
Needless to say, The Foundation was impressed.

01:54:54.969 --> 01:55:00.059
The last thing they needed to know was who
exactly this Miss J truly was.

01:55:00.059 --> 01:55:04.699
To do this, they’d conduct an interview,
and thankfully, they already had someone who

01:55:04.699 --> 01:55:08.879
had a pre-established rapport with the subject:
Xenia Chau.

01:55:08.879 --> 01:55:13.460
When Xenia began the interview, Miss J recognized
her immediately.

01:55:13.460 --> 01:55:18.860
She was delighted to see one of her students
go on to find such success in her chosen field.

01:55:18.860 --> 01:55:24.120
Xenia questioned Miss J on what she truly
was, and Miss J responded that she honestly

01:55:24.120 --> 01:55:25.189
wasn’t sure.

01:55:25.189 --> 01:55:29.399
All she knew for sure was that she was passionate
about helping lonely children who love to

01:55:29.399 --> 01:55:33.699
learn embrace their education, that’s really
all there was to it.

01:55:33.699 --> 01:55:36.780
And it appears that she was telling the truth.

01:55:36.780 --> 01:55:42.199
So far the Foundation has found nothing that
hints at a nefarious motivation behind Miss

01:55:42.199 --> 01:55:43.199
J’s actions.

01:55:43.199 --> 01:55:46.480
It would appear that she truly does just want
to help children.

01:55:46.480 --> 01:55:52.139
Xenia, touched by the kindness that this Safe-Class
anomaly showed to her as a neglected child,

01:55:52.139 --> 01:55:57.690
and having now seen the positive impact she
had on children like her, thanked Miss J for

01:55:57.690 --> 01:56:03.079
all she’d done and left the interview happy
that there was an SCP out there who just wanted

01:56:03.079 --> 01:56:05.689
to change people’s lives for the better.

01:56:05.689 --> 01:56:09.709
And probably all of us would be a little better
off if there were more

01:56:09.709 --> 01:56:15.689
After all, this was one of the few SCPs who’d
changed a few good people’s lives for the

01:56:15.689 --> 01:56:23.100
better, and all of us can probably learn something
from the kindness and patience of Miss J.

01:56:23.100 --> 01:56:27.610
Meet Trevor Hawthorn, now known as D-4651.

01:56:27.610 --> 01:56:32.189
On the outside, he was an armed robber who
murdered two people during a convenience store

01:56:32.189 --> 01:56:33.669
shoot-out in Texas.

01:56:33.669 --> 01:56:39.070
But now, since being condemned to death, he’s
been picked up for D-Class testing by the

01:56:39.070 --> 01:56:40.439
SCP Foundation.

01:56:40.439 --> 01:56:46.380
Now also meet Junior Researcher Dr. Julia
Reed - an aspiring Foundation scientist with

01:56:46.380 --> 01:56:48.679
an undiagnosed heart condition.

01:56:48.679 --> 01:56:53.860
The kind of heart condition that doesn’t
mix well with a high-pressure job at The SCP

01:56:53.860 --> 01:56:54.860
Foundation.

01:56:54.860 --> 01:57:00.590
These two woke up on the morning of December
6th, 2011, completely unaware of the fact

01:57:00.590 --> 01:57:04.730
they were only hours away from causing one
of the most devastating containment breaches

01:57:04.730 --> 01:57:08.149
Site 19 had seen in years.

01:57:08.149 --> 01:57:14.459
Many people died that day, but thankfully
for everyone else, SCP-131 were there to save

01:57:14.459 --> 01:57:15.479
the day.

01:57:15.479 --> 01:57:19.789
When you think of a hero, you probably don’t
picture a pair of little cyborgs with one

01:57:19.789 --> 01:57:24.579
eye and the intelligence of a household cat,
but this is the tale of how two of the most

01:57:24.579 --> 01:57:30.880
unassuming anomalies at Site 19 managed to
save thousands of people from two of the Site’s

01:57:30.880 --> 01:57:33.039
most dangerous inmates.

01:57:33.039 --> 01:57:35.199
Open your eyes, and keep them open.

01:57:35.199 --> 01:57:38.219
If you so much as blink, it’s all over for
you.

01:57:38.219 --> 01:57:39.979
How long can you hold it?

01:57:39.979 --> 01:57:40.979
Difficult, right?

01:57:40.979 --> 01:57:46.189
Now imagine you’re having a staring contest
with an entity that can kill you if you dare

01:57:46.189 --> 01:57:49.199
to blink for even a fraction of a second.

01:57:49.199 --> 01:57:55.389
Or, even worse, a creature that could potentially
kill hundreds or even thousands of people

01:57:55.389 --> 01:57:59.080
if your attention drifts from it for any amount
of time.

01:57:59.080 --> 01:58:01.800
Try keeping your eyes open with that kind
of crushing pressure.

01:58:01.800 --> 01:58:06.499
We’re talking about two of the most deadly
Euclid and Keter Class anomalies out there

01:58:06.499 --> 01:58:13.670
- SCP-173, the Killer Sculpture, a violent
Euclid-class entity that is incapable of moving

01:58:13.670 --> 01:58:14.899
while being looked at.

01:58:14.899 --> 01:58:19.620
If ever it’s unobserved, it’ll snap the
neck of anyone nearby.

01:58:19.620 --> 01:58:25.590
SCP-689, known as Haunter in the Dark, is
an equally dangerous and even more attention

01:58:25.590 --> 01:58:27.519
demanding statue.

01:58:27.519 --> 01:58:34.380
These two entities are beyond dangerous - even
SCP-682 is terrified of the Killer Sculpture,

01:58:34.380 --> 01:58:39.480
and researchers have been considering the
use of 689 to potentially eliminate the hard-to-destroy

01:58:39.480 --> 01:58:41.610
reptile for quite some time.

01:58:41.610 --> 01:58:46.420
Their greatest concern though, is whether
the 30-centimeter-tall statue would cause

01:58:46.420 --> 01:58:51.149
too much collateral damage to Foundation personnel
in the process.

01:58:51.149 --> 01:58:57.320
Trevor Hawthorn was part of the three-man
D-class detail meant to clean out SCP-173’s

01:58:57.320 --> 01:58:58.939
containment chamber at regular intervals.

01:58:58.939 --> 01:59:03.539
While on cleaning duty, two D-Classes can
keep staring at the Sculpture while the other

01:59:03.539 --> 01:59:07.050
tidies up the cell, alternating turns to blink.

01:59:07.050 --> 01:59:12.489
But that morning, Trevor had woken up in his
containment cell with a killer migraine, and

01:59:12.489 --> 01:59:17.189
soon, that migraine would be killing far more
than just him.

01:59:17.189 --> 01:59:21.699
The containment procedures in 689’s cell
were also a three person job.

01:59:21.699 --> 01:59:27.719
689 is a small, green soapstone statue of
a skeletal being sitting on a throne, believed

01:59:27.719 --> 01:59:33.369
to be some form of underworld death deity
discovered by German archaeologists in India.

01:59:33.369 --> 01:59:38.159
This is a work of religious art that demands
your attention, or you and anyone else who’s

01:59:38.159 --> 01:59:42.909
ever seen this Keter-class nightmare will
suffer a horrifying fate.

01:59:42.909 --> 01:59:47.030
Anyone who’s ever seen the statue is “infected”
by its anomalous effects.

01:59:47.030 --> 01:59:51.369
It must be observed constantly, or someone
who’s seen it in the past will suddenly

01:59:51.369 --> 01:59:57.429
drop dead of a severe health issue like a
stroke or multiple rupturing organs.

01:59:57.429 --> 02:00:01.929
Like the God of Death the statue represents,
it appears on top of the dead body of whoever

02:00:01.929 --> 02:00:02.929
it just killed.

02:00:02.929 --> 02:00:08.209
If not continually paid attention to, it’ll
keep hopping from person to person until it’s

02:00:08.209 --> 02:00:10.439
killed everyone who’s ever looked at it.

02:00:10.439 --> 02:00:15.070
Its teleporting abilities, and the fact that
it poses a threat to so many, make this a

02:00:15.070 --> 02:00:16.960
truly formidable foe.

02:00:16.960 --> 02:00:22.439
It’s kept in a constantly-lit cell, and
is observed by two members of D-Class personnel

02:00:22.439 --> 02:00:24.099
at all times.

02:00:24.099 --> 02:00:29.599
But a crucial third party in the containment
of SCP - 689 is a member of personnel at Level

02:00:29.599 --> 02:00:30.999
2 or above.

02:00:30.999 --> 02:00:36.739
They remain in a control room, wearing a special
visor to prevent them from ever seeing 689

02:00:36.739 --> 02:00:39.019
and becoming infected themselves.

02:00:39.019 --> 02:00:43.670
If the containment fails, it’s their job
to throw the kill switch on the D-Class observers

02:00:43.670 --> 02:00:46.590
to prevent them from becoming vectors for
infection.

02:00:46.590 --> 02:00:49.980
Today, this job fell on Dr. Julia Reed.

02:00:49.980 --> 02:00:55.019
She was linked to the two observers via an
audio feed, allowing her to remain in constant

02:00:55.019 --> 02:01:00.030
contact with them, and she had her finger
on the activation key for a pair of explosive

02:01:00.030 --> 02:01:03.289
collars that were around the D-Class’ necks.

02:01:03.289 --> 02:01:07.079
Little did they know, Dr. Reed’s heart was
its own time bomb.

02:01:07.079 --> 02:01:13.139
Now you know what we’re up against: A snap-happy
Sculpture, and a teleporting death statue

02:01:13.139 --> 02:01:17.199
with a hit list containing everyone who’s
ever glanced at it.

02:01:17.199 --> 02:01:19.959
What can SCP - 131 bring to the table?

02:01:19.959 --> 02:01:26.209
The two small, cycloptic anomalies have only
one remarkable ability: They never blink.

02:01:26.209 --> 02:01:29.139
That and a soft spot for humans.

02:01:29.139 --> 02:01:34.149
These Safe-Class SCPs pose no threat to their
handlers, and can even form attachments to

02:01:34.149 --> 02:01:37.699
researchers and other staff who show affection
towards them.

02:01:37.699 --> 02:01:42.639
Of course, forming these bonds is discouraged
by Site 19’s Director because it can be

02:01:42.639 --> 02:01:45.689
distracting, but that doesn’t mean it doesn’t
happen.

02:01:45.689 --> 02:01:53.449
The two Eye Pods, known as SCP-131-A and SCP-131-B,
are identical in appearance except for their

02:01:53.449 --> 02:01:54.449
colors.

02:01:54.449 --> 02:01:57.659
A is burnt orange, and B is mustard yellow.

02:01:57.659 --> 02:02:02.229
The two of them appear to communicate with
one another via high-pitched squeaking noises,

02:02:02.229 --> 02:02:06.840
and also seem to have an innate ability to
detect danger occurring in the vicinity, as

02:02:06.840 --> 02:02:10.679
well as danger occurring near individuals
they’ve bonded with.

02:02:10.679 --> 02:02:15.149
Because of their inability to cause harm and
their generally affectionate demeanor, the

02:02:15.149 --> 02:02:20.269
Eye Pods are allowed to roam around Site 19,
provided they keep out of the way of researchers

02:02:20.269 --> 02:02:22.400
and stay out of restricted areas.

02:02:22.400 --> 02:02:27.340
They seem to pretty much stick to the rules,
though check-ins on A and B are required every

02:02:27.340 --> 02:02:29.219
hour, just to be safe.

02:02:29.219 --> 02:02:33.659
As the Eye Pods were moving freely around
the facility, Trevor and another D-Class maintained

02:02:33.659 --> 02:02:38.209
a visual on the Sculpture in its containment
chamber while a third man swept up the mixture

02:02:38.209 --> 02:02:41.960
of blood and excrement staining the concrete
floors.

02:02:41.960 --> 02:02:45.949
Things were going fine, until Trevor’s migraine
got the better of him.

02:02:45.949 --> 02:02:51.630
A sudden flash of intense pain shot through
his head, and in a moment of weakness he made

02:02:51.630 --> 02:02:53.369
a terrible mistake.

02:02:53.369 --> 02:02:58.399
With an audible groan of pain, Trevor closed
his eyes and forced his fingers to his temples.

02:02:58.399 --> 02:03:02.409
The groan had taken his fellow observer off
guard, and the man’s eyes flitted over to

02:03:02.409 --> 02:03:04.090
him for a fraction of a second.

02:03:04.090 --> 02:03:08.440
But a fraction of a second is all the Sculpture
needs.

02:03:08.440 --> 02:03:12.820
In an instant, Trevor and his fellow watcher
had their necks snapped, and the third D-Class

02:03:12.820 --> 02:03:16.539
was murdered before he even had the chance
to turn around.

02:03:16.539 --> 02:03:20.139
Containment protocol dictates that the door
is to be sealed behind the cleaning crew while

02:03:20.139 --> 02:03:25.409
they’re working with 173, but this time,
perhaps due to complacency, the guards had

02:03:25.409 --> 02:03:27.550
neglected to reinforce the door.

02:03:27.550 --> 02:03:32.039
They got their heads twisted a hundred and
eighty degrees for their trouble.

02:03:32.039 --> 02:03:34.239
SCP-173 was loose.

02:03:34.239 --> 02:03:38.820
Mobile Task Forces were dispatched to aid
in the re-containment effort as 173 began

02:03:38.820 --> 02:03:43.769
wreaking havoc around the facility, but things
were about to get even worse.

02:03:43.769 --> 02:03:47.719
It seemed like business as usual over at the
containment cell of SCP-689.

02:03:47.719 --> 02:03:53.860
Two D-Classes observed while Dr. Reed dictated
to them over an earpiece from her control

02:03:53.860 --> 02:03:54.860
center.

02:03:54.860 --> 02:03:59.959
However, what Dr. Reed thought were just minor
chest pains was actually the onset of heart

02:03:59.959 --> 02:04:00.959
failure.

02:04:00.959 --> 02:04:05.429
When the two D-Classes heard their supervisor
experiencing a fatal heart attack on the other

02:04:05.429 --> 02:04:08.260
end of the line, they began to panic.

02:04:08.260 --> 02:04:13.469
This meant their attention wasn’t entirely
on SCP-689, and they were further distracted

02:04:13.469 --> 02:04:20.260
by the chaos SCP - 173 was causing elsewhere
in the facility: murdering researchers, guards,

02:04:20.260 --> 02:04:23.829
and maintenance workers alike which led to
power outages.

02:04:23.829 --> 02:04:27.360
The lights in 689’s containment cell shut
down.

02:04:27.360 --> 02:04:33.239
Guards were dispatched to execute the observers,
as is protocol for 689 containment breaches,

02:04:33.239 --> 02:04:38.570
but the fact that resources were already stretched
thin by the 173 breach caused a fatal error

02:04:38.570 --> 02:04:41.459
in judgment from a guard posted nearby.

02:04:41.459 --> 02:04:46.139
In a panic, he opened the door to find one
D-Class dead with the statue perched on his

02:04:46.139 --> 02:04:50.229
body and the other one running straight for
him in blind fear.

02:04:50.229 --> 02:04:53.119
The two collided and tumbled out into the
hall.

02:04:53.119 --> 02:04:59.139
Both were now infected by 689’s anomalous
attention, and both were now doomed.

02:04:59.139 --> 02:05:04.099
Moments later, the two of them were dead,
the statue perched on their bodies, accidentally

02:05:04.099 --> 02:05:09.659
catching the eye of several researchers and
guards running to deal with the 173 situation.

02:05:09.659 --> 02:05:15.409
For these two deadly anomalies, it was becoming
an all-you-can-kill buffet.

02:05:15.409 --> 02:05:20.590
The staff of Site 19 were now dealing with
one anomaly that needed to be looked at constantly,

02:05:20.590 --> 02:05:25.090
and another that if you even glance at it,
you are effectively infected with a fatal

02:05:25.090 --> 02:05:26.219
disease.

02:05:26.219 --> 02:05:31.570
The Eye Pods, sensing an imminent danger nearby,
immediately sprung into action.

02:05:31.570 --> 02:05:36.469
It would be up to these cute, harmless anomalies
to save the terrified staff during this chaotic

02:05:36.469 --> 02:05:38.349
double-containment breach.

02:05:38.349 --> 02:05:43.749
In a nearby hallway, a fleeing Foundation
researcher heard the crunches of her colleagues’

02:05:43.749 --> 02:05:45.650
necks breaking behind her.

02:05:45.650 --> 02:05:47.460
173 was getting closer.

02:05:47.460 --> 02:05:49.909
This thing couldn’t be outrun.

02:05:49.909 --> 02:05:55.499
She turned, and saw the statue standing there,
just ten feet away from her, a dead researcher

02:05:55.499 --> 02:05:57.749
laying on the ground in front of it.

02:05:57.749 --> 02:06:00.989
She was locked in a deadly staring contest
with The Sculpture.

02:06:00.989 --> 02:06:05.409
How long she could survive was now dependent
on how long she could keep her eyes open,

02:06:05.409 --> 02:06:07.749
and it was getting harder by the second.

02:06:07.749 --> 02:06:09.570
She could feel her eyes drying.

02:06:09.570 --> 02:06:12.010
They burned under the ceiling lights.

02:06:12.010 --> 02:06:14.289
173 just waited.

02:06:14.289 --> 02:06:16.670
This wasn’t a contest she could win.

02:06:16.670 --> 02:06:21.349
In a final moment of terror, the researcher
was forced to finally close her eyes and she

02:06:21.349 --> 02:06:22.969
waited for the crunch.

02:06:22.969 --> 02:06:24.360
But it never came.

02:06:24.360 --> 02:06:27.679
Instead, she heard familiar high pitched squeaking
noises.

02:06:27.679 --> 02:06:35.840
She opened her eyes, crying tears of relief,
as she saw SCP-131-A sitting behind 173, watching

02:06:35.840 --> 02:06:39.159
it with its constant, unblinking gaze.

02:06:39.159 --> 02:06:43.789
The Killer Sculpture was paralyzed by a cheerful
little Safe-Class anomaly.

02:06:43.789 --> 02:06:48.570
Across the facility, a similar situation had
unfolded with SCP-689.

02:06:48.570 --> 02:06:54.539
The statue of death had claimed many lives,
but SCP-131-B had swooped in and frozen the

02:06:54.539 --> 02:06:57.959
statue in place with its never ending gaze.

02:06:57.959 --> 02:07:03.739
Soon after, a Mobile Task Force with vision-blocking
visors used advanced echo-location technology

02:07:03.739 --> 02:07:08.570
to collect SCP-689 and return it to its containment
cell.

02:07:08.570 --> 02:07:13.140
Everyone who’d seen the anomaly was, as
standard protocol dictates, gathered up for

02:07:13.140 --> 02:07:14.590
later termination.

02:07:14.590 --> 02:07:20.039
Meanwhile, a Mobile Task Force returned the
paralyzed 173 back to its containment cell

02:07:20.039 --> 02:07:21.369
with a forklift.

02:07:21.369 --> 02:07:26.769
No containment breach is ever a picnic, containment
breaches with multiple dangerous anomalies

02:07:26.769 --> 02:07:32.919
are even less so, but the heroic role that
SCP-131 played in bringing things back under

02:07:32.919 --> 02:07:35.519
control was indispensable.

02:07:35.519 --> 02:07:40.139
After all, it’s not just raw power that
counts when it comes to anomalies.

02:07:40.139 --> 02:07:45.590
The only anomalous power 131 needed to save
the entire site was its ability to keep looking

02:07:45.590 --> 02:07:47.289
when nobody else could.

02:07:47.289 --> 02:07:52.209
They’re so effective in this role that they’ve
been seriously considered for permanent roles

02:07:52.209 --> 02:07:57.189
as “wardens” for SCPs like 173 and 689.

02:07:57.189 --> 02:08:00.659
And in our opinion, they’re more than qualified.

02:08:00.659 --> 02:08:02.650
Does life imitate art?

02:08:02.650 --> 02:08:04.400
Or does art imitate life?

02:08:04.400 --> 02:08:07.669
It’s a question that has been asked throughout
human history.

02:08:07.669 --> 02:08:12.599
This philosophical debate is about the ways
art either reflects the world around us, or

02:08:12.599 --> 02:08:19.320
influences it, but in the case of SCP-085,
the idea of “art imitating life takes”

02:08:19.320 --> 02:08:22.119
on a far more literal meaning.

02:08:22.119 --> 02:08:27.229
This entity was created during an experiment
involving two separate SCPs.

02:08:27.229 --> 02:08:33.329
The first of these was SCP-067, which is a
fountain pen that, when held by a user, will

02:08:33.329 --> 02:08:36.300
take full control of the person’s hand and
arm.

02:08:36.300 --> 02:08:41.820
SCP-067 then either writes about or draws
something linked to the user holding it.

02:08:41.820 --> 02:08:46.769
The second of these SCPs was SCP-914, better
known as The Clockworks.

02:08:46.769 --> 02:08:51.780
This massive piece of anomalous machinery
will have various effects depending on what,

02:08:51.780 --> 02:08:56.780
or who, is placed inside of it and which of
its several settings is is chosen on the selection

02:08:56.780 --> 02:08:57.849
panel.

02:08:57.849 --> 02:09:03.610
After Test Subject-1101F was given the anomalous
fountain pen the result on the page was a

02:09:03.610 --> 02:09:08.999
simple female figure around six inches tall
and 1.5 inches wide.

02:09:08.999 --> 02:09:13.689
She was drawn wearing a summer dress, with
her long hair tied back in a ponytail and

02:09:13.689 --> 02:09:17.479
a single word was written underneath her,
“Cassandra”.

02:09:17.479 --> 02:09:22.969
As part of the experiment, the drawing was
placed inside of SCP-914 and the “fine”

02:09:22.969 --> 02:09:27.340
setting selected, this is the setting that
is known to improve the object placed inside

02:09:27.340 --> 02:09:28.670
of it in some way.

02:09:28.670 --> 02:09:34.619
For example a hunk of steel placed inside
will be transformed into a pile of steel carpet

02:09:34.619 --> 02:09:38.519
tacks - a “refined” version of the steel.

02:09:38.519 --> 02:09:43.739
When the drawing was placed inside, something
truly amazing happened.

02:09:43.739 --> 02:09:49.599
Cassandra came to life, or as she now prefers
to be called, “Cassy.”

02:09:49.599 --> 02:09:54.590
SCP-085, sometimes known as “Hand Drawn
Cassy”, is a completely sentient being.

02:09:54.590 --> 02:09:58.989
She is fully able to communicate - however,
it all has to be done non-verbally.

02:09:58.989 --> 02:10:03.439
Her voice cannot be heard by anyone beyond
the page where she was drawn, but she is able

02:10:03.439 --> 02:10:09.000
to utilize sign language or create writing
on the page in order to communicate with Foundation

02:10:09.000 --> 02:10:10.079
researchers.

02:10:10.079 --> 02:10:15.099
SCP-085 has been shown to also be capable
of understanding text that is written on the

02:10:15.099 --> 02:10:17.710
same paper she exists on.

02:10:17.710 --> 02:10:22.989
She is fully animated, aware of her own existence
and the limitations of being two dimensional

02:10:22.989 --> 02:10:23.989
in nature.

02:10:23.989 --> 02:10:30.090
According to profiling conducted by the SCP
Foundation, she has her own distinct personality.

02:10:30.090 --> 02:10:35.460
Cassy is good-natured and agreeable, displaying
a natural drive and motivation, but also seems

02:10:35.460 --> 02:10:39.949
to feel the burden of loneliness, living in
solitude on the page.

02:10:39.949 --> 02:10:44.159
It should be noted that any and all attempts
to recreate the same experiment that formed

02:10:44.159 --> 02:10:48.860
SCP-085 have failed to create the same or
similar results.

02:10:48.860 --> 02:10:54.919
Tragically, Cassy might be the only one of
her kind in existence, a creation of pure

02:10:54.919 --> 02:10:57.749
luck with no chance of making another.

02:10:57.749 --> 02:10:59.429
No wonder she feels lonely.

02:10:59.429 --> 02:11:04.110
While Cassy is limited to her two dimensional
form and has so far been unable to enter our

02:11:04.110 --> 02:11:08.969
three dimensional world, she has demonstrated
several different abilities on the page.

02:11:08.969 --> 02:11:13.719
Firstly, she is not solely confined to the
same paper she was first drawn on.

02:11:13.719 --> 02:11:17.570
SCP-085 is able to transfer herself from sheet
to sheet.

02:11:17.570 --> 02:11:22.260
If another page is placed flush with hers,
she will be able to simply step across onto

02:11:22.260 --> 02:11:23.619
this new page.

02:11:23.619 --> 02:11:29.239
However, there is a limit to what kind of
page Cassy is able to transfer herself onto.

02:11:29.239 --> 02:11:33.340
She could easily take a stroll through the
pages of today’s newspaper but can’t just

02:11:33.340 --> 02:11:38.199
wander onto someone’s family photos - or
anything made of cardboard, glass, or parchment

02:11:38.199 --> 02:11:39.639
for that matter.

02:11:39.639 --> 02:11:45.699
SCP-085 can only exist on paper or canvas,
and only when they are directly connected

02:11:45.699 --> 02:11:48.179
to her original page.

02:11:48.179 --> 02:11:52.960
According to Foundation testing, this is not
exclusive to blank pieces of paper either.

02:11:52.960 --> 02:11:57.820
If Cassy ever transfers herself onto a page
bearing a repeated pattern like a piece of

02:11:57.820 --> 02:12:01.919
wallpaper, then she will appear to be in the
foreground while everything else on the paper

02:12:01.919 --> 02:12:04.289
appears to be behind her.

02:12:04.289 --> 02:12:10.169
SCP-085 will perceive each page she “enters”
as a completely new place, from her point

02:12:10.169 --> 02:12:13.639
of view patterned pages seem to be like endless
space.

02:12:13.639 --> 02:12:18.010
Additionally, Cassy can also “travel”
to other pieces of artwork, and adopts the

02:12:18.010 --> 02:12:21.119
same art style of each new environment she
appears in.

02:12:21.119 --> 02:12:25.590
For example, transferring herself onto the
pages of a comic book will cause Cassy to

02:12:25.590 --> 02:12:29.659
be rendered in an artistic manner matching
that of her surroundings.

02:12:29.659 --> 02:12:34.570
The same occurs if she travels to an oil painting,
watercolor, or charcoal sketch.

02:12:34.570 --> 02:12:38.989
Interestingly, when appearing in comic book
form, Cassy’s thoughts and speech are visible

02:12:38.989 --> 02:12:43.429
through bubbles that are commonly used to
display text within the comic medium.

02:12:43.429 --> 02:12:47.899
Her size, and the angle she is viewed from,
also changes to match the different panels

02:12:47.899 --> 02:12:49.860
of the comic page she is on.

02:12:49.860 --> 02:12:55.790
At one point, SCP-085 was introduced by Foundation
personnel to a print copy of “Ascending

02:12:55.790 --> 02:12:58.659
and Descending”, by the famous Dutch artist
M.C.

02:12:58.659 --> 02:12:59.829
Escher.

02:12:59.829 --> 02:13:04.880
This painting is of a large building, with
its roof consisting of a looped, never-ending

02:13:04.880 --> 02:13:05.880
staircase.

02:13:05.880 --> 02:13:10.760
When she transferred onto the print of Escher’s
painting, SCP-085 curiously explored her new

02:13:10.760 --> 02:13:15.079
environment, and was able to ascend and descend
the staircase.

02:13:15.079 --> 02:13:19.039
The researcher gave Cassy the name of the
piece, and asked for her thoughts on it.

02:13:19.039 --> 02:13:21.030
She remarked “It’s pretty, I guess.

02:13:21.030 --> 02:13:22.849
Would make a neat exercise track.”

02:13:22.849 --> 02:13:28.129
When the researcher asked if she noticed anything
inconsistent about the staircase, Cassy replied

02:13:28.129 --> 02:13:33.199
“No, as far as I can tell it just loops
around down/up all the time.

02:13:33.199 --> 02:13:35.059
Why don't more staircases do that?

02:13:35.059 --> 02:13:36.629
It's pretty neat.”

02:13:36.629 --> 02:13:41.269
Following this, Cassy directly requested more
“impossible” objects or optical illusions

02:13:41.269 --> 02:13:44.539
be drawn on her page and made part of her
environment.

02:13:44.539 --> 02:13:49.310
Unfortunately, her request is still pending
review from the O5 Council.

02:13:49.310 --> 02:13:54.550
Being able to step from page to page, transferring
herself onto canvas or sheets of paper, is

02:13:54.550 --> 02:13:58.510
but one of SCP-085’s unique abilities.

02:13:58.510 --> 02:14:02.489
She can also interact with other drawn objects
on the same page she is on.

02:14:02.489 --> 02:14:07.949
If someone draws an item of clothing on her
page, or a vehicle, even food or drink, then

02:14:07.949 --> 02:14:11.639
Cassy would be able to wear, use, or consume
these.

02:14:11.639 --> 02:14:16.610
Objects drawn for her behave as if they were
real, but only when Cassy is directly interacting

02:14:16.610 --> 02:14:17.610
with them.

02:14:17.610 --> 02:14:21.169
The rest of the time, they remain still, just
as they were drawn.

02:14:21.169 --> 02:14:25.479
Once SCP-085 touches them, these items will
animate.

02:14:25.479 --> 02:14:30.360
This same rule even applies to anything drawn
to depict something in motion, for example

02:14:30.360 --> 02:14:34.409
trees being blown in the wind, or the waves
of an ocean.

02:14:34.409 --> 02:14:40.409
These will also stay perfectly still when
drawn, and only move when acted upon by SCP-085.

02:14:40.409 --> 02:14:46.179
However, much like her ability to transfer
from page to page, Cassy’s power over other

02:14:46.179 --> 02:14:49.260
two dimensional drawings has limits.

02:14:49.260 --> 02:14:53.070
Drawing anything that would normally be an
inanimate object within the real world will

02:14:53.070 --> 02:14:57.729
provide SCP-085 something that she can directly
interact with.

02:14:57.729 --> 02:15:02.409
But this doesn’t appear to be the case for
living beings, like another person or an animal

02:15:02.409 --> 02:15:07.669
that would have its own autonomy and freedom
of movement in our three dimensional reality.

02:15:07.669 --> 02:15:13.040
Animals and people drawn for Cassy to interact
with will remain as static, unmoving drawings,

02:15:13.040 --> 02:15:18.420
and will not become animated like she is,
even if drawn using SCP-067.

02:15:18.420 --> 02:15:22.989
She cannot impart any of her own sentience
or free will onto these drawings, and they

02:15:22.989 --> 02:15:26.079
remain still even when she touches them.

02:15:26.079 --> 02:15:30.070
You might think that drawings of other people,
whether they are animated or not, might help

02:15:30.070 --> 02:15:35.689
alleviate Cassy’s solitude, but if anything,
it just reminds her how alone she is.

02:15:35.689 --> 02:15:41.289
SCP Foundation researchers have noted that
SCP-085 is very friendly towards them and

02:15:41.289 --> 02:15:44.979
any subjects brought in to conduct experiments
with her.

02:15:44.979 --> 02:15:48.840
Visits from the three dimensional world outside
the page she inhabits seems to offer some

02:15:48.840 --> 02:15:50.979
relief to Cassy's loneliness.

02:15:50.979 --> 02:15:55.519
Through much of her behavior, she has shown
a fascination with our reality, and in particular

02:15:55.519 --> 02:16:00.340
she has an interest in cars, expressing that
she wishes she had the ability to work on

02:16:00.340 --> 02:16:01.340
them.

02:16:01.340 --> 02:16:05.709
This desire appears to be completely genuine
too, as shown when her photo was taken with

02:16:05.709 --> 02:16:12.459
SCP-978, the camera that reveals its subjects
inner desires, and in Cassy’s case, showed

02:16:12.459 --> 02:16:17.270
her as a fully realized 3-d version of herself
working on a car.

02:16:17.270 --> 02:16:22.099
SCP-085’s curiosity about the world beyond
the page is most likely due to how different

02:16:22.099 --> 02:16:28.329
it is from her everyday two dimensional existence,
but on at least one occasion, Cassy’s curiosity

02:16:28.329 --> 02:16:32.929
got the better of her and unintentionally
led to a containment breach.

02:16:32.929 --> 02:16:38.380
From the moment she was first drawn to life,
and even after her initial testing with researchers,

02:16:38.380 --> 02:16:44.519
SCP-085 seemed unaware that she was a two
dimensional being in a three dimensional world.

02:16:44.519 --> 02:16:49.570
Foundation security protocols regarding SCP-085
meant that no one on the research team assigned

02:16:49.570 --> 02:16:53.200
to Cassy was permitted to tell her the truth
about her 2-D nature.

02:16:53.200 --> 02:16:57.769
The truth about her existence was kept from
her with the best of intentions, as research

02:16:57.769 --> 02:17:04.000
staff did not want to cause SCP-085 any undue
distress or trigger a possible psychological

02:17:04.000 --> 02:17:05.000
snap.

02:17:05.000 --> 02:17:09.870
Anything that Cassy raised as an inconsistency
or discrepancy within “her world” on the

02:17:09.870 --> 02:17:14.921
page was explained by researchers to be the
result of her imagination or dreams, and research

02:17:14.921 --> 02:17:20.229
personnel attempted to convince SCP-085 that
she was in a scenario wherein she was the

02:17:20.229 --> 02:17:25.740
only human survivor, searching for others
in a post-apocalyptic environment.

02:17:25.740 --> 02:17:29.899
However misguided this decision to conceal
the truth might have been, it was at least

02:17:29.899 --> 02:17:32.819
done with Cassy’s best interests at heart.

02:17:32.819 --> 02:17:39.059
But a lie, as they say, is harder to maintain
than the truth, and keeping SCP-085 in the

02:17:39.059 --> 02:17:43.869
dark about her true nature arguably led her
to more hardship that may have been avoided

02:17:43.869 --> 02:17:46.649
if she had been allowed to know the truth.

02:17:46.649 --> 02:17:50.529
In the incident in question, a Foundation
researcher entered the room where the drawing

02:17:50.529 --> 02:17:56.600
pad Cassy resides was found, and they were
carrying a paper copy of SCP-085’s Special

02:17:56.600 --> 02:17:59.019
Containment Procedures Report.

02:17:59.019 --> 02:18:02.250
Given that she had already partaken in tests
where she had transferred herself to other

02:18:02.250 --> 02:18:07.269
paper and canvas surfaces, Cassy assumed that
this file was yet another new environment

02:18:07.269 --> 02:18:08.679
for her to explore.

02:18:08.679 --> 02:18:13.859
The researcher allowed the SCP-085 to make
direct contact with the report, and she was

02:18:13.859 --> 02:18:18.449
able to transfer over to the document before
the researcher realized their mistake.

02:18:18.449 --> 02:18:22.650
Whether this occurred accidentally, or if
this researcher intended to confront Cassy

02:18:22.650 --> 02:18:25.989
with the truth about what she was, is unknown.

02:18:25.989 --> 02:18:31.740
Nevertheless, Cassy found herself on the pages
of her own SCP Foundation file.

02:18:31.740 --> 02:18:35.859
The record of every test the research staff
had conducted, a full description of how she

02:18:35.859 --> 02:18:43.269
had first been drawn by SCP-067 and brought
to life by SCP-914, all clear as day, in black

02:18:43.269 --> 02:18:47.099
and white, Cassy’s own true nature was presented
to her.

02:18:47.099 --> 02:18:51.750
Immediately, the yarns that Foundation researchers
had spun about her surviving an apocalypse

02:18:51.750 --> 02:18:53.059
began to unravel.

02:18:53.059 --> 02:18:58.109
It was all a lie, meant to keep her in the
dark and prevent her from ever knowing that

02:18:58.109 --> 02:19:00.330
she was trapped in two dimensions.

02:19:00.330 --> 02:19:05.219
She returned to her original page shortly
later, but the damage was already done.

02:19:05.219 --> 02:19:09.570
Due to her having breached containment and
briefly escaped into her own file, a number

02:19:09.570 --> 02:19:13.880
of Foundation researchers proposed that SCP-085
be destroyed.

02:19:13.880 --> 02:19:16.559
There was always a risk of this happening
again.

02:19:16.559 --> 02:19:21.030
What would happen if Cassy unwittingly found
herself inside another file, with access to

02:19:21.030 --> 02:19:23.460
more of the Foundation’s sensitive information.

02:19:23.460 --> 02:19:30.090
However, the 05 Council decreed that SCP-085
was not to be terminated, allowing Cassy to

02:19:30.090 --> 02:19:33.099
continue to exist despite the breach.

02:19:33.099 --> 02:19:37.199
Ever since she learned the truth about herself,
signs of depression have begun to manifest

02:19:37.199 --> 02:19:38.690
in her behavior.

02:19:38.690 --> 02:19:42.740
Finding out you are a drawing, trapped in
two dimensions with no chance of ever having

02:19:42.740 --> 02:19:46.609
someone else for company, would be enough
to crush anyone’s spirit.

02:19:46.609 --> 02:19:51.360
But luckily, researchers have since managed
to uplift Cassy a little and offer her a welcome

02:19:51.360 --> 02:19:54.080
distraction from her unfortunate revelation.

02:19:54.080 --> 02:19:58.590
The optical illusions like the never ending
staircase she requested were quickly drawn

02:19:58.590 --> 02:20:00.150
into her environment.

02:20:00.150 --> 02:20:05.390
Additionally, given the interest she had shown
in a technical drawing of a 1964 Ford Mustang

02:20:05.390 --> 02:20:10.050
Convertible, SCP-085 has been allowed to assemble
a car of her own.

02:20:10.050 --> 02:20:14.149
By transferring each individual component
of the car from the blueprint to her page,

02:20:14.149 --> 02:20:20.109
Hand Drawn Cassy has been gradually building
her very own Mustang, to keep herself preoccupied

02:20:20.109 --> 02:20:22.430
from her life in cartoon motion.

02:20:22.430 --> 02:20:26.560
And in the end, if she can distract herself
and find that tiny bit of happiness, isn’t

02:20:26.560 --> 02:20:28.470
that all that matters?

02:20:28.470 --> 02:20:33.330
In a sense, we’re all trapped within our
own dimension, Cassy in her 2-D one, us in

02:20:33.330 --> 02:20:38.040
our 3-D world, filling our lives with hobbies
and entertainment, all in an effort to make

02:20:38.040 --> 02:20:43.069
sure that we never tug too hard at the threads
of our reality and find out there just might

02:20:43.069 --> 02:20:46.590
be much more out there that we’re missing.

02:20:46.590 --> 02:20:52.319
In the office of SCP Foundation Researcher
Yoshihiro Takenaka, there sits a small containment

02:20:52.319 --> 02:20:59.770
capsule filled with ash - all that’s left
of a neutralized SCP - 1762.

02:20:59.770 --> 02:21:02.050
These ashes don’t pose any harm.

02:21:02.050 --> 02:21:05.510
They won’t bite, burn, or assume control
of your mind.

02:21:05.510 --> 02:21:13.430
But few can hear the sad story of SCP - 1762
and not be haunted by its tragic and mysterious

02:21:13.430 --> 02:21:14.430
tale.

02:21:14.430 --> 02:21:19.210
It weighs heavily on the hearts and minds
of all who came into contact with it during

02:21:19.210 --> 02:21:22.479
its ultimately brief time in the Foundation’s
hands.

02:21:22.479 --> 02:21:29.060
And to think, it all started with a simple
little box with an even simpler message: “Here

02:21:29.060 --> 02:21:30.200
Be Dragons.”

02:21:30.200 --> 02:21:34.620
The box, to look at it, was really nothing
special.

02:21:34.620 --> 02:21:43.080
A simple cardboard box, 32 cm x 20 cm x 26
cm, spray painted silver inside and out.

02:21:43.080 --> 02:21:47.040
Its short message scrawled across the lid
in black permanent marker.

02:21:47.040 --> 02:21:51.410
It appeared on the doorstep of Foundation
Agent Scott Thomas, who - after determining

02:21:51.410 --> 02:21:56.830
it wasn’t a bomb, anthrax, or a deadlier
kind of anomaly - turned it into his superiors.

02:21:56.830 --> 02:22:01.149
This is when it became Yoshihiro Takenaka’s
little pet project.

02:22:01.149 --> 02:22:06.520
Safe Class SCPs are rare treats for any overworked
Foundation scientist.

02:22:06.520 --> 02:22:14.359
The box itself - known as SCP - 1762 - 1 - is
certainly important, but what’s really interesting

02:22:14.359 --> 02:22:17.050
is what resides within the box.

02:22:17.050 --> 02:22:21.090
If you opened the box yourself, you’d find
that… it’s empty!

02:22:21.090 --> 02:22:27.060
However when the box chooses to open itself,
it’s an entirely different story.

02:22:27.060 --> 02:22:32.590
The box would sometimes open and emit great
plumes of thick, black smoke that would quickly

02:22:32.590 --> 02:22:33.590
dissipate.

02:22:33.590 --> 02:22:38.979
Around twenty seconds after this, an SCP - 1762
- 2 would emerge from the darkness of the

02:22:38.979 --> 02:22:40.040
box.

02:22:40.040 --> 02:22:48.069
1762 - 2 is the collective name given to all
the beings that exit 1762 - 1, which are - as

02:22:48.069 --> 02:22:49.949
you may have guessed - dragons.

02:22:49.949 --> 02:22:57.140
Eastern, western, big, small, and presenting
in a rainbow of colours, these dragons appear

02:22:57.140 --> 02:23:02.310
to be living origami sculptures made from
kami paper - and have been known to fly together

02:23:02.310 --> 02:23:06.149
in large groups and interact playfully with
nearby humans.

02:23:06.149 --> 02:23:11.069
These little paper dragons would then swoop
around their containment chamber, delighting

02:23:11.069 --> 02:23:14.489
all who were fortunate enough to see them,
for up to three hours.

02:23:14.489 --> 02:23:19.090
At which point, smoke would begin pouring
out of the box once more, and the dragons

02:23:19.090 --> 02:23:20.279
would return home.

02:23:20.279 --> 02:23:25.199
They’d fly through the smoke, disappearing
past the rim of the box, and then the lid

02:23:25.199 --> 02:23:26.590
would close once more.

02:23:26.590 --> 02:23:31.529
The dates on which the box would open were
seemingly random and indeterminable, and didn’t

02:23:31.529 --> 02:23:34.220
appear to work by any kind of external logic.

02:23:34.220 --> 02:23:38.890
And what’s more, the box would sometimes
act as a hub of communication between this

02:23:38.890 --> 02:23:43.920
world and another - known simply as “Fantasy.”

02:23:43.920 --> 02:23:48.649
Messages written or carved into various materials
would appear on the lid of the box, mostly

02:23:48.649 --> 02:23:52.370
after instances of 1762 - 2 emerging.

02:23:52.370 --> 02:23:56.040
This communication, though, would always be
one way.

02:23:56.040 --> 02:24:00.109
Attempts to pass messages back through the
box never resulted in success.

02:24:00.109 --> 02:24:05.189
The Foundation staff could only be observers
of the strange world of Fantasy, never active

02:24:05.189 --> 02:24:06.899
participants.

02:24:06.899 --> 02:24:10.370
So why is this particular SCP considered so
tragic?

02:24:10.370 --> 02:24:15.380
We’re going to answer that question right
now, but just know that what is learned cannot

02:24:15.380 --> 02:24:19.210
be unlearned, as much as you might wish you
could forget.

02:24:19.210 --> 02:24:23.540
If you’re ready, then it’s time to learn
about a period of time that lasted just under

02:24:23.540 --> 02:24:29.620
a year, during which a strange and sad series
of events took place, now known as The Jabberwocky

02:24:29.620 --> 02:24:30.620
Event.

02:24:30.620 --> 02:24:35.100
An event that took “Here Be Dragons” from
Safe to Neutralized.

02:24:35.100 --> 02:24:40.920
You’ve seen that SCP - 1762 would communicate
with Foundation staff via written messages

02:24:40.920 --> 02:24:43.050
after each instance of the box opening.

02:24:43.050 --> 02:24:46.750
The very first message the box gave up after
arriving at the site read:

02:24:46.750 --> 02:24:48.399
“You have found us.

02:24:48.399 --> 02:24:49.399
Thank you.

02:24:49.399 --> 02:24:51.899
It has been so long since we last saw each
other, friends.

02:24:51.899 --> 02:24:55.180
The Peace has been upheld.

02:24:55.180 --> 02:24:59.220
The Giants and Behemoths have kept their word
and have not caused any trouble since you

02:24:59.220 --> 02:25:01.420
last came and gave the Order.

02:25:01.420 --> 02:25:02.600
We missed Your company.

02:25:02.600 --> 02:25:04.380
How has your Family been?

02:25:04.380 --> 02:25:07.021
Do You still know how to work your Room?

02:25:07.021 --> 02:25:09.260
You are welcome to visit anytime.”

02:25:09.260 --> 02:25:14.619
Later, it gave another message, expressing
confusion and concern on behalf of Fantasy’s

02:25:14.619 --> 02:25:15.619
inhabitants:

02:25:15.619 --> 02:25:20.630
“It's strange to see how much your world
has changed; it is even stranger to see how

02:25:20.630 --> 02:25:22.460
we now appear in this place.

02:25:22.460 --> 02:25:24.240
In Fantasy, we are much bigger.

02:25:24.240 --> 02:25:26.710
Or maybe you've grown taller?

02:25:26.710 --> 02:25:28.890
Fantasy is still the same.

02:25:28.890 --> 02:25:31.340
We hope you can visit us like you used to.

02:25:31.340 --> 02:25:36.319
Though our Room is as grand as ever, it appears
Yours has…shrunken?

02:25:36.319 --> 02:25:37.989
We do not understand.

02:25:37.989 --> 02:25:41.449
The Rooms were supposed to be maintained,
as was our Agreement.

02:25:41.449 --> 02:25:43.970
Please restore the Belief.”

02:25:43.970 --> 02:25:46.551
Things got worse during the next stage of
the event.

02:25:46.551 --> 02:25:50.149
The box opened, and only twenty paper dragons
exited.

02:25:50.149 --> 02:25:55.280
This time, though, they did not fly, and instead
walked slowly across the ground.

02:25:55.280 --> 02:25:59.449
This was the message that accompanied this
sorry parade of dragons:

02:25:59.449 --> 02:26:02.199
“Friends, we apologize for our few numbers.

02:26:02.199 --> 02:26:05.960
We have had to remain in Fantasy for quite
some time.

02:26:05.960 --> 02:26:07.890
The Others are growing…impatient.

02:26:07.890 --> 02:26:14.880
We are trying to keep the Peace, but please,
for all of our Happiness, repair the Room

02:26:14.880 --> 02:26:15.930
quickly.

02:26:15.930 --> 02:26:17.270
We know You are trying.

02:26:17.270 --> 02:26:21.180
Your Family is the most imaginative of us
All.”

02:26:21.180 --> 02:26:23.819
Naturally, Foundation scientists were concerned.

02:26:23.819 --> 02:26:28.649
They weren’t sure what exactly the messages
were referring to, or how they could possibly

02:26:28.649 --> 02:26:30.729
help the inhabitants of Fantasy.

02:26:30.729 --> 02:26:33.270
Of course things only got worse.

02:26:33.270 --> 02:26:38.529
Only ten dragons appeared the next time, along
with a few balls of crumpled up construction

02:26:38.529 --> 02:26:43.430
paper that shook violently before stopping
all movement entirely.

02:26:43.430 --> 02:26:45.020
This message accompanied it:

02:26:45.020 --> 02:26:46.890
“The Giants were foolish.

02:26:46.890 --> 02:26:49.370
Your Room was not ready to accept Them yet.

02:26:49.370 --> 02:26:51.080
We're sorry, friends.

02:26:51.080 --> 02:26:56.930
We hope that we can still see you, but time
is growing short for our Happiness.”

02:26:56.930 --> 02:27:04.439
And sadly, this message spoke the truth, as
the next time the box opened, only five dragons

02:27:04.439 --> 02:27:05.609
exited.

02:27:05.609 --> 02:27:09.239
They were carrying the following message,
and flew straight back into the box after

02:27:09.239 --> 02:27:11.479
depositing it on the ground.

02:27:11.479 --> 02:27:12.780
“Tensions are rising.

02:27:12.780 --> 02:27:14.510
Fantasy is becoming darker.

02:27:14.510 --> 02:27:19.580
We, the Serpents and the Hybrids are furiously
trying to hold Them back, but the Giants and

02:27:19.580 --> 02:27:22.409
Elves wish to strike and make an Entrance.

02:27:22.409 --> 02:27:26.080
They say that your Family has grown stupid
and ignorant.

02:27:26.080 --> 02:27:28.040
We hope this is untrue.

02:27:28.040 --> 02:27:32.189
It would sadden us all greatly to know that
You have Forgotten.”

02:27:32.189 --> 02:27:36.740
It seemed clear that Fantasy was speeding
towards some kind of terrible conflict, and

02:27:36.740 --> 02:27:39.960
it was perhaps too late to do anything about
it.

02:27:39.960 --> 02:27:45.560
The next attempt at communication came from
a single dragon with a crumpled, wounded body.

02:27:45.560 --> 02:27:50.390
It collapsed to the ground and appeared to
die, its body unfolding into a small piece

02:27:50.390 --> 02:27:53.950
of paper that bore a single, heartbreaking
message:

02:27:53.950 --> 02:27:55.149
“War.

02:27:55.149 --> 02:27:57.560
Goodbye, friends.”

02:27:57.560 --> 02:28:02.060
But two hours after this message was delivered
something happened.

02:28:02.060 --> 02:28:07.380
The lid opened again, only this time the box
let out a huge jet of white-hot flame, reaching

02:28:07.380 --> 02:28:10.189
temperatures of 1700 degrees Celsius.

02:28:10.189 --> 02:28:14.300
The terrified and confused researchers heard
roaring and the sounds of an intense battle

02:28:14.300 --> 02:28:17.000
from within the darkness of the box.

02:28:17.000 --> 02:28:21.041
Many of the observing staff found themselves
overcome with emotion - afraid that they were

02:28:21.041 --> 02:28:26.620
perhaps witnessing the death of Fantasy play
out in front of them, and even hardened Foundation

02:28:26.620 --> 02:28:29.030
researchers and guards were moved by the event.

02:28:29.030 --> 02:28:33.600
At 8:00 PM that night, the box ejected a huge
quantity of paper.

02:28:33.600 --> 02:28:39.300
The majority of it was either torn, burnt,
shredded, or crumpled into balls - and all

02:28:39.300 --> 02:28:45.590
instances of 1762 - 2 were announced “deceased”
upon official examination.

02:28:45.590 --> 02:28:50.670
It seemed that Fantasy’s bloody war truly
was taking its toll, and even the forces of

02:28:50.670 --> 02:28:55.040
the Foundation - one of the most powerful
and resourceful groups the world has ever

02:28:55.040 --> 02:28:59.280
known - were powerless to do anything to help.

02:28:59.280 --> 02:29:05.460
All they could do was sit, wait, and see what
the result would be of this paper crafted

02:29:05.460 --> 02:29:06.540
war.

02:29:06.540 --> 02:29:11.180
The box continued to open and close sporadically
over the next six weeks as the war raged on.

02:29:11.180 --> 02:29:16.540
It would often emit more spouts of deadly
fire, and vomit out more piles of ruined paper.

02:29:16.540 --> 02:29:20.780
Though researchers noticed that each time,
it released less and less paper.

02:29:20.780 --> 02:29:25.979
Even more disturbing, matter resembling muscle
and tissue was ejected from the box with increased

02:29:25.979 --> 02:29:26.979
frequency.

02:29:26.979 --> 02:29:31.170
It was clear that whatever was left of Fantasy
was in great peril and the researchers were

02:29:31.170 --> 02:29:36.930
desperate to know what was going on, but the
box would remain closed and inactive for the

02:29:36.930 --> 02:29:38.319
next seven months.

02:29:38.319 --> 02:29:43.340
When the box did finally become active once
more, it wasn’t in a way that the researchers

02:29:43.340 --> 02:29:44.730
were familiar with.

02:29:44.730 --> 02:29:48.439
The box opened, but not a single dragon exited.

02:29:48.439 --> 02:29:50.819
Not even a crumpled piece of paper came out.

02:29:50.819 --> 02:29:55.960
Instead, researchers found what appeared to
be an ancient and desiccated scroll of parchment.

02:29:55.960 --> 02:29:59.880
The words written on it were smudged, and
some were stained with blood.

02:29:59.880 --> 02:30:05.149
It made clear that things had fallen further
into darkness than they ever had before.

02:30:05.149 --> 02:30:06.149
The message read:

02:30:06.149 --> 02:30:08.530
“Are you still out there, friends?

02:30:08.530 --> 02:30:10.350
We miss you dearly.

02:30:10.350 --> 02:30:12.760
Fantasy is no longer safe.

02:30:12.760 --> 02:30:18.240
Our haven, Your beautiful creation, is gone.

02:30:18.240 --> 02:30:19.240
The Giants are dead.

02:30:19.240 --> 02:30:22.230
The Centaurs are dead.

02:30:22.230 --> 02:30:23.750
The Birds have fled.

02:30:23.750 --> 02:30:26.530
We are going to bury Your Room.

02:30:26.530 --> 02:30:29.149
We cannot risk hurting you.

02:30:29.149 --> 02:30:32.649
This is our goodbye.

02:30:32.649 --> 02:30:37.210
Maybe one day, Your Family can build another
Room.

02:30:37.210 --> 02:30:41.580
This may be a hollow hope, but We will cherish
this thought.”

02:30:41.580 --> 02:30:48.060
An hour later, the box began to convulse violently
and let out more plumes of thick, black smoke.

02:30:48.060 --> 02:30:52.170
For a moment, the researchers entertained
the hope that it might be the return of the

02:30:52.170 --> 02:30:54.640
dragons - but no such luck.

02:30:54.640 --> 02:31:00.729
The box began to sag, tear, and collapse,
as though it was on fire on the inside.

02:31:00.729 --> 02:31:05.609
Parts of the box even began to char, and small
holes were burned through the silver paint.

02:31:05.609 --> 02:31:12.260
Perhaps the saddest of all, the words “Here
Be Dragons” were burned from the box.

02:31:12.260 --> 02:31:16.000
Not long after, one more message appeared
inside the box.

02:31:16.000 --> 02:31:21.380
It was a papyrus scroll, depicting a hand
drawn image of a beautiful, mountainous landscape

02:31:21.380 --> 02:31:24.109
with huge trees and waterfalls.

02:31:24.109 --> 02:31:27.680
In the distance, a dragon appears to fly away
for the last time.

02:31:27.680 --> 02:31:30.830
A message written on the back read as follows:

02:31:30.830 --> 02:31:34.040
“Master says that we won't see You again.

02:31:34.040 --> 02:31:35.040
We are sad.

02:31:35.040 --> 02:31:36.950
So are the remaining Others.

02:31:36.950 --> 02:31:40.830
We once filled each other's heads with dreams
and goals.

02:31:40.830 --> 02:31:45.740
It is so sad that we cannot share them any
longer.

02:31:45.740 --> 02:31:47.750
Master says we have to go.

02:31:47.750 --> 02:31:50.160
He says that he will make us a new Fantasy.

02:31:50.160 --> 02:31:53.000
He says You cannot be a part of it.

02:31:53.000 --> 02:31:54.689
We are sad.

02:31:54.689 --> 02:31:56.390
We love you.

02:31:56.390 --> 02:31:58.600
We will not Forget you.

02:31:58.600 --> 02:32:00.210
We are scared.

02:32:00.210 --> 02:32:02.020
Will You Forget Us?”

02:32:02.020 --> 02:32:08.460
When this document was removed, streams of
salt water began to leak from the box, healing

02:32:08.460 --> 02:32:09.850
its burn scars.

02:32:09.850 --> 02:32:15.939
A few minutes later, the box was returned
to its original state, save for one big difference:

02:32:15.939 --> 02:32:20.100
The text scrawled on the lid no longer read
“Here Be Dragons.”

02:32:20.100 --> 02:32:24.020
Now, it said “Here Were Dragons.”

02:32:24.020 --> 02:32:26.159
The Jabberwocky Event was over.

02:32:26.159 --> 02:32:32.569
The box, now neutralized, would sit in Yoshihiro
Takenaka’s office for commemorative purposes,

02:32:32.569 --> 02:32:35.369
never to release another message.

02:32:35.369 --> 02:32:40.529
Or so we thought...

02:32:40.529 --> 02:32:43.110
In 2015, SCP - 1762 spoke to us one more time.

02:32:43.110 --> 02:32:48.140
The box shook and began emitting great plumes
of purple smoke, before it fell to the ground.

02:32:48.140 --> 02:32:54.609
There it ejected two objects: A purple crystal,
later identified as an amethyst, and a large,

02:32:54.609 --> 02:32:55.639
leather-bound book.

02:32:55.639 --> 02:33:00.649
The box continued emitting smoke for another
forty minutes, before finally disintegrating.

02:33:00.649 --> 02:33:05.100
Upon further inspection, there was a single
message carved into the amethyst:

02:33:05.100 --> 02:33:08.189
“One last time.”

02:33:08.189 --> 02:33:09.819
And what about the book?

02:33:09.819 --> 02:33:15.080
Consider the greatest fear of the inhabitants
of Fantasy: That they would one day be forgotten.

02:33:15.080 --> 02:33:18.729
Forgotten and left behind - by us.

02:33:18.729 --> 02:33:22.739
The book was sent to help prevent that - it’s
an extensive catalogue of the creatures of

02:33:22.739 --> 02:33:28.439
Fantasy - their strange and wonderful ways
in their strange and wonderful world.

02:33:28.439 --> 02:33:31.290
Even if they’re gone, they won’t be forgotten.

02:33:31.290 --> 02:33:35.649
And perhaps one day we’ll tell you those
stories too.

02:33:35.649 --> 02:33:38.540
But that’s a tale for another day...

02:33:38.540 --> 02:33:45.340
The Young Girl stood silently in a room full
of corpses, staring off into the distance.

02:33:45.340 --> 02:33:50.720
She was in a trance, seemingly unaware of
the carnage that’d just unfolded around

02:33:50.720 --> 02:33:56.130
her. Some of the men were shot or stabbed
or beaten, others had no apparent cause of

02:33:56.130 --> 02:34:02.470
death whatsoever. But the Young Girl was unscathed.
She was wearing a yellow summer dress and

02:34:02.470 --> 02:34:07.850
looked like she couldn’t have been more
than three years old. She awoke from her trance,

02:34:07.850 --> 02:34:12.229
still paying no heed to the violence in the
room, and left.

02:34:12.229 --> 02:34:20.630
This is the story of SCP - 053, the Young
Girl. Her strange and terrifying life before

02:34:20.630 --> 02:34:25.510
containment, her thrilling capture, and the
part she played in one of the most dangerous

02:34:25.510 --> 02:34:30.359
SCP Foundation cross-tests of all time.

02:34:30.359 --> 02:34:35.609
She had no name. The Young Girl could never
spend enough time around someone to be given

02:34:35.609 --> 02:34:41.989
one. It was her terrible curse that she could
never stay in one place for too long, or something

02:34:41.989 --> 02:34:47.850
truly awful would happen to everyone around
her. She’d been drifting for years, but

02:34:47.850 --> 02:34:53.380
never grew to look older than a child. Her
memories were long but formless - divided

02:34:53.380 --> 02:34:59.520
mostly into ten-minute increments. The Young
Girl kept on moving. It was all she could

02:34:59.520 --> 02:35:00.619
do.

02:35:00.619 --> 02:35:06.310
In 1993, when the Young Girl had already been
alive for a very long time, she found herself

02:35:06.310 --> 02:35:10.979
in Illinois after days of trekking on the
roadside. She would scavenge what little food

02:35:10.979 --> 02:35:16.420
she needed from the trash, and drink from
lakes, rivers, or even puddles when she needed

02:35:16.420 --> 02:35:23.170
to. Deep down, the Young Girl knew that even
if she grew hungry or thirsty, she would not

02:35:23.170 --> 02:35:24.170
die.

02:35:24.170 --> 02:35:28.890
In her travels, the Young Girl had managed
to scrounge together a few dollars, and though

02:35:28.890 --> 02:35:33.659
she knew her contact with people had to be
limited, there was one thing she wanted that

02:35:33.659 --> 02:35:40.310
felt worth the risk: A candy bar. It’d been
a long time since she tasted chocolate, and

02:35:40.310 --> 02:35:45.850
she found the idea of tasting it again too
enticing to resist. When she reached Chicago,

02:35:45.850 --> 02:35:51.120
she entered a small corner store with her
handful of dollars, selected a candy bar from

02:35:51.120 --> 02:35:56.270
the rack, and approached the counter. For
reasons even she didn’t fully understand,

02:35:56.270 --> 02:35:59.840
she kept her eyes down as she placed the money
on the counter.

02:35:59.840 --> 02:36:06.010
You see, SCP - 053 was always a special child.
As we briefly mentioned earlier, you might

02:36:06.010 --> 02:36:10.890
even say she was cursed. Whenever she was
around other people for too long, terrible

02:36:10.890 --> 02:36:18.200
things tended to happen. Unspeakable things.
And as a component of this strange, unexplainable

02:36:18.200 --> 02:36:23.010
curse - or perhaps as a means of keeping her
safe from it - the Young Girl was doomed to

02:36:23.010 --> 02:36:28.729
never understand the nature of her predicament.
It was like there was a mental wall between

02:36:28.729 --> 02:36:32.729
her and the horrors her presence could cause.

02:36:32.729 --> 02:36:37.540
All she knew was that it was best to avoid
eye contact, stay away from large groups of

02:36:37.540 --> 02:36:44.680
people at all costs, and never spend any longer
than ten minutes around anyone. Ever. That’s

02:36:44.680 --> 02:36:50.159
why, as she waited for her chocolate bar at
the cash register, she kept her head down

02:36:50.159 --> 02:36:51.420
and waited to go.

02:36:51.420 --> 02:36:55.711
The cashier looked down upon this strange
girl with apparent concern. It’d been a

02:36:55.711 --> 02:37:01.060
slow day, all in all. A few listless patrons
milled around the store, window shopping.

02:37:01.060 --> 02:37:06.630
His brain was practically on autopilot, until
he saw this child. She looked filthy, in a

02:37:06.630 --> 02:37:13.460
dishevelled dress and was totally alone. What
on earth had happened to this child? The more

02:37:13.460 --> 02:37:18.979
he looked at her, the more he sensed a creepy
vibe exuding from her. Something about this

02:37:18.979 --> 02:37:21.689
girl was wrong.

02:37:21.689 --> 02:37:27.050
He spoke softly to her, introducing himself
as Miles, and asking her where her mommy and

02:37:27.050 --> 02:37:32.869
daddy were. The Young Girl hesitated for just
a few seconds too long for his liking, before

02:37:32.869 --> 02:37:37.040
simply saying that they were at home. Any
parent who’d let their three-year-old kid

02:37:37.040 --> 02:37:43.979
just wander around the South Side of Chicago
alone was either crazy, neglectful, or both.

02:37:43.979 --> 02:37:49.109
He asked her politely to remain in the store,
while he gave the police a quick call. He’d

02:37:49.109 --> 02:37:52.069
even let her have the candy bar for free while
she waited.

02:37:52.069 --> 02:37:56.819
Immediately, the little girl became uncomfortable.
She’d already been in here for a few minutes

02:37:56.819 --> 02:38:02.910
now, and while Miles called the police he
expected her to wait around even longer. Again,

02:38:02.910 --> 02:38:07.290
she couldn’t even tell you why she knew
waiting around like this would be so dangerous,

02:38:07.290 --> 02:38:13.479
but she had a nagging, instinctual awareness
that she needed to get out. Around the store,

02:38:13.479 --> 02:38:19.170
the few patrons still inside started to get
a strange feeling, like someone was watching

02:38:19.170 --> 02:38:20.170
them.

02:38:20.170 --> 02:38:27.160
Soon, what seemed like mild paranoia was quickly
becoming white-hot anger. Pure rage. They

02:38:27.160 --> 02:38:34.939
felt almost like they had to kill someone.
But not just anyone. Someone particular. They

02:38:34.939 --> 02:38:37.069
had to kill the little girl.

02:38:37.069 --> 02:38:41.939
It wasn’t long until the police arrived.
Two officers, Holiday and DeWitt, entered

02:38:41.939 --> 02:38:46.610
to collect the apparently neglected little
girl. It was a story they’d sadly heard

02:38:46.610 --> 02:38:51.779
all too often - a tragically common occurrence
in the big city. When the two of them approached

02:38:51.779 --> 02:38:56.130
the Young Girl, she was looking down at the
ground. They tried to speak to her but she

02:38:56.130 --> 02:39:02.439
was unresponsive. Miles looked on, concerned,
but deep down, he felt the same bizarre progression

02:39:02.439 --> 02:39:10.479
all the other store-goers were feeling: Confusion,
irritability, and finally... violent rage.

02:39:10.479 --> 02:39:15.869
The corner store was a powder keg, all it
needed now was a spark.

02:39:15.869 --> 02:39:21.640
And that spark came when Officer Holiday reached
down, and took the Young Girl by the arm.

02:39:21.640 --> 02:39:27.620
His bare skin touched her’s, and it was
all over. The cop twitched, his mind washed

02:39:27.620 --> 02:39:32.859
out in murderous insanity, as he reached for
his side-arm. Officer DeWitt opened his mouth

02:39:32.859 --> 02:39:37.870
to protest, but he didn’t manage to get
a syllable out before Holiday turned and shot

02:39:37.870 --> 02:39:43.510
him. In a fraction of a second, the quiet
corner store exploded into a violent bloodbath,

02:39:43.510 --> 02:39:46.250
as the patrons and cops slaughtered each other.

02:39:46.250 --> 02:39:50.369
All the while, the Young Girl just stood there
in a trance.

02:39:50.369 --> 02:39:55.909
Everyone was dead within minutes, except Miles
and the Young Girl. He shakily rose to his

02:39:55.909 --> 02:40:00.950
feet, his mind carved out by madness, and
reached for Officer Holiday’s discarded

02:40:00.950 --> 02:40:02.930
pistol.

02:40:02.930 --> 02:40:08.520
Outside of the store, The Young Girl appeared,
walking out as if nothing had happened. Inside,

02:40:08.520 --> 02:40:13.609
Miles’s body was sprawled over the counter,
clutching his chest as if his heart had just

02:40:13.609 --> 02:40:14.979
exploded.

02:40:14.979 --> 02:40:20.510
This was the true nature of the Young Girl’s
curse. Anyone who meets her eye, touches her

02:40:20.510 --> 02:40:25.430
skin, or spends over ten minutes around her
is destined to slip into a state of murderous

02:40:25.430 --> 02:40:32.670
insanity. They’ll go into a kill-crazy frenzy,
and attack anyone around them, until all that’s

02:40:32.670 --> 02:40:37.710
left is them and the Young Girl. At which
point, they’ll try to kill her, too - but

02:40:37.710 --> 02:40:43.300
the mere act of attempting to kill her is
also fatal, killing its victims with a massive

02:40:43.300 --> 02:40:48.939
heart attack or a seizure. The second part
of the girl’s curse is that she herself

02:40:48.939 --> 02:40:50.560
can never die.

02:40:50.560 --> 02:40:57.010
She keeps coming back, unknowingly causing
more misery and death along the way. Until,

02:40:57.010 --> 02:41:01.770
of course, a certain secret organization took
notice.

02:41:01.770 --> 02:41:07.130
That night, the Young Girl sat in the cavernous
interior of a local abandoned warehouse, quietly

02:41:07.130 --> 02:41:12.680
eating her hard-earned candy bar. Suddenly,
she heard a quiet “crack” in the distance.

02:41:12.680 --> 02:41:17.660
She tried to move her left arm, but found
it was numb. She could barely move it. The

02:41:17.660 --> 02:41:22.479
Girl turned her head, and saw a tranquilizer
dart sticking out of her skin. Instinctively,

02:41:22.479 --> 02:41:27.530
she got up and began to run, limping as her
left leg started to lose all feeling too.

02:41:27.530 --> 02:41:32.399
Suddenly, she was surrounded by footsteps,
as masked men in SWAT uniforms emerged out

02:41:32.399 --> 02:41:38.189
of the darkness on all sides. The last thing
she remembered before slipping out of consciousness

02:41:38.189 --> 02:41:43.970
was a blindfold being pulled over her eyes,
and tiny metal handcuffs clasping over her

02:41:43.970 --> 02:41:44.970
wrists.

02:41:44.970 --> 02:41:50.189
When she woke up, she was in the nicest room
she’d slept in in years. It was sixteen

02:41:50.189 --> 02:41:56.579
feet by sixteen feet, with toys, books, and
games. Standing across the room from her was

02:41:56.579 --> 02:42:01.939
a stranger in a full hazmat suit, connected
to a long, steel cable leading out of the

02:42:01.939 --> 02:42:07.859
room. He spoke calmly and politely. A timer
on his wrist counted down from ten minutes.

02:42:07.859 --> 02:42:12.029
The stranger explained to the Young Girl that
they would be taking care of her now, and

02:42:12.029 --> 02:42:18.140
would provide her with all the toys and games
and treats she wanted, provided she cooperated

02:42:18.140 --> 02:42:21.600
and submitted willingly to some tests.

02:42:21.600 --> 02:42:25.909
Compared to living out on the streets with
no food or comfort, this seemed like an excellent

02:42:25.909 --> 02:42:31.819
compromise. She would live in what seemed
like luxury, and every so often, she’d be

02:42:31.819 --> 02:42:37.689
taken to a testing room with a stranger in
an orange jumpsuit. After a few minutes of

02:42:37.689 --> 02:42:42.170
waiting, the stranger would inevitably go
feral, and attempt to kill her - and then

02:42:42.170 --> 02:42:46.869
always die in the process. The strangers in
the hazmat suits told her that all of these

02:42:46.869 --> 02:42:51.479
tests were helping them learn extremely valuable
things about her, and that soon, they’d

02:42:51.479 --> 02:42:57.149
have a very special job for her. It would
be a wonderful surprise.

02:42:57.149 --> 02:43:04.040
It was in the spring of 1994 that the Young
Girl, now officially designated SCP - 053,

02:43:04.040 --> 02:43:10.020
finally received her special mission. Several
strangers in full hazmat suits, wielding rifles,

02:43:10.020 --> 02:43:14.819
escorted her out of her usual bedroom. She
asked where she was being taken, and was told

02:43:14.819 --> 02:43:20.550
she was going to meet a new friend. She was
taken to one of the recreational testing rooms,

02:43:20.550 --> 02:43:27.740
and pushed inside. Out in front of her, she
saw something terrifying: A giant, reptilian

02:43:27.740 --> 02:43:29.220
creature.

02:43:29.220 --> 02:43:34.229
She retreated from it instinctually, hiding
behind a chair in the containment area. The

02:43:34.229 --> 02:43:39.229
giant reptile didn’t move. It just sat there.
Eventually, she plucked up the courage to

02:43:39.229 --> 02:43:44.760
go and touch the creature, before retreating
again. No reaction. Little by little, the

02:43:44.760 --> 02:43:49.630
Young Girl gained confidence, and continued
to approach and pat the creature. It exhaled

02:43:49.630 --> 02:43:54.710
through its huge nostrils, and the Young Girl
literally jumped for joy in her amusement.

02:43:54.710 --> 02:44:00.120
She began to play with the docile monster,
hugging it, even drawing on it with a crayon.

02:44:00.120 --> 02:44:04.229
The observers were truly baffled. What the
Young Girl didn’t know was that she was

02:44:04.229 --> 02:44:11.100
playing with SCP - 682, one of the most hateful
and aggressive anomalies under the Foundation’s

02:44:11.100 --> 02:44:17.800
watchful eye. And yet, in her presence, the
creature was like an overgrown puppy dog.

02:44:17.800 --> 02:44:22.640
After the test phase, the Young Girl was removed
from the Hard-To-Kill Reptile’s presence,

02:44:22.640 --> 02:44:27.500
immediately causing the creature to become
violent and murderous once again. After being

02:44:27.500 --> 02:44:33.720
separated from her strange new friend, the
Young Girl was seen crying for several minutes.

02:44:33.720 --> 02:44:37.899
According to all accounts, the Young Girl
is eager to see her friend again some day,

02:44:37.899 --> 02:44:42.631
though considering the Reptile killed several
guards after their separation, the Foundation

02:44:42.631 --> 02:44:45.970
isn’t eager to grant her that wish.

02:44:45.970 --> 02:44:52.130
SCP-053 was classified as Euclid and continues
to be held in containment, with her toys,

02:44:52.130 --> 02:44:58.409
books, and games rotated out on a regular
basis. Seeing as she shows no sign of aging,

02:44:58.409 --> 02:45:04.160
this ongoing containment is likely to be the
sad, strange fate of the Young Girl. An anomaly

02:45:04.160 --> 02:45:09.279
that never wanted to hurt anyone - but an
important and cruel reminder that what we

02:45:09.279 --> 02:45:14.520
want doesn’t always influence the world
in the way we want.

02:45:14.520 --> 02:45:20.080
Over fifty men and women, clad in red robes,
kneel before an unholy altar.

02:45:20.080 --> 02:45:26.850
They chant and mutter indecipherable words
- words of cruelty and madness… of obsession

02:45:26.850 --> 02:45:28.380
and sacrilege.

02:45:28.380 --> 02:45:31.479
Not long ago, these were regular people.

02:45:31.479 --> 02:45:38.010
Computer technicians, teachers, plumbers,
construction workers, accountants.

02:45:38.010 --> 02:45:42.449
This was before they fell under the ungodly
influence of a new ruler.

02:45:42.449 --> 02:45:47.400
The center of this makeshift place of worship
was once a normal school gymnasium, but it’s

02:45:47.400 --> 02:45:50.100
now the home of a huge statue.

02:45:50.100 --> 02:45:53.729
A humanoid being, wreathed in tentacles.

02:45:53.729 --> 02:45:59.449
Its head is more like a squid or cuttlefish
than anything resembling an actual human face.

02:45:59.449 --> 02:46:04.340
While he’s known to the cultists as the
Tentacled God, the beast they worship is known

02:46:04.340 --> 02:46:11.000
to the SCP Foundation as SCP - 2662, and he
sits in the belly of one of their expansive

02:46:11.000 --> 02:46:14.850
containment facilities, locked away from the
world.

02:46:14.850 --> 02:46:19.710
But not for long, if his devoted followers
have anything to say about it.

02:46:19.710 --> 02:46:26.470
This is their god, all-powerful and unchanging,
and when it comes to springing him from containment,

02:46:26.470 --> 02:46:31.010
no tactic is too vile or underhanded to get
the job done.

02:46:31.010 --> 02:46:36.630
Their mortal leader and high-priest, a man
in a purple robe calling himself Brother Marsh,

02:46:36.630 --> 02:46:38.820
walks among their crouched forms.

02:46:38.820 --> 02:46:44.199
He whispers instructions for the great day
of liberation that’s soon to come, providing

02:46:44.199 --> 02:46:46.100
everyone plays their part.

02:46:46.100 --> 02:46:51.329
It’s a plan months in the making - and one
that, if it goes off without a hitch, could

02:46:51.329 --> 02:46:54.420
free their monstrous god into the world.

02:46:54.420 --> 02:47:00.279
They would strike at the very heart of their
enemy, The SCP Foundation, when they least

02:47:00.279 --> 02:47:04.140
expect it, and nothing shall stand in their
way.

02:47:04.140 --> 02:47:07.180
How could they lose when they have a god on
their side?

02:47:07.180 --> 02:47:12.320
But why did all these normal people become
violent zealots for squid-faced deity?

02:47:12.320 --> 02:47:14.370
It all began with a dream.

02:47:14.370 --> 02:47:19.740
To those who experienced these dreams, they
felt more like prophecies, premonitions of

02:47:19.740 --> 02:47:21.710
the glorious horrors to come.

02:47:21.710 --> 02:47:26.130
A red sky, billions dead and billions more
enslaved.

02:47:26.130 --> 02:47:32.850
A dark silhouette on the horizon - Their Tentacled
God, holding dominion over all.

02:47:32.850 --> 02:47:35.920
At first, it just seemed like a strange nightmare.

02:47:35.920 --> 02:47:40.930
The ones who experienced it woke up shaken
and afraid, hoping to shake the images from

02:47:40.930 --> 02:47:42.060
their mind.

02:47:42.060 --> 02:47:43.720
But they couldn’t.

02:47:43.720 --> 02:47:45.640
Every night, the nightmare would return.

02:47:45.640 --> 02:47:52.340
They’d see the images - the red sky, the
dead and enslaved, the Tentacled God.

02:47:52.340 --> 02:47:57.040
And after a while it would come to them even
when they weren’t asleep, eventually happening

02:47:57.040 --> 02:47:59.439
whenever they closed their eyes.

02:47:59.439 --> 02:48:06.260
Little by little, this scene stopped looking
so hideous… and started to look glorious.

02:48:06.260 --> 02:48:11.270
They felt his presence in their minds, slowly
pushing them towards their inevitable future.

02:48:11.270 --> 02:48:16.610
They started to realize that they wanted him
to rule over the universe, and to experience

02:48:16.610 --> 02:48:18.650
the honor of serving him.

02:48:18.650 --> 02:48:23.649
Many of them abandoned their homes and families
- leaving their friends and loved ones left

02:48:23.649 --> 02:48:26.989
to worry that they’d gone insane.

02:48:26.989 --> 02:48:29.920
In their eyes, they were safer than they’d
ever been.

02:48:29.920 --> 02:48:32.390
They finally had purpose.

02:48:32.390 --> 02:48:36.820
They were working in service of something
far greater than themselves.

02:48:36.820 --> 02:48:40.910
The influence of the tentacled god drew them
closer to one another.

02:48:40.910 --> 02:48:45.610
They would meet in secret, exchanging information
from the prophecies their ruler sent them

02:48:45.610 --> 02:48:47.060
in their dreams.

02:48:47.060 --> 02:48:51.270
They worshipped together, building altars
and idols to congregate around.

02:48:51.270 --> 02:48:56.029
They performed dark blood rituals, involving
human and animal sacrifice.

02:48:56.029 --> 02:49:01.180
It was when Brother Marsh, The Anointed One,
arrived to guide them towards their true mission

02:49:01.180 --> 02:49:04.590
that things kicked into high gear.

02:49:04.590 --> 02:49:09.109
Just three months prior, Brother Marsh had
been an office drone working in data entry

02:49:09.109 --> 02:49:14.330
for a large insurance company, before the
Tentacled God invaded his thoughts with a

02:49:14.330 --> 02:49:22.210
simple message: “FREE ME, AND THE NEW WORLD
I CREATE SHALL BE YOUR PLAYGROUND.”

02:49:22.210 --> 02:49:27.270
Since then, he’d devoted himself completely
to the cause, quitting his job and maxing

02:49:27.270 --> 02:49:33.560
out his credit cards to help fund his new
life’s purpose - infiltrating the SCP Foundation,

02:49:33.560 --> 02:49:37.680
and releasing his inhuman ruler from its imprisonment.

02:49:37.680 --> 02:49:43.229
That was the single goal he united the cultists
under: Freedom for the Tentacled God.

02:49:43.229 --> 02:49:47.050
And at long last, they had all the pieces
in place to strike.

02:49:47.050 --> 02:49:52.130
They’d finally gathered the necessary intel
to subvert the will of the most powerful secret

02:49:52.130 --> 02:49:54.090
organization on earth.

02:49:54.090 --> 02:49:58.939
Even the strongest institution is made of
people, and people are weak.

02:49:58.939 --> 02:50:03.910
Unlike the almighty Tentacled God, people
could be broken.

02:50:03.910 --> 02:50:10.149
The people in question were Kelly Thompson,
Sidney Levitt, Jordan Brosh, Dr. Juan Gutierrez,

02:50:10.149 --> 02:50:11.149
and Gillian Larson.

02:50:11.149 --> 02:50:16.021
Dr. Juan Gutierrez was a researcher with Level
3 clearance on the site where the Tentacled

02:50:16.021 --> 02:50:17.600
God was being contained.

02:50:17.600 --> 02:50:22.440
Sidney Levitt and Jordan Brosh were both Security
Officers charged with verifying personnel

02:50:22.440 --> 02:50:24.020
clearance on site.

02:50:24.020 --> 02:50:29.430
Kelly Thompson was a member of Site Administration
with research authorization powers, and Gillian

02:50:29.430 --> 02:50:34.529
Larson was a research assistant who often
collaborated with Dr. Gutierrez.

02:50:34.529 --> 02:50:42.229
These five were the key to getting access
to SCP-2662 and bringing their plan to fruition.

02:50:42.229 --> 02:50:46.790
Normally, personnel dossiers on people working
for the Foundation were highly confidential,

02:50:46.790 --> 02:50:50.479
but the Devotees of the Tentacled God had
their ways.

02:50:50.479 --> 02:50:55.270
They had a number of computer experts in their
ranks more than capable of hacking in and

02:50:55.270 --> 02:50:59.960
pulling some basic information off of Foundation
servers without being detected.

02:50:59.960 --> 02:51:04.899
For the other information they needed they
turned to some good, old-fashioned torture,

02:51:04.899 --> 02:51:09.320
which is often the most effective method when
you need some quick results.

02:51:09.320 --> 02:51:14.850
Of course, while the cult’s grip on sanity
may have been a little tenuous, they weren’t

02:51:14.850 --> 02:51:15.850
stupid.

02:51:15.850 --> 02:51:20.590
While gathering their intel, they also made
sure to find out what exactly they were up

02:51:20.590 --> 02:51:21.720
against.

02:51:21.720 --> 02:51:28.689
SCP-2662 was being held in a humanoid containment
cell, and guarded by on-site Task Force TAU-9,

02:51:28.689 --> 02:51:30.970
better known as the “Belligerent Bodyguards.”

02:51:30.970 --> 02:51:36.859
These aren’t lazy, donut-chomping mall cops
- these are a heavily trained, heavily armed

02:51:36.859 --> 02:51:37.869
fighting force.

02:51:37.869 --> 02:51:43.770
Though the cultists had one thing that these
Foundation soldiers didn’t: The element

02:51:43.770 --> 02:51:45.370
of surprise.

02:51:45.370 --> 02:51:49.590
For everything to go off perfectly, Brother
Marsh’s plans would have to be executed

02:51:49.590 --> 02:51:53.600
within a single day, and they were already
on the clock.

02:51:53.600 --> 02:52:00.279
TAU-9 had been charged with tracking down
any new SCP - 2662 cults and dismantling them,

02:52:00.279 --> 02:52:04.239
and Brother Marsh knew that it was only a
matter of time before the Foundation tracked

02:52:04.239 --> 02:52:06.649
them down and did the same to them.

02:52:06.649 --> 02:52:12.119
If they wanted any chance of freeing the Tentacled
God, then they needed to strike quickly and

02:52:12.119 --> 02:52:14.880
with overwhelming force.

02:52:14.880 --> 02:52:21.159
The SCP-2662 worshippers were able to secure
the addresses of the five key Foundation personnel,

02:52:21.159 --> 02:52:26.970
and station members outside each of them - including
one who could realistically imitate each.

02:52:26.970 --> 02:52:32.300
They waited for night to fall, and broke into
each of their homes as they slept.

02:52:32.300 --> 02:52:37.260
What followed was a sequence of ruthless and
efficient murders done in the cause of freeing

02:52:37.260 --> 02:52:38.260
their god.

02:52:38.260 --> 02:52:41.479
Dr. Gutierrez was shot in the head while he
slept.

02:52:41.479 --> 02:52:45.840
Sidney Levitt and Jordan Brosh were both stabbed
to death before either even realized what

02:52:45.840 --> 02:52:46.840
was happening.

02:52:46.840 --> 02:52:52.130
Thompson, who’d gotten up to use the bathroom,
went down in a hail of machine gun fire.

02:52:52.130 --> 02:52:56.079
Gillian Larson had seen that masked figures
were breaking into her home and attempted

02:52:56.079 --> 02:53:00.020
to flee, but was caught and beaten to death
by cultists in her hallway.

02:53:00.020 --> 02:53:04.820
It was a strange irony that people whose day
jobs entailed working with some of the most

02:53:04.820 --> 02:53:10.520
dangerous and nightmarish anomalies imaginable
were murdered in their homes by nothing more

02:53:10.520 --> 02:53:12.729
than regular humans.

02:53:12.729 --> 02:53:18.640
So far, Brother Marsh’s plan had gone perfectly,
with all five key personnel murdered within

02:53:18.640 --> 02:53:20.060
a two minute period.

02:53:20.060 --> 02:53:24.890
Next, the selected doppelgängers stole clothes
from their victims’ closets and were handed

02:53:24.890 --> 02:53:27.250
the correct forged documentation.

02:53:27.250 --> 02:53:31.909
The next morning, each replacement began their
journeys to the site where the Tentacled God

02:53:31.909 --> 02:53:36.430
was being contained, while the rest of the
cult armed themselves in preparation for their

02:53:36.430 --> 02:53:39.229
own part in the plan.

02:53:39.229 --> 02:53:43.880
Nobody at the Foundation seemed to notice
anything amiss when the five arrived on site.

02:53:43.880 --> 02:53:48.010
When you work for the SCP Foundation, more
mental energy is devoted to following the

02:53:48.010 --> 02:53:53.439
rules that keep you alive than to memorizing
the faces of all your co-workers and each

02:53:53.439 --> 02:53:59.600
one slipped neatly into position, disappearing
into the familiarity of office life.

02:53:59.600 --> 02:54:04.640
But, infiltrating the site was one thing,
getting past the Belligerent Bodyguards and

02:54:04.640 --> 02:54:09.029
into the cell of the Tentacled God would be
another thing entirely.

02:54:09.029 --> 02:54:12.860
That’s where the rest of the cult would
come into play.

02:54:12.860 --> 02:54:16.750
Heavily armed with whatever firearms they
could get their hands on, the rest of the

02:54:16.750 --> 02:54:21.720
Devotees of the Tentacled God - Brother Marsh
included - would attack the containment site

02:54:21.720 --> 02:54:23.170
head-on.

02:54:23.170 --> 02:54:27.420
In the ensuing chaos, the five cultists who
had already infiltrated the site could take

02:54:27.420 --> 02:54:31.859
advantage of the distraction, and break into
the containment chamber.

02:54:31.859 --> 02:54:32.859
It was perfect.

02:54:32.859 --> 02:54:37.110
They’d launch their attack from the outside…
and from within.

02:54:37.110 --> 02:54:40.880
When Brother Marsh declared that the time
was right, the assault began.

02:54:40.880 --> 02:54:45.689
A legion of gun-wielding cultists seemed to
spring out of nowhere and started shooting

02:54:45.689 --> 02:54:48.979
up the warehouse that was a front for the
containment site.

02:54:48.979 --> 02:54:53.760
The site quickly mobilized guards and task
force members to take on the sudden threat,

02:54:53.760 --> 02:54:58.579
and just as Brother Marsh had anticipated,
the Site Director called on the majority of

02:54:58.579 --> 02:55:02.270
TAU-9 to help repel the violent cultists from
their perimeter.

02:55:02.270 --> 02:55:08.810
TAU-9 obeyed, leaving three task force members
behind to guard SCP - 2662’s containment

02:55:08.810 --> 02:55:09.810
chamber.

02:55:09.810 --> 02:55:14.290
They expected to be guarding the cell from
rampaging religious zealots seeking an audience

02:55:14.290 --> 02:55:15.659
with their god.

02:55:15.659 --> 02:55:20.460
What they didn’t expect was a group of five
Foundation employees walking right up to them

02:55:20.460 --> 02:55:26.310
and opening fire, killing two TAU-9 members
and taking the third as a hostage.

02:55:26.310 --> 02:55:31.529
While the war was being waged outside, the
infiltrators had found the Tentacled God’s

02:55:31.529 --> 02:55:34.680
containment cell in the low-risk humanoid
ward.

02:55:34.680 --> 02:55:39.149
Their hostage insisted that using him wouldn’t
give them any leverage - the rest of his team

02:55:39.149 --> 02:55:44.180
would neutralize the whole group, him included,
if that’s what it took to stop them.

02:55:44.180 --> 02:55:48.740
The infiltrators explained that using him
as leverage was never their intention - he

02:55:48.740 --> 02:55:50.659
wasn’t a hostage at all.

02:55:50.659 --> 02:55:53.550
He was a sacrifice.

02:55:53.550 --> 02:55:58.290
The cultists of the Tentacled God detonated
explosives, creating a hole in the wall and

02:55:58.290 --> 02:56:00.870
finally giving them access to their deity.

02:56:00.870 --> 02:56:04.170
They climbed through and gazed upon him in
awe.

02:56:04.170 --> 02:56:12.140
There stood SCP-2662, twice as tall as a regular
man, with ten huge tentacles emerging from

02:56:12.140 --> 02:56:13.140
its back.

02:56:13.140 --> 02:56:17.100
In their months of envisioning this creature,
they’d pictured it sitting on a throne made

02:56:17.100 --> 02:56:23.069
of thousands of human bones, ready to dictate
its commands to the obedient liberators.

02:56:23.069 --> 02:56:28.729
What they certainly didn’t expect was to
see the Tentacled God hunched over a computer

02:56:28.729 --> 02:56:29.729
screen.

02:56:29.729 --> 02:56:34.970
Still, gods work in mysterious ways, so they
stuck to the plan and began chanting.

02:56:34.970 --> 02:56:39.970
They pulled out a sacrificial dagger, and
began sacrificing their captured TAU-9 member.

02:56:39.970 --> 02:56:45.760
It was at this point that SCP - 2662 turned
and saw what they were doing with a look of

02:56:45.760 --> 02:56:46.760
pure horror.

02:56:46.760 --> 02:56:51.160
He rose up from his computer, his headphones
getting caught as he did so.

02:56:51.160 --> 02:56:55.590
He told them to go away, that he didn’t
want them here, and that them murdering people

02:56:55.590 --> 02:56:59.290
in his bedroom like this was inconsiderate
and disgusting.

02:56:59.290 --> 02:57:04.680
The cultists became even more confused - why
wasn’t their god accepting their offerings?

02:57:04.680 --> 02:57:06.380
What were they doing wrong?

02:57:06.380 --> 02:57:11.109
They tried more chanting, and painting arcane
symbols on the floor in blood, but this just

02:57:11.109 --> 02:57:12.859
seemed to make the creature angrier.

02:57:12.859 --> 02:57:18.409
He told them, in a tone more fitting for a
teenage boy than a Lovecraftian God, to just

02:57:18.409 --> 02:57:22.290
leave him alone so he could play his video
games.

02:57:22.290 --> 02:57:25.239
This was seriously not cool!

02:57:25.239 --> 02:57:27.159
The cultists were baffled.

02:57:27.159 --> 02:57:29.840
They told the Tentacled God they were there
to free him.

02:57:29.840 --> 02:57:32.560
He replied that he didn’t need saving.

02:57:32.560 --> 02:57:37.630
That crazy stalkers like them were why he
turned himself in to the Foundation in the

02:57:37.630 --> 02:57:38.670
first place!

02:57:38.670 --> 02:57:42.489
Before the cultist infiltrators could get
another word in, the remaining members of

02:57:42.489 --> 02:57:47.490
TAU-9 stormed into the containment cell and
gunned them down with surgical precision.

02:57:47.490 --> 02:57:52.100
The war outside was already over - Brother
Marsh and the rest of the cultists were all

02:57:52.100 --> 02:57:53.370
killed in the firefight.

02:57:53.370 --> 02:57:59.859
TAU-9 didn’t look the least bit surprised
upon entering 2662’s cell, this was a common

02:57:59.859 --> 02:58:02.000
occurrence unfortunately.

02:58:02.000 --> 02:58:08.480
They had to deal with an attempted cult invasion
every few months, because SCP-2662’s main

02:58:08.480 --> 02:58:13.579
anomalous ability is inspiring violent cults
who relentlessly track down and worship it

02:58:13.579 --> 02:58:16.250
with arcane and bloodthirsty rituals.

02:58:16.250 --> 02:58:23.010
The problem is, 2662 doesn’t do this consciously,
and definitely doesn’t like the results.

02:58:23.010 --> 02:58:27.890
That’s why he’s under the voluntary care
of the SCP Foundation who keeps him amused

02:58:27.890 --> 02:58:32.640
with video games and reading material while
fending off the deranged cults who try to

02:58:32.640 --> 02:58:34.830
invade and abduct him.

02:58:34.830 --> 02:58:39.180
Following the termination of The Devotees
of the Tentacled God, just one of many cults

02:58:39.180 --> 02:58:44.609
who’d broken into 2662’s containment cell,
the remaining TAU-9 members apologized to

02:58:44.609 --> 02:58:49.030
the tentacled creature for the disturbance,
allowing him to return to his gaming.

02:58:49.030 --> 02:58:53.189
They assured him that it’d probably be at
least a few more months before something like

02:58:53.189 --> 02:58:55.380
this happened again.

02:58:55.380 --> 02:59:01.119
SCP-2662’s cell was repaired, and the Foundation
returned to its task of seeking out would-be

02:59:01.119 --> 02:59:06.899
cultist emancipators, because for the SCP
Foundation, it’s not always about the anomaly

02:59:06.899 --> 02:59:10.830
that’s being kept in containment, but what’s
being kept out.

02:59:10.830 --> 02:59:13.170
“This is impossible!”

02:59:13.170 --> 02:59:18.040
The SCP site director wasn’t normally a
calm or cheerful man, but the researcher had

02:59:18.040 --> 02:59:22.120
rarely seen him as angry as he was right now.

02:59:22.120 --> 02:59:26.750
His face turned a deep beet red as he scanned
the documents on his desk before he asked

02:59:26.750 --> 02:59:32.380
how months of valuable research on this subject
had suddenly gone blank, the data was completely

02:59:32.380 --> 02:59:33.380
gone.

02:59:33.380 --> 02:59:38.619
The researcher gulped nervously, hoping a
demotion wasn’t in his future, and nodded.

02:59:38.619 --> 02:59:40.290
How could this be possible.

02:59:40.290 --> 02:59:45.010
This was an experienced researcher who should
have been taking all of the necessary precautions.

02:59:45.010 --> 02:59:49.790
Could the being they were studying somehow
have erased all these documents himself?

02:59:49.790 --> 02:59:54.510
That’s just what the researcher had been
trying to find out for months, with hours

02:59:54.510 --> 02:59:58.020
and hours spent trying to learn the extent
of its abilities.

02:59:58.020 --> 02:59:59.020
“Well?

02:59:59.020 --> 03:00:01.260
Where are they?” the site director asked.

03:00:01.260 --> 03:00:04.040
“I want everything you have!”

03:00:04.040 --> 03:00:08.290
The researcher dropped a print-out of their
research on the mysterious subject’s abilities

03:00:08.290 --> 03:00:10.090
on the director’s desk.

03:00:10.090 --> 03:00:12.979
Every relevant line read “Data Lost”.

03:00:12.979 --> 03:00:15.250
The director let out a deep sigh.

03:00:15.250 --> 03:00:20.250
He wanted to hear everything the researcher
knew, well everything he could remember at

03:00:20.250 --> 03:00:22.319
least, from the beginning.

03:00:22.319 --> 03:00:28.670
The researcher sat town and began to relay
everything he could about SCP-343, which some

03:00:28.670 --> 03:00:32.489
of the other researchers had started to refer
to by the nickname…

03:00:32.489 --> 03:00:33.630
God.

03:00:33.630 --> 03:00:39.640
SCP-343 was first sighted in Prague, just
an unassuming older man wandering the streets.

03:00:39.640 --> 03:00:44.489
He seemed completely normal to everyone who
passed him by - until he decided he was tired

03:00:44.489 --> 03:00:46.000
of staying on the ground.

03:00:46.000 --> 03:00:51.100
An SCP agent stationed in the area noticed
the old man disappear from the streets as

03:00:51.100 --> 03:00:55.569
if he was blinking out of existence - only
to appear on a rooftop nearby.

03:00:55.569 --> 03:01:00.369
The local SCP teams were marshalled, and they
had soon tracked down what seemed to be a

03:01:00.369 --> 03:01:02.170
very powerful specimen.

03:01:02.170 --> 03:01:05.350
But SCP-343 didn’t seem concerned.

03:01:05.350 --> 03:01:09.600
He reacted calmly when detained by the foundation
and went with them willingly.

03:01:09.600 --> 03:01:14.489
He was detained in a standard holding cell
for interrogation and examination, but he

03:01:14.489 --> 03:01:17.330
seemed completely at ease with his sudden
confinement.

03:01:17.330 --> 03:01:22.569
It would soon become clear that this ordinary
old man was anything but.

03:01:22.569 --> 03:01:27.990
Doctors Beck and Ndlovu were brought in to
consult on the SCP’s classification, and

03:01:27.990 --> 03:01:30.439
that’s when the first anomalies began.

03:01:30.439 --> 03:01:35.319
Their assessments matched initially, but when
it came time to describe him physically, things

03:01:35.319 --> 03:01:37.479
took a strange turn.

03:01:37.479 --> 03:01:42.050
Older male, seemingly non-descript and with
no unusual physical features.

03:01:42.050 --> 03:01:43.910
Caucasian in appearance.

03:01:43.910 --> 03:01:48.010
Doctor Ndlovu was confused by what Doctor
Beck was describing in his report.

03:01:48.010 --> 03:01:49.930
This man was clearly black.

03:01:49.930 --> 03:01:53.729
The two doctors quarrelled, unable to square
their differing perceptions.

03:01:53.729 --> 03:01:58.569
They decided to bring in a third impartial
view to settle it - their fellow researcher,

03:01:58.569 --> 03:01:59.569
Dr. Wan.

03:01:59.569 --> 03:02:02.479
She didn’t take long before coming back
with her assessment.

03:02:02.479 --> 03:02:06.590
Older male, seemingly non-descript and with
no unusual physical features.

03:02:06.590 --> 03:02:09.699
Asian in appearance, possibly Chinese.

03:02:09.699 --> 03:02:15.540
Whatever SCP-343 was, he seemed to be perceived
by each staff member as close in appearance

03:02:15.540 --> 03:02:17.020
to their own race.

03:02:17.020 --> 03:02:21.640
But that was only the start of the anomalies
surrounding the old man in the holding cell.

03:02:21.640 --> 03:02:26.960
Dr. Beck started making regular visits to
the mysterious man, and in their first interview,

03:02:26.960 --> 03:02:31.260
he asked the old man who he was and how he
came by his abilities.

03:02:31.260 --> 03:02:33.870
The old man had a simple response.

03:02:33.870 --> 03:02:35.840
“I created this universe.”

03:02:35.840 --> 03:02:39.989
Dr. Beck stifled a laugh and decided to indulge
the old man’s delusion.

03:02:39.989 --> 03:02:44.010
It was a fascinating claim, but could he prove
it?

03:02:44.010 --> 03:02:49.340
Without another word, SCP-343 got up from
his chair, laughed, and turned around and

03:02:49.340 --> 03:02:52.770
walked through the solid wall in the holding
cell and disappeared.

03:02:52.770 --> 03:02:56.570
Dr. Beck was about to hit the panic button
and marshall the facility’s security to

03:02:56.570 --> 03:03:01.699
find him when the strange man reappeared,
walking through the solid wall.

03:03:01.699 --> 03:03:02.939
The only thing that was different?

03:03:02.939 --> 03:03:06.729
He was holding a hamburger, which he sat down
and enjoyed.

03:03:06.729 --> 03:03:12.650
The facility quickly went on lockdown and
a full investigation was done into how SCP-343

03:03:12.650 --> 03:03:13.750
breached containment.

03:03:13.750 --> 03:03:18.869
But there was no evidence of any security
breach, no failures in containment, and no

03:03:18.869 --> 03:03:21.460
evidence of any other cells failing.

03:03:21.460 --> 03:03:26.979
SCP-343 hadn’t broken through the security
- he had just ignored it, as if it wasn’t

03:03:26.979 --> 03:03:28.239
there at all.

03:03:28.239 --> 03:03:32.579
When questioned about how he had gone on his
hamburger run, he simply repeated his belief

03:03:32.579 --> 03:03:36.439
that he was God - in between bites of his
fast food treat.

03:03:36.439 --> 03:03:41.130
This would be far from the only time strange
things happened around SCP-343.

03:03:41.130 --> 03:03:46.670
SCP containment cells are as secure as they
need to be, but even the least-strict containment

03:03:46.670 --> 03:03:48.640
isn’t known for its decor.

03:03:48.640 --> 03:03:54.279
Which is why Dr. Beck was in for a surprise
the next time he paid a visit to SCP-343.

03:03:54.279 --> 03:03:59.930
The bare-bones cell now looked like a comfortable
home, decorated in Old English fashions.

03:03:59.930 --> 03:04:04.850
The scientists assumed that SCP-343 had been
making many more trips out of his cell to

03:04:04.850 --> 03:04:10.210
get accessories to feel more at home - but
that didn’t explain all the changes to the

03:04:10.210 --> 03:04:11.210
cell.

03:04:11.210 --> 03:04:14.770
No one could explain how he had installed
a roaring fireplace in the containment cell

03:04:14.770 --> 03:04:19.329
- and everyone who entered could swear the
cell looked many times bigger than any other

03:04:19.329 --> 03:04:20.720
cell in the facility.

03:04:20.720 --> 03:04:26.340
SCP-343 wasn’t just breaking containment
- he now seemed to be breaking the laws of

03:04:26.340 --> 03:04:28.250
physics in the facility.

03:04:28.250 --> 03:04:34.020
The rules of the SCP containment facility
didn’t seem to be a concern to SCP-343,

03:04:34.020 --> 03:04:38.050
but there was one thing he didn’t seem to
want to do - escape.

03:04:38.050 --> 03:04:43.529
After every sudden exit, he would always return
to his personal cell and treat it as his home.

03:04:43.529 --> 03:04:48.359
When interviewed by staff members, he was
polite but vague, and everyone seemed to enjoy

03:04:48.359 --> 03:04:49.470
talking to him.

03:04:49.470 --> 03:04:54.930
It was decided to keep him on site, not attempt
to increase his security, but restrict access

03:04:54.930 --> 03:04:59.860
and keep his room guarded at all times to
ensure only researchers with Level 3 access

03:04:59.860 --> 03:05:02.520
and above were allowed to meet with him.

03:05:02.520 --> 03:05:05.680
But God works in mysterious ways.

03:05:05.680 --> 03:05:11.550
Minimal Security Site 17 was one of the less-restrictive
SCP containment sites, hosting anomalies that

03:05:11.550 --> 03:05:15.989
could be safely contained and weren’t likely
to mount violent escapes.

03:05:15.989 --> 03:05:21.630
But as in every SCP facility, security was
still taken seriously and only those with

03:05:21.630 --> 03:05:24.529
proper clearance could interact with the subjects.

03:05:24.529 --> 03:05:28.330
So why did SCP-343 seem impossible to guard?

03:05:28.330 --> 03:05:32.680
While only Level 3 clearance and above were
allowed in, the guards assigned to protect

03:05:32.680 --> 03:05:36.220
the entrance all seemed to fall down on the
job.

03:05:36.220 --> 03:05:41.100
Security Officer James, who was supposed to
be keeping people out of SCP-343’s cell,

03:05:41.100 --> 03:05:46.359
had instead let in multiple visitors in addition
to dropping in several times himself.

03:05:46.359 --> 03:05:50.910
When questioned on why he had gone against
orders and done so, he simply replied that

03:05:50.910 --> 03:05:56.100
343 seemed lonely and was so happy every time
he got company that it just seemed like the

03:05:56.100 --> 03:05:57.530
right thing to do.

03:05:57.530 --> 03:06:01.920
The security guard was reassigned and new
ones were brought in - but history repeated

03:06:01.920 --> 03:06:03.140
itself.

03:06:03.140 --> 03:06:08.100
Guards were given stricter instructions to
minimize exposure - but SCP-343’s presence

03:06:08.100 --> 03:06:10.859
always seemed to influence them anyway.

03:06:10.859 --> 03:06:15.279
His containment cell was a revolving door,
with staff members at the facility entering

03:06:15.279 --> 03:06:17.580
regularly for friendly conversations.

03:06:17.580 --> 03:06:22.140
Dr. Beck decided it was time to take matters
into his own hands.

03:06:22.140 --> 03:06:28.350
He would meet with SCP-343 one-on-one and
express how dangerous these security breaches

03:06:28.350 --> 03:06:29.350
were.

03:06:29.350 --> 03:06:33.060
He would try to convince the mysterious being
that he needed to stop influencing the minds

03:06:33.060 --> 03:06:37.989
of the guards watching him, or the facility
would have to look into new measures to contain

03:06:37.989 --> 03:06:38.989
him.

03:06:38.989 --> 03:06:44.430
Dr. Beck entered the containment cell and
had a long conversation with SCP-343, and

03:06:44.430 --> 03:06:49.130
when he emerged...he had a big smile on his
face, like he had just finished a reunion

03:06:49.130 --> 03:06:50.310
with an old friend.

03:06:50.310 --> 03:06:54.680
He gave the current guard a friendly clap
on the back, and told him not to worry so

03:06:54.680 --> 03:06:56.340
much about security.

03:06:56.340 --> 03:07:00.120
After all, nothing bad was going to happen
from letting people at the facility visit

03:07:00.120 --> 03:07:01.359
SCP-343, right?

03:07:01.359 --> 03:07:04.060
He wasn’t dangerous in any way.

03:07:04.060 --> 03:07:08.189
He also said that security should bring him
anything he requests so he would feel less

03:07:08.189 --> 03:07:10.199
need to leave his cell.

03:07:10.199 --> 03:07:15.930
Minimal Security Site 17 soon became a model
SCP facility, with morale being the highest

03:07:15.930 --> 03:07:20.710
of any site - with most giving the credit
to the presence of SCP-343.

03:07:20.710 --> 03:07:25.859
Employees generally make daily visits to his
chambers, and he seems to have an encyclopedic

03:07:25.859 --> 03:07:30.579
knowledge of anything they want to talk about
- including things he should have no way of

03:07:30.579 --> 03:07:31.590
knowing.

03:07:31.590 --> 03:07:35.970
Guards no longer quit their posts or break
protocol, as their only real duty is to keep

03:07:35.970 --> 03:07:41.810
track of who meets with SCP-343 so they can
be interviewed and debriefed after.

03:07:41.810 --> 03:07:45.820
Everyone’s conversation is different, but
they all report being in a better mood after

03:07:45.820 --> 03:07:48.050
leaving than when they came in.

03:07:48.050 --> 03:07:54.680
No further information is available on SCP-343’s
origins, the full extent of his powers, or

03:07:54.680 --> 03:07:59.140
whether he is telling the truth about being
the God who created the universe.

03:07:59.140 --> 03:08:02.699
The site director rubbed his temples after
hearing the researcher’s explanation.

03:08:02.699 --> 03:08:07.630
“So what you’re telling me is that we
have an uncontained, highly powerful SCP that

03:08:07.630 --> 03:08:12.160
has not only been breaking containment whenever
it wants, but has managed to destroy all the

03:08:12.160 --> 03:08:14.590
files regarding the research on it?”

03:08:14.590 --> 03:08:16.710
The researcher’s answer was yes.

03:08:16.710 --> 03:08:21.391
However, the situation at Site 17 seemed to
be stable, and they had come up with a plan

03:08:21.391 --> 03:08:26.779
that should help to maximize the positive
effect SCP-343 has on the facility.

03:08:26.779 --> 03:08:31.130
They were even hypothesizing that staff from
other sites and even certain anomalies could

03:08:31.130 --> 03:08:33.990
be pacified by 343’s presence.

03:08:33.990 --> 03:08:35.950
The site director wasn’t impressed though.

03:08:35.950 --> 03:08:40.050
He wanted the researcher to go back to the
drawing board and redo the research.

03:08:40.050 --> 03:08:44.170
After all, if all the files were blank, how
could they ever learn how to properly contain

03:08:44.170 --> 03:08:45.170
it?

03:08:45.170 --> 03:08:48.680
That’s what the C in SCP stood for after
all - containment.

03:08:48.680 --> 03:08:52.360
The researcher finally had to stand up to
the director though, and told them that it

03:08:52.360 --> 03:08:53.819
wasn’t a good idea.

03:08:53.819 --> 03:08:58.300
That they had already tried everything to
contain SCP-343, but that it wasn’t that

03:08:58.300 --> 03:09:03.069
he broke containment, it was as if he didn’t
even acknowledge that an attempt had been

03:09:03.069 --> 03:09:04.449
made to contain him.

03:09:04.449 --> 03:09:09.649
He was omnipotent, aware of things he shouldn’t,
and able to do things that broke the laws

03:09:09.649 --> 03:09:12.350
of physics without breaking a sweat.

03:09:12.350 --> 03:09:17.359
There was no evidence that this was God, the
creator of the universe as he claimed to be,

03:09:17.359 --> 03:09:21.859
but there also wasn’t any evidence yet to
conclusively prove he wasn’t.

03:09:21.859 --> 03:09:26.449
The researcher’s best guess was that this
was a powerful reality bender whose abilities

03:09:26.449 --> 03:09:31.149
knew no limits, and that the only reason he
was staying in the facility was because he

03:09:31.149 --> 03:09:37.189
wanted to, and doing anything to change that
might cause him to change his benevolent ways.

03:09:37.189 --> 03:09:38.479
The director sighed.

03:09:38.479 --> 03:09:42.539
As much as he hated to admit it, his researcher
was making good points.

03:09:42.539 --> 03:09:44.989
He wanted to meet SCP-343 personally.

03:09:44.989 --> 03:09:47.789
But did he need to know anything first?

03:09:47.789 --> 03:09:51.810
“Well, sir…” the researcher replied,
“he likes hamburgers.

03:09:51.810 --> 03:09:53.960
But beyond that, he’ll take care of the
rest.

03:09:53.960 --> 03:09:58.220
He’s right where we left him, in his home
- waiting for his next guest.”

03:09:58.220 --> 03:10:04.420
An SCP Foundation researcher sits at a table
inside of a standard containment cell.

03:10:04.420 --> 03:10:09.520
These are often dangerous places to be, especially
when the SCP you’re supposed to be studying

03:10:09.520 --> 03:10:11.550
is one that you can’t see.

03:10:11.550 --> 03:10:16.890
The researcher is taking notes, unsure of
exactly what’s going to happen next.

03:10:16.890 --> 03:10:22.319
He can hear the sounds of knives scraping
behind, of flesh sizzling and searing from

03:10:22.319 --> 03:10:23.750
high heat.

03:10:23.750 --> 03:10:28.460
He braces himself as a burst of heat hits
the back of his head, as if a fireball has

03:10:28.460 --> 03:10:29.460
erupted.

03:10:29.460 --> 03:10:32.740
Just then it happens - an object floats through
the air and settles in front of him on the

03:10:32.740 --> 03:10:33.740
table.

03:10:33.740 --> 03:10:37.010
It’s a plate of food, and it looks delicious.

03:10:37.010 --> 03:10:41.470
It may surprise you to learn that there is
no rule that the SCP Foundation must deal

03:10:41.470 --> 03:10:45.130
exclusively with violent and vicious creatures.

03:10:45.130 --> 03:10:50.140
Not every SCP held in containment shares the
same malevolence and contempt for humanity

03:10:50.140 --> 03:10:57.739
as SCP-682, or the world-ending threat posed
by the likes of SCP-2317.

03:10:57.739 --> 03:11:03.750
Some - perhaps not many, but some - are benign
and might even seem outwardly friendly, but

03:11:03.750 --> 03:11:09.039
you’d still be taking a huge risk to assume
that anything contained by the SCP Foundation

03:11:09.039 --> 03:11:11.029
is completely harmless.

03:11:11.029 --> 03:11:14.470
Such is the case with SCP-5031.

03:11:14.470 --> 03:11:19.130
As per the Foundation’s containment procedures,
this quasi-humanoid – meaning it appears

03:11:19.130 --> 03:11:24.479
to have some vaguely human features - is held
in an airtight cell that is regularly checked

03:11:24.479 --> 03:11:28.149
by Foundation personnel on a bi-weekly basis.

03:11:28.149 --> 03:11:34.040
SCP-5031 has no need for regular nutrition
or regular interactions from staff.

03:11:34.040 --> 03:11:40.779
The trick with SCP-5031, is not being eaten
by it, since though it doesn’t need food,

03:11:40.779 --> 03:11:46.239
it does still hunt and consume anything it
encounters - human or otherwise.

03:11:46.239 --> 03:11:52.109
Avoiding being eaten is hard enough with creatures
that can actually be seen, but like so many

03:11:52.109 --> 03:11:58.430
other creatures the Foundation keeps contained,
SCP-5031 has developed an almost-perfect defense

03:11:58.430 --> 03:12:04.660
mechanism - which is that when observed, it
will literally cease to exist.

03:12:04.660 --> 03:12:09.000
Some might choose to refer to this as a ‘quantum
lock’, however it is worth noting that traces

03:12:09.000 --> 03:12:15.240
left by SCP-5031 still remain observable when
the creature has temporarily disappeared.

03:12:15.240 --> 03:12:21.270
For example, trails of blood and scratch marks
left behind by SCP-5031 still exist when the

03:12:21.270 --> 03:12:24.069
SCP itself does not.

03:12:24.069 --> 03:12:29.370
Naturally, this makes both avoiding the creature
and capturing it using cameras difficult.

03:12:29.370 --> 03:12:35.250
However, when SCP-5031’s existence ceases
it still casts a shadow.

03:12:35.250 --> 03:12:40.770
From this, researchers have been able to determine
several of the creature’s physical traits.

03:12:40.770 --> 03:12:45.859
Based on its silhouette, it has been deduced
that SCP-5031 levitates about half a meter

03:12:45.859 --> 03:12:52.069
above ground level, it sports an abnormally
small, neckless head atop an elongated torso

03:12:52.069 --> 03:12:58.229
- approximately 1.9 meters long - with three
sets of spindly lower arms that branch outwards.

03:12:58.229 --> 03:13:03.819
Using these arms and its loosely hanging body,
SCP-5031 will lower itself to hunt any human

03:13:03.819 --> 03:13:10.790
or animal that draws near to it and uses the
bladelike tail to cut up food.

03:13:10.790 --> 03:13:16.310
Perhaps the most interesting facet of SCP-5031
beyond its defensive capabilities and apparent

03:13:16.310 --> 03:13:22.199
physical attributes, are the series of nine
tests conducted by Senior Researcher Stanley

03:13:22.199 --> 03:13:23.460
Huxtable.

03:13:23.460 --> 03:13:27.220
Appalled by the conditions that the creature
was being kept in, Huxtable took over the

03:13:27.220 --> 03:13:31.370
role of HCL Supervisor for SCP-5031.

03:13:31.370 --> 03:13:35.930
Having grown increasingly frustrated and empathetic
towards the creature, listening to its screams

03:13:35.930 --> 03:13:41.789
from inside its iron containment unit, Huxtable
devised a series of tests to introduce SCP-5031

03:13:41.789 --> 03:13:47.080
to various different stimuli as a way to better
understand the creature and hopefully keep

03:13:47.080 --> 03:13:51.340
it contained in a way that didn’t seem to
cause so much suffering.

03:13:51.340 --> 03:13:56.529
It's worth remembering that the SCP Foundation
makes it its mission to be cold, not cruel,

03:13:56.529 --> 03:14:01.359
in performing their duties to protect normality
and many of the researchers and staff are

03:14:01.359 --> 03:14:07.380
just as capable of having empathy for creatures
as you might for a stray animal at a shelter.

03:14:07.380 --> 03:14:12.720
The first of Huxtable’s tests involved installing
speakers in SCP-5031’s cell, through which

03:14:12.720 --> 03:14:16.789
a variety of different ambient and popular
pieces of music were played to see if they

03:14:16.789 --> 03:14:19.899
had any effect on reducing the creature’s
stress.

03:14:19.899 --> 03:14:25.910
By judging SCP-5031’s stress levels based
on how much it screamed when compared to normal,

03:14:25.910 --> 03:14:30.540
Huxtable was able to determine how to best
to use music to calm the creature.

03:14:30.540 --> 03:14:35.460
SCP-5031 seemed to convey higher levels of
stress when listening to ‘Morning Forest’,

03:14:35.460 --> 03:14:40.649
‘Deep Grotto’ and ‘Seaside Paradise’
ambience, as well as the best of late 60s

03:14:40.649 --> 03:14:42.610
British rock band Jethro Tull.

03:14:42.610 --> 03:14:47.750
However, the best of Mozart, Enya, KISS and
Ben Folds produced dramatically different

03:14:47.750 --> 03:14:52.079
results, decreasing SCP-5031’s apparent
stress.

03:14:52.079 --> 03:14:56.660
Following this test, Senior Researcher Huxtable
compiled a playlist featuring SCP-5031’s

03:14:56.660 --> 03:14:58.649
favorite music.

03:14:58.649 --> 03:15:04.430
Over time, the stress-reducing effects of
music on SCP-5031 seemed to decrease, but

03:15:04.430 --> 03:15:08.200
keeping the playlist on shuffle seemed to
keep the creature consistently calmer than

03:15:08.200 --> 03:15:10.760
it had been previously.

03:15:10.760 --> 03:15:16.370
The next test involved introducing inanimate
objects into SCP-5031’s enclosure to monitor

03:15:16.370 --> 03:15:19.550
its reactions and how its stress levels were
affected.

03:15:19.550 --> 03:15:25.390
When a softball was thrown into the enclosure,
SCP-5031 immediately sliced the ball in two

03:15:25.390 --> 03:15:27.910
with its tail in one swift motion.

03:15:27.910 --> 03:15:32.130
A similar result occurred when researchers
threw the creature a basketball, which was

03:15:32.130 --> 03:15:36.729
quickly punctured and sliced open by SCP-5031’s
tail.

03:15:36.729 --> 03:15:40.960
Its stress levels first seemed to diminish
when the creature was offered a bowling ball,

03:15:40.960 --> 03:15:45.430
which it rolled around the enclosure and then
later knocked against a second bowling ball.

03:15:45.430 --> 03:15:51.859
However, when one of the balls chipped, rendering
it unable to roll properly, SCP-5031’s stress

03:15:51.859 --> 03:15:56.300
increased dramatically, until a replacement
was offered.

03:15:56.300 --> 03:16:01.029
Researcher Huxtable noted that SCP-5031 seemed
to possess a similar level of motor skills

03:16:01.029 --> 03:16:06.689
to an average human toddler, with similarly
explosive emotional reactions to match.

03:16:06.689 --> 03:16:12.300
Next, when given the choice between two food
sources at opposite ends of its enclosure,

03:16:12.300 --> 03:16:17.720
SCP-5031 seemed to gravitate towards higher-quality
food, most notably favoring cooked rotisserie

03:16:17.720 --> 03:16:19.850
chickens over animal carcasses.

03:16:19.850 --> 03:16:25.420
It even chose this option over a live chicken,
using its tail to cut its food into more manageable

03:16:25.420 --> 03:16:30.189
bite-sized portions, rather than ripping its
meat with its hands or teeth like many of

03:16:30.189 --> 03:16:33.080
its fellow SCPs.

03:16:33.080 --> 03:16:37.569
Researcher Huxtable recorded these findings
and highlighted that, even though SCP-5031

03:16:37.569 --> 03:16:42.710
didn’t need to eat in order to survive,
providing the creature with food of a better

03:16:42.710 --> 03:16:46.869
quality marginally reduced its stress.

03:16:46.869 --> 03:16:51.819
Senior Researcher Huxtable next attempted
to test SCP-5031’s coexistence with other

03:16:51.819 --> 03:16:57.720
living subjects, each time making sure that
the creature had been adequately fed to avoid

03:16:57.720 --> 03:16:59.430
any unseemly incidents.

03:16:59.430 --> 03:17:02.930
First, a live chicken was introduced.

03:17:02.930 --> 03:17:08.090
SCP-5031 rolled its bowling ball at high speed
towards the chicken, increasing both its and

03:17:08.090 --> 03:17:12.560
the chicken’s stress levels, and inadvertently
killing the chicken in the process.

03:17:12.560 --> 03:17:18.670
When a second chicken was introduced, SCP-5031
gently rolled a basketball towards it but

03:17:18.670 --> 03:17:23.109
ceased any further engagement after the chicken
squawked from being hit by the ball.

03:17:23.109 --> 03:17:27.670
Next to be introduced into the enclosure was
a blindfolded D Class staff member, who was

03:17:27.670 --> 03:17:32.430
instructed to sit down and roll the basketball
towards SCP-5031.

03:17:32.430 --> 03:17:36.990
After doing so for several minutes, the creature
began to approach the D class subject, who

03:17:36.990 --> 03:17:40.850
was instructed to remove their blindfold to
cease the creature’s existence and prevent

03:17:40.850 --> 03:17:43.280
any potentially deadly incidents.

03:17:43.280 --> 03:17:49.270
Finally, Researcher Huxtable had another Class-D
engage in a game of catch with SCP-5031 while

03:17:49.270 --> 03:17:52.000
facing away from the creature.

03:17:52.000 --> 03:17:57.399
This test proceeded successfully, and Senior
Researcher Huxtable remarked how SCP-5031’s

03:17:57.399 --> 03:17:59.080
motor skills were improving.

03:17:59.080 --> 03:18:05.489
Albeit gradually, and with some gentle encouragement,
through Huxtable’s tests the creature was

03:18:05.489 --> 03:18:06.779
learning.

03:18:06.779 --> 03:18:12.890
The next test, focused on teaching SCP-5031
linguistic symbols, utilized LCD displays

03:18:12.890 --> 03:18:15.750
and buttons connected to a food dispenser.

03:18:15.750 --> 03:18:20.079
One display showed an image of a rock, and
the other an image of a rotisserie chicken.

03:18:20.079 --> 03:18:25.270
After some brief probing, SCP-5031 was quickly
able to understand that pressing the button

03:18:25.270 --> 03:18:29.120
under the correct display would dispense a
rotisserie chicken for it to eat.

03:18:29.120 --> 03:18:33.770
The creature was later able to adapt when,
the following day, the screen displays and

03:18:33.770 --> 03:18:38.220
materials dispensed were swapped, and then
later set to swap at random intervals.

03:18:38.220 --> 03:18:42.420
When additional rock-dispensing stations were
introduced, this time displaying the word

03:18:42.420 --> 03:18:48.510
‘rock’ as opposed to an image, SCP-5031
was able to determine which station dispensed

03:18:48.510 --> 03:18:51.360
‘chicken’ through a process of elimination.

03:18:51.360 --> 03:18:56.170
Whenever the functions and displays were swapped,
SCP-5031 would find whichever displayed the

03:18:56.170 --> 03:18:58.460
word ‘chicken’ to receive its food.

03:18:58.460 --> 03:19:04.189
The final phase of this test presented SCP-5031
with a single station, displaying the word

03:19:04.189 --> 03:19:08.329
‘chicken’, but with a button that would
remain inactive unless the creature spelled

03:19:08.329 --> 03:19:13.210
out the same word with a collection of lettered
blocks it was provided with.

03:19:13.210 --> 03:19:17.490
After some initial confusion and frustration
as to why the button would not dispense food

03:19:17.490 --> 03:19:23.949
when pressed, SCP-5031 was able to assemble
the word correctly, not only activating the

03:19:23.949 --> 03:19:28.550
button and dispensing food, but proving to
Researcher Huxtable that the creature was

03:19:28.550 --> 03:19:31.319
capable of learning language.

03:19:31.319 --> 03:19:36.130
Huxtable continued to test the creature, encouraging
it to spell words using lettered blocks as

03:19:36.130 --> 03:19:37.770
a method of communicating.

03:19:37.770 --> 03:19:43.710
By increasing SCP-5031’s vocabulary and
the amount of human interaction it received,

03:19:43.710 --> 03:19:50.560
Senior Researcher Huxtable observed that SCP-5031
was gradually learning to sing - albeit nonverbally

03:19:50.560 --> 03:19:55.659
- as well as to juggle with its six hands
and was even communicating its own food preferences

03:19:55.659 --> 03:19:57.640
and dish pairings.

03:19:57.640 --> 03:20:05.590
Later, another Class-D, D-52125, was introduced
to SCP-5031’s enclosure to aid in further

03:20:05.590 --> 03:20:06.590
testing.

03:20:06.590 --> 03:20:11.720
Through D-52125’s instructions, the creature
quickly learned to draw using crayons, and

03:20:11.720 --> 03:20:19.050
created artworks depicting itself, its newfound
friend D-52125, Researcher Huxtable, a cat

03:20:19.050 --> 03:20:21.420
and a rotisserie chicken.

03:20:21.420 --> 03:20:26.289
SCP-5031’s new creative side didn’t stop
there though, as the creature quickly learned

03:20:26.289 --> 03:20:31.899
to play Chopsticks in only two days once a
piano was introduced into the enclosure.

03:20:31.899 --> 03:20:38.159
SCP-5031 even managed to start creating its
own original, admittedly crude, compositions.

03:20:38.159 --> 03:20:44.659
Next, a spice rack was placed inside the creature’s
cell and D-52125 demonstrated how to season

03:20:44.659 --> 03:20:45.659
meat.

03:20:45.659 --> 03:20:51.229
This proved to be SCP-5031’s new favorite
hobby, as it spent the next three days experimenting

03:20:51.229 --> 03:20:57.109
with different combinations of foods and spices,
using its letter blocks to request ‘more,

03:20:57.109 --> 03:20:59.270
more, more’ garlic powder.

03:20:59.270 --> 03:21:05.550
Interestingly, the creature only created artwork
or music when D-52125 was present, but seemed

03:21:05.550 --> 03:21:10.229
to thoroughly enjoy its experimentation with
food when left alone.

03:21:10.229 --> 03:21:16.220
Following this development, Senior Researcher
Huxtable devised a new test for SCP-5031.

03:21:16.220 --> 03:21:22.350
Providing the creature with cooking utensils
and using D-52125 to demonstrate, 5031 was

03:21:22.350 --> 03:21:27.489
shown how to prepare a variety of different
dishes, from hamburgers and tacos, to Mongolian

03:21:27.489 --> 03:21:31.199
Beef, steak, clam chowder and profiteroles.

03:21:31.199 --> 03:21:37.619
In addition to a small peanut allergy, this
eighth test revealed SCP-5031 to be a phenomenal

03:21:37.619 --> 03:21:42.159
chef, possessing culinary skills far beyond
the average person.

03:21:42.159 --> 03:21:46.579
The creature quickly and enthusiastically
embraced its newfound talents, concocting

03:21:46.579 --> 03:21:52.810
its very own brand-new recipes, with D-52125
even volunteering to be the first to taste

03:21:52.810 --> 03:21:55.319
test 5031’s dishes.

03:21:55.319 --> 03:22:02.409
It was shortly after this test that SCP-5031
spoke its very first word, and it should come

03:22:02.409 --> 03:22:05.989
as no surprise that the word was ‘salt’.

03:22:05.989 --> 03:22:10.109
Naturally, Senior Researcher Huxtable was
very proud of the progress the creature had

03:22:10.109 --> 03:22:12.180
made with its development.

03:22:12.180 --> 03:22:15.560
The final test almost seemed to be what the
creature was born for.

03:22:15.560 --> 03:22:21.449
Over the course of two months, SCP-5031 was
tasked with creating a full three-course meal

03:22:21.449 --> 03:22:25.460
which would then be served to Foundation staff
for Thanksgiving.

03:22:25.460 --> 03:22:31.229
SCP-5031 not only rose to the task, but exceeded
all of Researcher Huxtable’s expectations,

03:22:31.229 --> 03:22:35.979
creating a meal that even Gordon Ramsey would
be hard pressed to find fault with.

03:22:35.979 --> 03:22:41.560
The creature created a first course consisting
of sweet potato miso soup seasoned with turmeric.

03:22:41.560 --> 03:22:46.369
Next came a beautiful duck confit, glazed
luxuriously with apple cider and topped generously

03:22:46.369 --> 03:22:50.970
with sweet cranberry compote, paired with
a side of butternut squash gnocchi and served

03:22:50.970 --> 03:22:53.770
on a bed of kale seasoned with truffle salt.

03:22:53.770 --> 03:22:59.000
The grand finale of the exquisite meal was
a spiced cassava pie for dessert, complemented

03:22:59.000 --> 03:23:03.140
with the finest French vanilla ice cream and
a maple-hazelnut syrup.

03:23:03.140 --> 03:23:10.140
And SCP-5031 didn’t stop there, the creature
also debuted one of its original musical compositions

03:23:10.140 --> 03:23:13.189
to compliment the decadent meal it had created.

03:23:13.189 --> 03:23:19.350
As the staff enjoyed the food, SCP-5031 performed
live from its enclosure the deeply moving

03:23:19.350 --> 03:23:25.810
Piano Concerto for Six Hands, to an overwhelmingly
positive response from not only Senior Researcher

03:23:25.810 --> 03:23:29.250
Huxtable, but the entire Foundation staff.

03:23:29.250 --> 03:23:33.579
As a fitting end to the creature’s tale,
Huxtable reported that, during the Thanksgiving

03:23:33.579 --> 03:23:39.989
banquet it had created, SCP-5031’s stress
levels reduced entirely.

03:23:39.989 --> 03:23:45.079
New kinder containment measures that would
keep 5031 safer but also far more contented

03:23:45.079 --> 03:23:47.350
were submitted for approval.

03:23:47.350 --> 03:23:51.819
Perhaps some of you may find it refreshing
to learn that SCP-5031 isn’t simply just

03:23:51.819 --> 03:23:55.989
another malicious, malevolent monster that
the Foundation has to keep under lock and

03:23:55.989 --> 03:23:58.670
key for the safety of the world.

03:23:58.670 --> 03:24:04.710
Instead, SCP-5031 is a gentle – if a little
frightening at first creature - that just

03:24:04.710 --> 03:24:10.920
requires careful and considered guidance instead
of a cold iron cage and around-the-clock armed

03:24:10.920 --> 03:24:11.920
guards.

03:24:11.920 --> 03:24:16.479
Through testing, Senior Researcher Stanley
Huxtable and his fellow Foundation staff were

03:24:16.479 --> 03:24:21.851
not only able to help the creature develop,
but also found what makes it tick; and not

03:24:21.851 --> 03:24:24.390
just for the purposes of containing it.

03:24:24.390 --> 03:24:30.880
Instead, it is hoped that SCP-5031’s creativity
and flair for culinary and musical masterpieces

03:24:30.880 --> 03:24:37.399
can continue to thrive and grow, under the
proud watch of Researcher Huxtable.

03:24:37.399 --> 03:24:43.939
In an old house, an old woman gathers her
knitting supplies. This is a special project,

03:24:43.939 --> 03:24:50.790
for a little boy named Tommy she loves dearly.
She knits furiously, and soon the mix of cotton,

03:24:50.790 --> 03:24:55.710
synthetic fiber, and cloth of every color
turn from raw materials into something else

03:24:55.710 --> 03:25:02.140
- a teddy bear. She puts the finishing touches
on the bear - this is a very special bear,

03:25:02.140 --> 03:25:07.530
after all, and sends the patchwork bear off
to its destination with a red get-well card.

03:25:07.530 --> 03:25:12.300
The card is labeled “Kairos the Bear”,
and inside she writes a personal note.

03:25:12.300 --> 03:25:13.409
“To Tommy,

03:25:13.409 --> 03:25:15.790
Because only time can mend all wounds.

03:25:15.790 --> 03:25:17.210
Love, Grammy”

03:25:17.210 --> 03:25:21.390
But this package full of love would never
reach its destination.

03:25:21.390 --> 03:25:27.220
SCP-2295 was found at the site of a crashed
mail truck, and it looks exactly like a standard

03:25:27.220 --> 03:25:32.729
handmade teddy bear - with one difference.
On the left side of its chest, just under

03:25:32.729 --> 03:25:39.449
its jaunty tan bow, it wears a heart shaped
pin. But not a standard cartoon heart - this

03:25:39.449 --> 03:25:45.060
is a disturbingly realistic, anatomically
correct pin of a heart organ. And that’s

03:25:45.060 --> 03:25:50.550
because SCP-2295 has a specific purpose - and
it’s one that has everything to do with

03:25:50.550 --> 03:25:53.109
actual human organs.

03:25:53.109 --> 03:25:59.090
SCP-2295 spends most of its time completely
inert, spending its days as just another cuddly

03:25:59.090 --> 03:26:04.819
stuffed toy. Tests performed on the toy revealed
it had no unusual properties and seems to

03:26:04.819 --> 03:26:11.250
be a normal handmade keepsake - that is, until
someone is injured in its presence. Not any

03:26:11.250 --> 03:26:16.329
injury will do, a paper cut or even a broken
arm for example won’t do much to activate

03:26:16.329 --> 03:26:21.779
its anomalous properties. But if it detects
a critical injury to a human organ nearby,

03:26:21.779 --> 03:26:26.250
it will trigger its secret power - one that
the Foundation is still trying to figure out

03:26:26.250 --> 03:26:32.010
how it works. Because SCP-2295 is a miracle
worker.

03:26:32.010 --> 03:26:36.270
When it senses the presence of someone with
a serious injury to an organ and is within

03:26:36.270 --> 03:26:43.340
two meters of them, SCP-2295 springs into
action. Suddenly, from unknown sources, the

03:26:43.340 --> 03:26:47.990
bear will produce objects including scissors,
white thread, and sewing needles or a crocheting

03:26:47.990 --> 03:26:52.979
hook from its mouth. If there are any crafting
supplies on hand, it will incorporate those

03:26:52.979 --> 03:26:58.600
as well. And then, it gets to work. Despite
only having hands made of fabric and stuffing

03:26:58.600 --> 03:27:03.640
with no fingers, the anomalous bear is still
able to craft what will end up being a patchwork

03:27:03.640 --> 03:27:09.289
recreation of the damaged human’s organ.
Cute, if a little creepy, but that’s just

03:27:09.289 --> 03:27:10.289
the beginning.

03:27:10.289 --> 03:27:15.479
The injured person mysteriously falls unconscious,
and the patchwork organ, which the Foundation

03:27:15.479 --> 03:27:23.130
has designated as an SCP-2295-1 instance,
will disappear. The SCP-2295-1 instance will

03:27:23.130 --> 03:27:28.200
then physically replace the damaged organ
inside the person’s body. It’s unknown

03:27:28.200 --> 03:27:33.070
how this happens, the patchwork organ will
simply appear inside of their body, taking

03:27:33.070 --> 03:27:38.229
the place of the original lung, or kidney,
or whichever organ was failing. It’s unknown

03:27:38.229 --> 03:27:44.739
where the original organ goes to, since it
seems to just disappear as soon as the 2295-1

03:27:44.739 --> 03:27:46.330
instance takes its place.

03:27:46.330 --> 03:27:50.710
Surprisingly, having this new cotton stuffed
heart of liver does not seem to cause any

03:27:50.710 --> 03:27:55.520
harm, and in fact, it works exactly like the
real thing. There are never any of the usual

03:27:55.520 --> 03:28:00.380
issues that come with a transplant like the
risk of it being rejected by the body, as

03:28:00.380 --> 03:28:04.540
the organic tissue seems to have no issue
connecting with the organ and treating it

03:28:04.540 --> 03:28:12.039
like it was there all along. In all instances
of SCP-2295 performing this adorable but rudimentary

03:28:12.039 --> 03:28:16.110
surgery, the subjects have made a full and
complete recovery.

03:28:16.110 --> 03:28:20.989
SCP-2295 might sound like a miracle worker,
but that isn’t to say that its abilities

03:28:20.989 --> 03:28:23.420
aren’t without their own set of complications.

03:28:23.420 --> 03:28:29.660
When faced with two injured subjects, SCP-2295
seems to always gravitate towards fixing the

03:28:29.660 --> 03:28:34.430
younger subject up first - maybe owing to
its creation by a grandmother who wanted to

03:28:34.430 --> 03:28:39.850
heal whatever was ailing her grandson. No
one knows who Tommy was or exactly what disease

03:28:39.850 --> 03:28:44.420
or injury he was recovering from, but his
grandmother clearly felt it was serious enough

03:28:44.420 --> 03:28:50.670
to create this special bear for him. While
SCP-2295 will heal anyone, it seems to be

03:28:50.670 --> 03:28:55.850
primarily a guardian for the young. And it
takes its duties very seriously - even to

03:28:55.850 --> 03:28:57.380
the point of self-sacrifice.

03:28:57.380 --> 03:29:03.680
While SCP-2295 is able to pull some of its
supplies out of thin air, it still always

03:29:03.680 --> 03:29:09.770
needs some raw materials to craft the new
organ, including fabric and stuffing. And

03:29:09.770 --> 03:29:16.199
if there are none available, SCP-2295 will
obtain them the hard way. The patchwork bear

03:29:16.199 --> 03:29:21.189
will sacrifice its own body, tearing itself
open and removing any fabric or stuffing it

03:29:21.189 --> 03:29:27.320
needs without any concern for its own well-being,
in order to craft a new organ for its patient.

03:29:27.320 --> 03:29:32.580
It slowly regenerates its own stuffing, at
the rate of around a gram of stuffing per

03:29:32.580 --> 03:29:37.880
day, but it needs to harvest fabric to repair
its outer layer, which the Foundation happily

03:29:37.880 --> 03:29:42.470
makes available to it, offering it a variety
of patterns and types.

03:29:42.470 --> 03:29:46.880
It’s no surprise that a teddy bear capable
of healing mortal wounds would be of great

03:29:46.880 --> 03:29:52.330
interest to the SCP Foundation, and as soon
it was recovered from the crashed mail truck,

03:29:52.330 --> 03:29:58.160
they immediately began tests to find out more
about it. Could it heal literally any organ?

03:29:58.160 --> 03:30:03.960
Were there any limits to its abilities? There
was only one way to find out, and the Foundation

03:30:03.960 --> 03:30:10.130
had the perfect test subjects - D-Class Personnel,
whose interactions with non-cuddly teddy bear

03:30:10.130 --> 03:30:15.649
SCPs frequently left them with critical external
and internal injuries.

03:30:15.649 --> 03:30:21.110
The first test subject brought in, D-2353,
a thirty-eight year old man who was in poor

03:30:21.110 --> 03:30:27.470
health not due to his work as a D-class personnel,
but from his years and years of heavy smoking.

03:30:27.470 --> 03:30:32.170
His lungs were seriously damaged, which gave
him trouble breathing and made any serious

03:30:32.170 --> 03:30:37.550
physical exertion extremely difficult. He
wasn’t critically injured or in danger of

03:30:37.550 --> 03:30:45.329
dying immediately, but that didn’t matter
to SCP-2295. D-2353 quickly passed out and

03:30:45.329 --> 03:30:50.930
the bear sprang into action. It proceeded
to take two textile swatches, one black and

03:30:50.930 --> 03:30:56.030
one red, and create a pair of fabric lungs
which it installed in the patient. When he

03:30:56.030 --> 03:31:02.270
awoke, D-2353 found he had full, healthy lung
function again, as if he’d never picked

03:31:02.270 --> 03:31:03.900
up his deadly habit.

03:31:03.900 --> 03:31:09.890
But now the Foundation researchers needed
to know how SCP-2295 would do with even more

03:31:09.890 --> 03:31:12.320
complicated ailments.

03:31:12.320 --> 03:31:18.109
D-3542 was fifty years old and his heart was
not in good shape. Not only did he have a

03:31:18.109 --> 03:31:22.890
serious case of atherosclerosis, which is
a disease where cholesterol plaque builds

03:31:22.890 --> 03:31:27.859
up and blocks blood flow and can put you at
a serious risk of a heart attack, but he also

03:31:27.859 --> 03:31:33.359
had an irregular heartbeat. This D-Class was
in bad shape, but that was no problem for

03:31:33.359 --> 03:31:39.400
SCP-2295, who took a collection of different
colors of yarn and a crocheting hook and created

03:31:39.400 --> 03:31:45.189
a plushy heart. Just like the lungs had acted
as if they were completely regular organs,

03:31:45.189 --> 03:31:50.109
after the heart anomalously ended up inside
the man’s chest it began to beat normally

03:31:50.109 --> 03:31:54.860
and performed all the complicated functions
of a human heart. But there was one detail

03:31:54.860 --> 03:32:00.270
that shocked the onlooking doctors. Before
the yarn organ had vanished, the doctors had

03:32:00.270 --> 03:32:02.439
seen that it was beating.

03:32:02.439 --> 03:32:08.789
So is there any organ that SCP-2295 can’t
replace? That was about to be tested when

03:32:08.789 --> 03:32:14.619
D-7894 was brought in. A twenty-four-year-old
woman, she had suffered serious burns all

03:32:14.619 --> 03:32:19.949
over her torso, left abdomen, and right leg.
She was brought in and sedated to numb the

03:32:19.949 --> 03:32:24.649
agonizing pain, and researchers were worried
that they had come up against the limit of

03:32:24.649 --> 03:32:31.830
SCP-2295’s abilities, since the skin is
the largest organ after all. But SCP-2295

03:32:31.830 --> 03:32:37.470
wasn’t fazed at all, the bear immediately
started sewing segments of patchwork fabric

03:32:37.470 --> 03:32:43.660
and layering them onto the damaged skin, replacing
the dermis and epidermis layer by layer. Unlike

03:32:43.660 --> 03:32:50.490
the other cases, these replacement organs
are visible, and D-7894 now has patchwork

03:32:50.490 --> 03:32:56.229
skin, just like her talented surgeon. And
amazingly, the fabric has the same sense of

03:32:56.229 --> 03:32:58.920
touch that her regular skin did.

03:32:58.920 --> 03:33:07.050
The final test of SCP-2295’s abilities came
with D-2723, who was only eighteen years old.

03:33:07.050 --> 03:33:11.399
This last minute D-Class test was performed
because he was showing signs of a severe cerebral

03:33:11.399 --> 03:33:16.329
hemorrhage, the kind that would cause brain
damage in only minutes, and would be followed

03:33:16.329 --> 03:33:22.990
soon after by complete brain death. SCP-2295
sprung to life, but as soon as it examined

03:33:22.990 --> 03:33:28.060
the test subject, it became distressed. It
started frantically grasping at random materials

03:33:28.060 --> 03:33:32.600
around it, as if it didn’t know what to
do with them. Then, it reached inside itself

03:33:32.600 --> 03:33:38.149
and provided a large chocolate bar, which
it offered to the subject, sadly to no effect.

03:33:38.149 --> 03:33:43.699
It then seemed to admit defeat as it grabbed
tightly onto the subject’s leg. Observers

03:33:43.699 --> 03:33:48.460
reported that it was leaking a tear-like solution
from its small knitted eyes as it embraced

03:33:48.460 --> 03:33:51.180
the dying D-Class in his final moments.

03:33:51.180 --> 03:33:59.729
Sadly, it seems that the human brain is the
one mystery that even SCP-2295 can’t solve.

03:33:59.729 --> 03:34:05.520
SCP-2295 appears to pose no threat to anyone
and was classified as safe after testing.

03:34:05.520 --> 03:34:09.779
It’s inactive when not in the presence of
an injured person and has never displayed

03:34:09.779 --> 03:34:14.819
hostile instincts when active. The Foundation
determined that it should be stored in a standard

03:34:14.819 --> 03:34:19.729
containment locker in Site-37, where it can
be kept safely until it’s needed for tests

03:34:19.729 --> 03:34:25.760
or to repair an injured SCP personnel. Access
is limited to those with Level 3 or higher

03:34:25.760 --> 03:34:30.600
security clearance, and any contact with the
bear is highly regulated.

03:34:30.600 --> 03:34:37.979
But there is one element of SCP-2295’s existence
that continues to worry Foundation staff.

03:34:37.979 --> 03:34:44.229
SCP-2295’s full origins and the grandmother
who crafted it are unknown. The note it was

03:34:44.229 --> 03:34:48.899
found with is the only clue as to where it
may have come from, but there are plenty within

03:34:48.899 --> 03:34:54.250
the Foundation who are suspicious of the veracity
of the letter. And they have good reason not

03:34:54.250 --> 03:35:00.810
to be too trusting, because another bear with
similar abilities exists - and it is distinctly

03:35:00.810 --> 03:35:08.490
less benevolent than SCP-2295. SCP-1048 is
also a teddy bear, but it is capable of moving

03:35:08.490 --> 03:35:13.210
on its own and communicating through gestures
at all times. It was initially allowed to

03:35:13.210 --> 03:35:19.510
wander around independently and seemed to
make its home at Site 24 a happier place.

03:35:19.510 --> 03:35:23.239
But then it began to display its own crafting
abilities.

03:35:23.239 --> 03:35:30.039
SCP-1048 is able to craft duplicates of itself,
and while the original was seemingly harmless,

03:35:30.039 --> 03:35:35.920
the ones it made were not. These similarly
shaped bears were made of disturbing materials

03:35:35.920 --> 03:35:43.029
and were extremely hostile towards any humans
they encountered. The first, SCP-1048-A, was

03:35:43.029 --> 03:35:48.270
made entirely out of human ears and when it
shrieked, it caused anyone nearby to generate

03:35:48.270 --> 03:35:54.520
ear-like growths all over their bodies, eventually
causing them to suffocate. The creature disappeared

03:35:54.520 --> 03:35:58.310
- and an on-site researcher was found to be
missing an ear.

03:35:58.310 --> 03:36:03.880
The creations of SCP-1048 only got stranger
and deadlier from there.

03:36:03.880 --> 03:36:10.069
SCP-1048-B was found in the Site’s cafeteria,
where it was moving around in a halted, jerky

03:36:10.069 --> 03:36:15.630
fashion. It then started bursting at the seams
and revealed what appeared to be a human fetus

03:36:15.630 --> 03:36:20.479
inside. When the creature screamed, it sounded
like a much louder version of a human infant

03:36:20.479 --> 03:36:26.899
and its croes caused massive internal damage
to anyone around it. SCP-1048-B was killed

03:36:26.899 --> 03:36:31.659
in the ensuing conflict with Foundation agents,
ending its threat.

03:36:31.659 --> 03:36:35.220
But SCP-1048 was learning deadlier techniques.

03:36:35.220 --> 03:36:41.170
When SCP-1048-C was discovered, it looked
to be a teddy bear made entirely out of rusty

03:36:41.170 --> 03:36:47.119
scrap metal. When it was spotted by Dr. Carver
and targeted by Foundation personnel, the

03:36:47.119 --> 03:36:51.550
creature turned violent and proved to have
incredible strength - jumping through the

03:36:51.550 --> 03:36:56.960
agents who were trying to neutralize it, tearing
through their bodies like tissue paper. Attempts

03:36:56.960 --> 03:37:01.550
to damage it were unsuccessful, and both it
and the bear made out of ears are still on

03:37:01.550 --> 03:37:07.851
the loose along with the original SCP-1048.
Capturing it is a major priority for the Foundation

03:37:07.851 --> 03:37:12.390
- because no one wants to see what it will
create next.

03:37:12.390 --> 03:37:16.680
Is there a connection between these two very
different teddy bears?

03:37:16.680 --> 03:37:22.911
No one has been able to answer this question.
The origins of SCP-1048 are unknown, and so

03:37:22.911 --> 03:37:28.150
is any connection to the mysterious grandmother
who may have made Kairos the Bear. But their

03:37:28.150 --> 03:37:34.369
abilities are similar, with both able to craft
living objects out of seemingly any material.

03:37:34.369 --> 03:37:38.640
They just have very different ideas as to
what a good use of their crafting abilities

03:37:38.640 --> 03:37:45.761
are. It’s fortunate that an anomaly as potentially
powerful as SCP-2295 seems to only want to

03:37:45.761 --> 03:37:51.569
do one thing. To help those in need, especially
those who are the most vulnerable.

03:37:51.569 --> 03:37:54.609
They’d spent hours making the costume.

03:37:54.609 --> 03:37:59.570
The two young boys - let’s call them Johnny
and Max - had always been on the creative

03:37:59.570 --> 03:38:00.939
side.

03:38:00.939 --> 03:38:04.220
Sometimes they got teased for it at school,
but they didn’t care.

03:38:04.220 --> 03:38:09.920
As long as they had each other, they could
handle anything - they were best friends.

03:38:09.920 --> 03:38:14.120
Maybe one day, they’d build great things
together out of concrete and steel, but for

03:38:14.120 --> 03:38:16.430
now, they worked with cardboard.

03:38:16.430 --> 03:38:20.619
Prior projects had included building a rocket
out of cardboard in Johnny’s back yard,

03:38:20.619 --> 03:38:22.569
like the kind that put a man on the moon.

03:38:22.569 --> 03:38:27.479
They also made a box fort like no other - more
a box castle, really.

03:38:27.479 --> 03:38:32.960
The kind that would stand for a hundred years
- as long as it didn’t rain, of course.

03:38:32.960 --> 03:38:36.700
But all of that felt like nothing compared
to The Tunnel Monster.

03:38:36.700 --> 03:38:40.050
To those two young friends, it was a thing
of beauty.

03:38:40.050 --> 03:38:45.460
A fully articulated cardboard monster costume,
meticulously cobbled together from boxes,

03:38:45.460 --> 03:38:51.109
masking tape, cardboard tubes for arms and
legs, and a little twine to bring it all together.

03:38:51.109 --> 03:38:52.109
Frankenstein?

03:38:52.109 --> 03:38:53.109
Dracula?

03:38:53.109 --> 03:38:54.420
Freddy Kreuger?

03:38:54.420 --> 03:38:57.689
Those silver-screen phonies were nothing compared
to The Tunnel Monster.

03:38:57.689 --> 03:39:02.630
They even cut out eye holes in the head, and
drew the scariest, snarling mouth they could

03:39:02.630 --> 03:39:03.630
right below.

03:39:03.630 --> 03:39:07.550
The making was over, and now, they were ready
to play.

03:39:07.550 --> 03:39:11.970
Johnny and Max took the costume down to one
of their favorite places in town: The abandoned

03:39:11.970 --> 03:39:14.010
Brecher Construction Site.

03:39:14.010 --> 03:39:18.970
To many, it would seem like a strange and
dangerous place for two children to play,

03:39:18.970 --> 03:39:22.140
but for Johnny and Max, it was perfect.

03:39:22.140 --> 03:39:27.130
After all, they were at the age where they
had more imagination than sense.

03:39:27.130 --> 03:39:29.320
Max would be the one wearing the costume.

03:39:29.320 --> 03:39:34.030
Johnny helped him put it on, piece by piece,
using extra masking tape and twine where necessary

03:39:34.030 --> 03:39:36.779
to fasten all the pieces together.

03:39:36.779 --> 03:39:41.779
Little by little, Max became the Tunnel Monster,
the transformation was complete and it was

03:39:41.779 --> 03:39:44.520
finally time for the games to begin.

03:39:44.520 --> 03:39:48.869
Johnny ran, wielding a stick as a defensive
weapon while Max gave chase.

03:39:48.869 --> 03:39:52.210
He could feel his own hot breath within the
cardboard mask.

03:39:52.210 --> 03:39:54.330
It was oddly exhilarating.

03:39:54.330 --> 03:39:59.130
He gave a monstrous roar and charged after
his friend, chasing him into the child-sized

03:39:59.130 --> 03:40:02.399
pipes of an unfinished water drainage system.

03:40:02.399 --> 03:40:06.630
It was more fun than anything they could have
imagined.

03:40:06.630 --> 03:40:08.289
Max really got into his role.

03:40:08.289 --> 03:40:12.199
He lunged forwards, grabbing Johnny with his
cardboard gauntlets and tried to drag him

03:40:12.199 --> 03:40:16.170
back into the tunnel all the while giving
low, guttural growls.

03:40:16.170 --> 03:40:21.319
Johnny laughed, and swatted at Max with his
stick like a knight wielding a sword.

03:40:21.319 --> 03:40:26.080
They ran and crawled through the tunnels,
the best of friends having the best of times,

03:40:26.080 --> 03:40:29.130
making the kinds of memories that would last
forever.

03:40:29.130 --> 03:40:32.250
And in that sense, they were right.

03:40:32.250 --> 03:40:36.460
Something they made that day would echo on
forever, but it wouldn’t be something they

03:40:36.460 --> 03:40:38.789
would look back upon fondly.

03:40:38.789 --> 03:40:42.420
If they weren’t so busy running through
the tunnels, Max and Johnny might have noticed

03:40:42.420 --> 03:40:43.930
that something was amiss.

03:40:43.930 --> 03:40:48.700
They might have seen that, even though it
was only 3:00 PM on a Summer’s day, the

03:40:48.700 --> 03:40:50.460
sky was beginning to darken.

03:40:50.460 --> 03:40:56.000
It may not have saved them, but it might have
given them time to prepare for what was coming.

03:40:56.000 --> 03:41:00.329
Max was still chasing Johnny down a pipe,
still fully in character as the Tunnel Monster,

03:41:00.329 --> 03:41:04.560
his arms extended to grab his fleeing friend
when Johnny tripped.

03:41:04.560 --> 03:41:07.829
Max stopped to help him up but something was
wrong.

03:41:07.829 --> 03:41:13.249
When Max helped Johnny stand up, Johnny instinctually
pushed him away, as though it wasn’t actually

03:41:13.249 --> 03:41:14.810
his friend anymore.

03:41:14.810 --> 03:41:17.500
Max stumbled backwards in shock and horror.

03:41:17.500 --> 03:41:21.370
He could feel something changing beneath the
cardboard.

03:41:21.370 --> 03:41:25.479
He was suddenly in pain, this terrible pain.

03:41:25.479 --> 03:41:28.149
Like he was being pulled apart and put back
together.

03:41:28.149 --> 03:41:30.170
He started to scream.

03:41:30.170 --> 03:41:34.050
It was a horrible sound, like nails on a chalkboard.

03:41:34.050 --> 03:41:39.029
Johnny had to hold his ears as the screaming
got louder and louder, but Max couldn’t

03:41:39.029 --> 03:41:40.029
stop.

03:41:40.029 --> 03:41:42.869
He was hurting too much to stop.

03:41:42.869 --> 03:41:43.979
Johnny was crying.

03:41:43.979 --> 03:41:47.990
He didn’t know what was happening, only
that his friend was in terrible pain and there

03:41:47.990 --> 03:41:51.130
was seemingly nothing he could do to stop
it.

03:41:51.130 --> 03:41:55.359
Even Max didn’t know much more than that,
but he thought it must have something to do

03:41:55.359 --> 03:41:56.470
with the suit.

03:41:56.470 --> 03:42:00.149
It felt like it was full of fire ants, crawling
and biting.

03:42:00.149 --> 03:42:03.520
It felt like his body was full of fire ants.

03:42:03.520 --> 03:42:06.630
He needed to take the suit off before it got
any worse.

03:42:06.630 --> 03:42:10.199
But he couldn’t, the suit wouldn’t come
off.

03:42:10.199 --> 03:42:13.930
He reached for the cardboard mask and tried
to tug it off his head, but it wouldn’t

03:42:13.930 --> 03:42:14.930
budge.

03:42:14.930 --> 03:42:17.760
It felt like he was tugging at the skin of
his own face.

03:42:17.760 --> 03:42:22.149
He could suddenly feel everything that brushed
against the cardboard, like it was connected

03:42:22.149 --> 03:42:23.779
to his nerve endings.

03:42:23.779 --> 03:42:26.819
The fear and the panic got worse and he kept
screaming.

03:42:26.819 --> 03:42:29.870
It was a deafening, ear-splitting scream.

03:42:29.870 --> 03:42:35.079
He didn’t know it, but anything electrical
within a 200 meter radius was dying.

03:42:35.079 --> 03:42:36.590
TVs shut off.

03:42:36.590 --> 03:42:37.900
Radios fizzled out.

03:42:37.900 --> 03:42:39.569
Cars stopped running.

03:42:39.569 --> 03:42:43.699
Nobody who didn’t work for the SCP Foundation
would ever know why.

03:42:43.699 --> 03:42:48.760
It wasn’t even 3:30 PM, but the sky above
looked black as midnight.

03:42:48.760 --> 03:42:53.869
Max was afraid but all he could do was cling
to the familiar - he lunged forwards and grabbed

03:42:53.869 --> 03:42:56.130
Johnny, pulling him into his trembling embrace.

03:42:56.130 --> 03:42:58.060
Is he still Max now?

03:42:58.060 --> 03:43:00.020
No, he doesn’t think so anymore.

03:43:00.020 --> 03:43:02.520
He’s something else entirely.

03:43:02.520 --> 03:43:06.640
As he held his friend, Max tried to dig his
fingers into the mask and tear it off.

03:43:06.640 --> 03:43:09.340
They pierced through the cardboard, tearing
holes into it.

03:43:09.340 --> 03:43:12.270
It was agonizing, but the mask stayed put.

03:43:12.270 --> 03:43:14.060
There was no escape.

03:43:14.060 --> 03:43:16.619
He closed his eyes, just for a moment.

03:43:16.619 --> 03:43:18.290
Maybe it was a bad dream.

03:43:18.290 --> 03:43:20.120
Maybe he could make it disappear.

03:43:20.120 --> 03:43:24.279
But it didn’t disappear - only he did.

03:43:24.279 --> 03:43:25.810
Max was no more.

03:43:25.810 --> 03:43:28.069
There was only the Tunnel Monster.

03:43:28.069 --> 03:43:31.609
When Johnny woke up, he was disoriented and
afraid.

03:43:31.609 --> 03:43:36.560
He was in complete darkness but he could feel
the old metal of a rusty railroad track beneath

03:43:36.560 --> 03:43:37.560
his feet.

03:43:37.560 --> 03:43:41.290
He didn’t remember how he got there, and
he didn’t remember Max either.

03:43:41.290 --> 03:43:43.859
Not his face or even his name.

03:43:43.859 --> 03:43:46.810
But that’s alright - Max didn’t remember
him either.

03:43:46.810 --> 03:43:51.189
When the terrified Johnny eventually found
his way out of the old railway tunnel he’d

03:43:51.189 --> 03:43:57.100
somehow found himself in, he was rescued by
emergency services and treated for dehydration.

03:43:57.100 --> 03:44:01.560
Because of the incredibly strange circumstances
of his disappearance and reappearance over

03:44:01.560 --> 03:44:06.590
4,000 kilometers away, it was only natural
for the SCP Foundation to check in.

03:44:06.590 --> 03:44:14.239
But, seeing as Johnny had no memory of where
he was prior to his mysterious teleportation,

03:44:14.239 --> 03:44:17.729
all they ever did was investigate the tunnel
he’d appeared in.

03:44:17.729 --> 03:44:20.640
Of course, they didn’t find a thing.

03:44:20.640 --> 03:44:25.930
The case was closed shortly afterwards, written
off as a kind of one-off spatial anomaly.

03:44:25.930 --> 03:44:30.239
Johnny was given amnestic treatment, and reintegrated
back into his normal life.

03:44:30.239 --> 03:44:34.039
He would never remember his encounter with
the Tunnel Monster.

03:44:34.039 --> 03:44:38.560
But many would, for decades and decades to
come.

03:44:38.560 --> 03:44:43.550
There would be stories and scattered witness
accounts from all kinds of people.

03:44:43.550 --> 03:44:47.760
Maintenance workers doing electrical repairs
on subway tunnels, sewer workers cleaning

03:44:47.760 --> 03:44:52.540
out blockages in pipes, road workers fixing
the asphalt in underpasses.

03:44:52.540 --> 03:44:57.749
The challenge with being an SCP Foundation
field agent is often separating the genuine

03:44:57.749 --> 03:45:04.489
leads from the urban legends and spooky stories,
but the details here were all too similar

03:45:04.489 --> 03:45:05.970
and specific.

03:45:05.970 --> 03:45:11.880
After all, it would be such a strange thing
to make up - a moldy old pile of cardboard

03:45:11.880 --> 03:45:14.570
boxes, getting up and running towards you?

03:45:14.570 --> 03:45:20.610
But stranger still, these incidents and encounters
were occurring all over the United States,

03:45:20.610 --> 03:45:25.210
with the only commonalities being that all
of them happened in tunnels or tunnel-like

03:45:25.210 --> 03:45:26.210
structures.

03:45:26.210 --> 03:45:30.350
The Foundation didn’t know if they were
dealing with one entity, or many.

03:45:30.350 --> 03:45:34.149
Another peculiar factor they observed was
that sometimes, people who had encounters

03:45:34.149 --> 03:45:39.100
with the Tunnel Monster then themselves appear
in tunnels extremely far away from the ones

03:45:39.100 --> 03:45:41.409
in which they first encountered it.

03:45:41.409 --> 03:45:46.239
As far as the Foundation was aware, besides
transporting them vast distances, it never

03:45:46.239 --> 03:45:48.970
actually harmed any of its victims.

03:45:48.970 --> 03:45:53.430
But according to one Boston sewer worker,
Gus Zagarella, when the Tunnel Monster laid

03:45:53.430 --> 03:45:58.930
its cardboard hand on him, he felt the most
profound sense of paranoia and dread.

03:45:58.930 --> 03:46:03.409
He described it as feeling like a thousand
eyes in the dark, watching you die.

03:46:03.409 --> 03:46:09.770
Then, he blinked, and he woke up in an Arizona
viaduct, roughly six hours later.

03:46:09.770 --> 03:46:14.319
Everyone who reported a similar experience
with the Tunnel Monster was detained, debriefed,

03:46:14.319 --> 03:46:16.689
and given amnestics by the Foundation.

03:46:16.689 --> 03:46:20.989
Eventually, they gathered enough data on prior
encounters to accurately predict the next

03:46:20.989 --> 03:46:24.100
tunnel that the Tunnel Monster would manifest
inside.

03:46:24.100 --> 03:46:30.359
A new Mobile Task Force was formed to secure
the creature: MTF Nu-4, also known as the

03:46:30.359 --> 03:46:31.359
"Box Cutters.”

03:46:31.359 --> 03:46:36.280
What they didn’t expect, when they finally
engaged the beast, was that it was no larger

03:46:36.280 --> 03:46:38.270
than a human child.

03:46:38.270 --> 03:46:43.899
It wasn’t some huge, tunnel-dwelling nightmare;
even after all these decades, the Tunnel Monster

03:46:43.899 --> 03:46:47.489
was little more than a frightened, lonely
little boy.

03:46:47.489 --> 03:46:52.489
He growled, attempting and failing to come
off as intimidating to these hardcore MTF

03:46:52.489 --> 03:46:56.109
members, and referred to himself as the Tunnel
Monster.

03:46:56.109 --> 03:47:00.649
When they didn’t react with fear and surprise
like all the others, he became subdued.

03:47:00.649 --> 03:47:05.930
They were able to peacefully apprehend him,
and take him back to Site-54 for testing and

03:47:05.930 --> 03:47:06.930
containment.

03:47:06.930 --> 03:47:10.750
Preliminary X-Rays found that the cardboard
costume hadn’t just fused with the boy,

03:47:10.750 --> 03:47:12.910
it had completely transformed him.

03:47:12.910 --> 03:47:18.340
On the inside, he was filled with crude, cardboard
copies of all the major internal organs, with

03:47:18.340 --> 03:47:22.899
his blood vessels and nerve endings made out
of colored pieces of string.

03:47:22.899 --> 03:47:27.210
They couldn’t find any information on who
the boy once was, if he had ever been a boy

03:47:27.210 --> 03:47:32.560
at all, and he was given the designation SCP-3663.

03:47:32.560 --> 03:47:38.850
In order to find out more, one of the leading
researchers on the SCP-3663 case, Researcher

03:47:38.850 --> 03:47:42.430
Doyle, decided to conduct an interview with
the Tunnel Monster.

03:47:42.430 --> 03:47:46.770
It has been the only interview with the creature
to date, due to the emotional distress it

03:47:46.770 --> 03:47:48.300
caused the creature.

03:47:48.300 --> 03:47:52.649
When asked about its identity, it replied
with only, “The tunnel monster.”

03:47:52.649 --> 03:47:56.569
When asked why it attacked and teleported
people to different locations, the creature

03:47:56.569 --> 03:47:59.149
replied, “The tunnel monster captures people.

03:47:59.149 --> 03:48:01.810
That's me, I'm the tunnel monster.

03:48:01.810 --> 03:48:02.810
I…

03:48:02.810 --> 03:48:06.610
I capture people and take them into the tunnels
where I live.

03:48:06.610 --> 03:48:07.670
In the tunnels.

03:48:07.670 --> 03:48:08.680
The pipes.

03:48:08.680 --> 03:48:11.090
I'm the tunnel monster.”

03:48:11.090 --> 03:48:15.550
As the interview progressed, the Tunnel Monster
became increasingly upset, until it began

03:48:15.550 --> 03:48:20.960
weeping through its cardboard face, finally
culminating with it crying out between sobs,

03:48:20.960 --> 03:48:21.960
“Please.

03:48:21.960 --> 03:48:24.460
I don't want to play anymore.”

03:48:24.460 --> 03:48:30.140
SCP-3663 only feels comfortable in tunnels,
and it will teleport away in distress if confined

03:48:30.140 --> 03:48:31.630
anywhere else.

03:48:31.630 --> 03:48:36.579
As such, its containment chamber is technically
the maintenance tunnels underneath Site-54,

03:48:36.579 --> 03:48:38.890
where it seems to have made a home for itself.

03:48:38.890 --> 03:48:44.170
Occasionally, if it experiences fear, damage,
or stress, it may demanifest and appear in

03:48:44.170 --> 03:48:45.170
tunnels elsewhere.

03:48:45.170 --> 03:48:50.619
At that point, the Box Cutters are deployed
to collect 3663 once again and bring him back

03:48:50.619 --> 03:48:52.329
to Site-54.

03:48:52.329 --> 03:48:58.050
So far, there has only been one major containment
breach with SCP-3663, but it was a little

03:48:58.050 --> 03:49:03.060
more deadly than you might expect for a boy-sized
creature made of cardboard.

03:49:03.060 --> 03:49:07.800
The Tunnel Monster escaped from the Site-54
tunnels, and began wailing in pain.

03:49:07.800 --> 03:49:13.329
It went positively berserk, attacking surrounding
staff and trashing parts of the facility.

03:49:13.329 --> 03:49:17.710
Anyone who heard the wails of the Tunnel Monster
reported becoming extremely psychologically

03:49:17.710 --> 03:49:19.020
disturbed by them.

03:49:19.020 --> 03:49:23.749
During this four hour rampage, the monster
also tried multiple times to destroy itself

03:49:23.749 --> 03:49:27.829
with various implements, but was unsuccessful.

03:49:27.829 --> 03:49:33.500
After SCP-3663 was recontined, two deceased
members of personnel were recovered from the

03:49:33.500 --> 03:49:34.500
scene.

03:49:34.500 --> 03:49:38.479
Autopsies showed the cause of death was a
buildup of paper residue and wood pulp in

03:49:38.479 --> 03:49:43.729
all of their major blood vessels, as well
as sinuses, ear tubes, and the majority of

03:49:43.729 --> 03:49:46.560
the digestive and respiratory systems.

03:49:46.560 --> 03:49:50.239
A number of other staff members were found
to have been affected to a lesser degree,

03:49:50.239 --> 03:49:53.539
but are expected to make full recoveries.

03:49:53.539 --> 03:49:56.789
What triggered this explosive and deadly outburst?

03:49:56.789 --> 03:50:00.560
Not even the Tunnel Monster itself knew the
answer to that question.

03:50:00.560 --> 03:50:01.590
But we do.

03:50:01.590 --> 03:50:08.109
At exactly the same time, a 79 year old man
passed away from natural causes after what

03:50:08.109 --> 03:50:11.539
seemed like a thoroughly unremarkable life.

03:50:11.539 --> 03:50:14.859
That man’s name was Johnny.

03:50:14.859 --> 03:50:19.720
Think back to your childhood, and ask yourself:
what was the most pain you ever felt while

03:50:19.720 --> 03:50:20.819
growing up?

03:50:20.819 --> 03:50:26.220
As we develop, our understanding of pain evolves
according to our different experiences.

03:50:26.220 --> 03:50:30.490
The older we get, the injuries we suffered
as children like a scraped knee, or a bee

03:50:30.490 --> 03:50:35.100
sting rarely cause us the same level of distress
as they used to.

03:50:35.100 --> 03:50:39.749
Of course, when you are young and unfamiliar
with sensations of pain, what you really need

03:50:39.749 --> 03:50:44.289
in that moment straight after you’ve fallen
off your bike, or tripped playing soccer,

03:50:44.289 --> 03:50:48.729
is someone to pick you back up and give your
sore spot a kiss.

03:50:48.729 --> 03:50:51.600
Perhaps you even need a bowl of warm soup
to comfort you.

03:50:51.600 --> 03:50:56.119
Luckily for you, SCP-348 is exactly that.

03:50:56.119 --> 03:51:01.220
While many of the anomalies held in containment
by the SCP Foundation have earned the “Euclid”

03:51:01.220 --> 03:51:07.319
or infamous “Keter” class designations,
SCP-348 is one of the few considered to be

03:51:07.319 --> 03:51:12.990
Safe - both in the sense it poses no containment
risk, and in that it wouldn’t hurt a fly.

03:51:12.990 --> 03:51:17.859
It is neither an ancient, eldritch abomination
from another dimension spreading its influence

03:51:17.859 --> 03:51:22.319
in our world through memetic stimuli, nor
is it a recording of a basketball game in

03:51:22.319 --> 03:51:25.760
which all the players and spectators are trapped
inside.

03:51:25.760 --> 03:51:31.029
It isn’t an indestructible, limb-regenerating
reptile, or a towering winged being, wielding

03:51:31.029 --> 03:51:34.569
a flaming sword and guarding the entrance
to the Garden of Eden.

03:51:34.569 --> 03:51:37.970
To put it simply, SCP-348 is a bowl.

03:51:37.970 --> 03:51:43.529
A white ceramic bowl, the kind you would find
almost anywhere in the world.

03:51:43.529 --> 03:51:47.270
It may even look indistinguishable from one
in your own kitchen cabinet.

03:51:47.270 --> 03:51:52.430
Of course, SCP-348 is hardly as ordinary as
it outwardly appears to be.

03:51:52.430 --> 03:51:57.040
And it certainly isn’t the only inanimate
object that the Foundation keeps safely stored

03:51:57.040 --> 03:51:58.040
away.

03:51:58.040 --> 03:52:03.120
The key thing that differentiates SCP-348
from most other anomalies is how genuinely

03:52:03.120 --> 03:52:04.800
harmless it is.

03:52:04.800 --> 03:52:09.470
Its anomalous properties do not cause injury
to any individual that interacts with it,

03:52:09.470 --> 03:52:13.699
nor does this bowl have any adverse effects
on the world around it.

03:52:13.699 --> 03:52:19.039
SCP-348 cannot bend or reshape reality, it
does not cause the person eating from it to

03:52:19.039 --> 03:52:24.100
have premonitions of their own death, and
using it certainly does not manifest a contract-making

03:52:24.100 --> 03:52:26.779
entity at the opposite side of the table.

03:52:26.779 --> 03:52:30.239
So, what makes this bowl in any way anomalous?

03:52:30.239 --> 03:52:35.340
What about it categorizes it as an SCP, and
not just a harmless piece of fine crockery?

03:52:35.340 --> 03:52:39.310
Well, why don’t we start with how SCP-348
was first discovered.

03:52:39.310 --> 03:52:44.359
Some time ago, the SCP Foundation was made
aware of rumors surrounding a child living

03:52:44.359 --> 03:52:46.880
in an unknown part of the world.

03:52:46.880 --> 03:52:50.609
According to the intelligence gathered by
the Foundation, this child seemed to possess

03:52:50.609 --> 03:52:55.729
some sort of healing ability, or at least
this is what rumors suggested.

03:52:55.729 --> 03:53:00.289
Upon further investigation, the source of
these so-called “remarkable recovery abilities”

03:53:00.289 --> 03:53:05.340
wasn’t the child, but appeared to come from
a small ceramic bowl, which we now know as

03:53:05.340 --> 03:53:07.370
SCP-348.

03:53:07.370 --> 03:53:12.489
This is not to say that the bowl has any inherently
supernatural healing properties, and it doesn’t

03:53:12.489 --> 03:53:15.989
impart any regenerative power to those that
eat from it, either.

03:53:15.989 --> 03:53:20.489
It does heal in a certain sense, but not in
the way you’re probably imagining.

03:53:20.489 --> 03:53:26.590
When the SCP Foundation recovered SCP-348,
there were no markings on it indicating where

03:53:26.590 --> 03:53:30.250
the bowl came from or who it was manufactured
by.

03:53:30.250 --> 03:53:34.189
The only visually distinct details worthy
of note were flowery patterns that appeared

03:53:34.189 --> 03:53:39.520
to be hand-painted around both the inside
and outside of SCP-348.

03:53:39.520 --> 03:53:44.020
The ceramic surface also bore the Chinese
letters 想着你.

03:53:44.020 --> 03:53:47.029
Which translates to the phrase, “thinking
of you.”

03:53:47.029 --> 03:53:51.300
The child that first discovered it found the
ceramic bowl in the attic of their home.

03:53:51.300 --> 03:53:55.600
The child’s parents were both full-time
workers and seemed to be somewhat neglectful

03:53:55.600 --> 03:54:00.470
of their child, although they refused to comment
on this, but according to the findings of

03:54:00.470 --> 03:54:06.439
the SCP Foundation, the child had come to
rely on SCP-348.

03:54:06.439 --> 03:54:11.439
Deciding to further investigate the anomalous
properties of SCP-348, the Foundation began

03:54:11.439 --> 03:54:12.770
testing it.

03:54:12.770 --> 03:54:16.979
Given that the child who first discovered
the bowl had relied upon it, tests involved

03:54:16.979 --> 03:54:22.899
Foundation researchers presenting certain
children to SCP-348 and observing the results.

03:54:22.899 --> 03:54:24.760
So, was this bowl haunted?

03:54:24.760 --> 03:54:29.899
Perhaps harboring some malicious spirit or
entity that sought to corrupt these children,

03:54:29.899 --> 03:54:33.970
maybe even healing them in order to somehow
use them as a vessel to break into our world?

03:54:33.970 --> 03:54:34.970
No.

03:54:34.970 --> 03:54:39.779
And while it may not have “healed” in
any overt or expected way, it did heal in

03:54:39.779 --> 03:54:42.029
at least a metaphorical sense.

03:54:42.029 --> 03:54:47.840
If presented with an injured child, sporting
any form of minor ailment such as a cut or

03:54:47.840 --> 03:54:51.540
a runny nose, SCP-348 fills with warm soup.

03:54:51.540 --> 03:54:54.390
And yes, that’s right, we said soup.

03:54:54.390 --> 03:54:55.640
What kind, you may ask?

03:54:55.640 --> 03:54:58.079
Well, that seems to vary.

03:54:58.079 --> 03:55:01.779
Sometimes it is tomato soup, other times it
might be chicken noodle soup.

03:55:01.779 --> 03:55:06.340
While the ingredients used in its soups are
often different, there are notable consistencies

03:55:06.340 --> 03:55:08.899
to how SCP-348 heals.

03:55:08.899 --> 03:55:12.830
If anyone between the ages of four years old
and eighteen years old sits down in front

03:55:12.830 --> 03:55:17.579
of the blue flowered bowl, then SCP-348 will
fill with soup.

03:55:17.579 --> 03:55:21.130
Numerous young test subjects brought in by
the Foundation to eat from this particular

03:55:21.130 --> 03:55:25.800
bowl of soup have reported that they enjoyed
their meal, usually finishing the entire bowl

03:55:25.800 --> 03:55:28.510
when permitted to by research staff.

03:55:28.510 --> 03:55:33.840
Many of the injured children that were tested
have stated that the soup they eat from SCP-348

03:55:33.840 --> 03:55:36.170
reminds them of their parents’ cooking.

03:55:36.170 --> 03:55:40.590
These children have expressed contentment
and feelings of comfort after acquiring their

03:55:40.590 --> 03:55:42.710
various cuts and bruises.

03:55:42.710 --> 03:55:47.899
Some even claimed that, even though they were
in a room all alone, they didn’t feel lonely

03:55:47.899 --> 03:55:49.880
when they were eating the soup.

03:55:49.880 --> 03:55:54.430
And the anomalous properties don’t end after
a child finishes the soup.

03:55:54.430 --> 03:55:59.740
Usually, although not always, the bowl will
leave the child a message, often some brief

03:55:59.740 --> 03:56:02.439
words of reassurance or comfort.

03:56:02.439 --> 03:56:07.359
These messages materialize on the inside rim
of the bowl, and seem to be specifically tailored

03:56:07.359 --> 03:56:09.749
to the subject that has just eaten.

03:56:09.749 --> 03:56:13.780
The words will not only be written in the
child’s first language, but are often linked

03:56:13.780 --> 03:56:17.819
to the child’s home life or relationship
with their parents.

03:56:17.819 --> 03:56:23.460
Messages that appear on SCP-348 usually fade
over time, normally disappearing after a few

03:56:23.460 --> 03:56:26.920
hours, or when the bowl refills with more
soup.

03:56:26.920 --> 03:56:32.569
One test of SCP-348 saw a little girl, aged
eight and suffering from a sore throat, brought

03:56:32.569 --> 03:56:34.290
before the bowl.

03:56:34.290 --> 03:56:38.040
According to a background screening made by
research personnel, the girl lived with her

03:56:38.040 --> 03:56:43.479
biological parents, and apparently had a good
relationship with both her mother and father.

03:56:43.479 --> 03:56:49.119
When SCP-348 filled with soup for her, the
girl took almost a half hour to finish eating,

03:56:49.119 --> 03:56:52.970
and afterwards reported that she felt her
sore throat get better as she ate.

03:56:52.970 --> 03:56:57.289
By the end of the meal, this test subject
remarked that she felt completely normal.

03:56:57.289 --> 03:57:00.990
In this instance, no message appeared within
the bowl.

03:57:00.990 --> 03:57:07.210
Another child was brought in to continue the
testing of SCP-348, this time a boy of ten.

03:57:07.210 --> 03:57:12.210
Unlike the previous test, this boy was not
on good terms with his parents and often argued

03:57:12.210 --> 03:57:13.210
with them.

03:57:13.210 --> 03:57:17.930
At the time of testing, the boy had sustained
several minor bruises, the result of a small

03:57:17.930 --> 03:57:21.920
accident that had occurred while the boy had
been out riding his bike.

03:57:21.920 --> 03:57:27.210
Much like the little girl, this subject ate
the soup that SCP-348 presented him with.

03:57:27.210 --> 03:57:30.670
This time though, the bowl offered a message
to the boy.

03:57:30.670 --> 03:57:36.340
The lettering found on the ceramic surface
of SCP-348 simply read “Don’t forget to

03:57:36.340 --> 03:57:37.340
brush.”

03:57:37.340 --> 03:57:41.800
Messages also appeared when an eleven year
old boy with a slight cold ate soup from the

03:57:41.800 --> 03:57:42.800
bowl.

03:57:42.800 --> 03:57:48.050
This child had been adopted by a foster family,
and after eating from SCP-348, he saw the

03:57:48.050 --> 03:57:51.499
message “I’m glad you’re happy” appear.

03:57:51.499 --> 03:57:56.180
Another young test subject, a boy aged six,
had a similar experience.

03:57:56.180 --> 03:58:01.239
In this instance, the child had several scrapes
and scratches from playing with his friends.

03:58:01.239 --> 03:58:05.090
His parents had divorced, and he was living
with his mother at the time of testing.

03:58:05.090 --> 03:58:10.630
This time, SCP-348’s to message this boy
read “I’m sorry, son.”

03:58:10.630 --> 03:58:14.770
A seven year old girl suffering from a cough
was brought before SCP-348.

03:58:14.770 --> 03:58:20.939
She had lost her father to a traffic accident
some time before testing commenced, and received

03:58:20.939 --> 03:58:24.970
the message “I love you” after finishing
her soup.

03:58:24.970 --> 03:58:29.140
Further testing conducted by the Foundation
revealed that anyone over the age of eighteen

03:58:29.140 --> 03:58:34.720
years who attempted to eat soup from SCP-348
experienced things slightly differently.

03:58:34.720 --> 03:58:39.470
Unlike the children, older subjects mostly
displayed a disinterest in finishing their

03:58:39.470 --> 03:58:40.470
meal.

03:58:40.470 --> 03:58:44.470
A common complaint among those over eighteen
was that the soup was “missing something.”

03:58:44.470 --> 03:58:50.810
However, in a few isolated cases, testing
SCP-348 on older candidates still revealed

03:58:50.810 --> 03:58:55.560
messages, although the words seemed to be
faded, not the clear, hand-painted blue that

03:58:55.560 --> 03:58:58.630
appeared when the children had finished their
soup.

03:58:58.630 --> 03:59:03.750
One woman, aged thirty, who was suffering
from a headache sat down in front of SCP-348.

03:59:03.750 --> 03:59:07.920
Much like it had done before, the bowl filled
with soup and the woman ate.

03:59:07.920 --> 03:59:12.170
As with some of the younger subjects, a key
aspect of this woman’s background seemed

03:59:12.170 --> 03:59:14.710
to be what triggered the message to appear.

03:59:14.710 --> 03:59:18.750
Specifically, she admitted to being on bad
terms with her mother and father.

03:59:18.750 --> 03:59:23.170
The woman explained that she had opted to
live on her own, isolating herself from her

03:59:23.170 --> 03:59:24.170
family.

03:59:24.170 --> 03:59:28.160
In fact, she even described having rejected
an offer her father made to her many years

03:59:28.160 --> 03:59:32.530
earlier, refusing some career training that
he was willing to give in order to help her

03:59:32.530 --> 03:59:34.120
secure a job.

03:59:34.120 --> 03:59:39.090
When she’d finished the soup, one word appeared
in the bowl: “Why?”

03:59:39.090 --> 03:59:44.300
Another woman, who was forty years old, was
also brought in for the SCP-348 testing.

03:59:44.300 --> 03:59:48.490
Much like the previous subject, she had moved
away from home and become estranged from her

03:59:48.490 --> 03:59:50.079
parents over the years.

03:59:50.079 --> 03:59:54.749
But unlike the previous test, this woman had
taken it upon herself to not only send money

03:59:54.749 --> 03:59:58.970
to her parents, but also arranged senior care
for both as well.

03:59:58.970 --> 04:00:03.170
Prior to testing, her father had died peacefully
of natural causes after spending his last

04:00:03.170 --> 04:00:06.160
days in the care that this woman had paid
for.

04:00:06.160 --> 04:00:10.579
As the woman ate the soup from the bowl, she
remarked about its apparently “bitter”

04:00:10.579 --> 04:00:14.460
taste, but also described her meal as “fulfilling”.

04:00:14.460 --> 04:00:19.960
After she had finished, the words “Thank
you” appeared within SCP-348.

04:00:19.960 --> 04:00:25.770
One other adult subject that produced a noticeable
result from SCP-348 was a forty year old male.

04:00:25.770 --> 04:00:29.829
The results of this test appeared to be the
most distinctly different from any previous

04:00:29.829 --> 04:00:31.359
adult or child.

04:00:31.359 --> 04:00:36.789
By now, researchers working for the SCP Foundation
had determined that familial history seemed

04:00:36.789 --> 04:00:43.079
to play an important role in the outcome of
any interaction with SCP-348, and this individual

04:00:43.079 --> 04:00:45.499
was certainly different to most.

04:00:45.499 --> 04:00:50.920
The man in question had murdered his father
roughly a year before the testing took place.

04:00:50.920 --> 04:00:55.840
He began the test with SCP-348 while afflicted
with aches in his back.

04:00:55.840 --> 04:01:00.670
After one taste of the soup that appeared
in the bowl before him, the murderer was immediately

04:01:00.670 --> 04:01:01.670
repulsed.

04:01:01.670 --> 04:01:04.979
He complained about the taste, refusing to
eat any more from SCP-348.

04:01:04.979 --> 04:01:09.800
Shortly after, the man began to experience
severe stomach pain.

04:01:09.800 --> 04:01:15.590
The potentially poisonous soup was disposed
of, but SCP-348 immediately filled with salt

04:01:15.590 --> 04:01:19.960
water, which took three hours to disappear
from the bowl.

04:01:19.960 --> 04:01:25.579
Despite conducting numerous tests with subjects
of all ages and ailments, the SCP Foundation

04:01:25.579 --> 04:01:29.930
researchers have so far been unable to determine
the origins of the messages that sometimes

04:01:29.930 --> 04:01:33.040
appear in SCP-348.

04:01:33.040 --> 04:01:37.250
Some have theorized, because of the family
histories of some children and adults tested,

04:01:37.250 --> 04:01:42.380
that the words somehow come from the father
of whoever eats the soup, since even when

04:01:42.380 --> 04:01:47.289
a subject’s father is alive or present in
their life, the message seems to convey feelings

04:01:47.289 --> 04:01:50.420
that their father has, or would have.

04:01:50.420 --> 04:01:56.590
Other researchers claim this is just the purpose
of SCP-348, to provide comfort to small children

04:01:56.590 --> 04:01:59.789
dealing with pain, both inside and out.

04:01:59.789 --> 04:02:06.600
And after all, isn’t providing comfort what
a good bowl of soup, anomalous or not, is

04:02:06.600 --> 04:02:07.789
best at?

04:02:07.789 --> 04:02:12.890
Almost all cross-testing to kill or pacify
SCP – 682 had failed miserably.

04:02:12.890 --> 04:02:17.640
If you haven’t seen it, go watch our video
on the legendary Hard To Kill Reptile, to

04:02:17.640 --> 04:02:21.100
see just how powerful and terrifying this
creature is.

04:02:21.100 --> 04:02:26.390
It faced the Gate Guardian, an SCP with a
flaming sword hotter than the sun – capable

04:02:26.390 --> 04:02:29.970
of tearing your atoms to shreds – and came
out fine.

04:02:29.970 --> 04:02:36.130
In its face-off with the horrifying SCP – 096,
also known as the Shy Guy, it broke the Shy

04:02:36.130 --> 04:02:39.850
Guy’s mind and reduced it to gibbering despair.

04:02:39.850 --> 04:02:46.409
Even SCPs with supposedly unlimited powers
simply refused to engage the beast in combat.

04:02:46.409 --> 04:02:52.840
So, when it was proposed that they test 682
with SCP – 999, a creature known among Foundation

04:02:52.840 --> 04:02:56.779
staff as “The Tickle Monster,” the idea
was considered laughable.

04:02:56.779 --> 04:03:03.270
682 had been burned, suffocated, cut up, incinerated,
and growled in the faces of Gods.

04:03:03.270 --> 04:03:07.369
How could this so-called Tickle Monster ever
hope to survive an encounter, let alone win

04:03:07.369 --> 04:03:08.649
a fight?

04:03:08.649 --> 04:03:12.180
Some even believed that this was the last
we’d see of SCP – 999.

04:03:12.180 --> 04:03:17.340
But what makes this story truly remarkable
is that that isn’t how this played out.

04:03:17.340 --> 04:03:23.899
As you’ll soon discover, 0SCP – 999 is
an amazing and unique SCP in and of itself,

04:03:23.899 --> 04:03:28.770
but its secret origins and its interactions
with some other prominent figures in the SCP

04:03:28.770 --> 04:03:33.739
universe are what make this humble, slimy
creature beyond extraordinary.

04:03:33.739 --> 04:03:38.409
Prepare yourself for the heartwarming – yes,
you heard that right - the heartwarming story

04:03:38.409 --> 04:03:41.789
of SCP – 999.

04:03:41.789 --> 04:03:47.460
Several highly-trained agents on 682 detail
placed 999 into the immortal lizard’s cell.

04:03:47.460 --> 04:03:52.090
Compared to the giant, reptilian sitting across
from it, 999 wasn’t much to look at – it’s

04:03:52.090 --> 04:03:55.689
a large, orange, amorphous blob of anomalous
slime.

04:03:55.689 --> 04:04:01.130
Weighing in at around 120 pounds, SCP - 999
was nothing compared to the monstrosity it

04:04:01.130 --> 04:04:02.270
was supposed to face.

04:04:02.270 --> 04:04:07.340
While its weight has, in the past, caused
minor injuries to some of its human handlers,

04:04:07.340 --> 04:04:12.260
it has never caused serious or long-lasting
damage of any kind to a living thing.

04:04:12.260 --> 04:04:17.539
Even its diet consists only of candy and sweets,
with a particular preference for M&amp;Ms and

04:04:17.539 --> 04:04:18.640
Necco wafers.

04:04:18.640 --> 04:04:23.039
It consumes these treats through the cell
membrane of its slimy body, much like an amoeba.

04:04:23.039 --> 04:04:27.220
This extremely stretchy membrane means the
creature is highly malleable, including the

04:04:27.220 --> 04:04:31.729
ability to stretch and flatten itself out
to a mere two centimeters thick.

04:04:31.729 --> 04:04:37.170
At rest, the creature takes a dome-like shape
around two meters wide and one meter in height.

04:04:37.170 --> 04:04:42.130
The closest things the creature has to limbs
are prehensile pseudopods, those are the arm-like

04:04:42.130 --> 04:04:47.260
projections normally seen on single celled
organisms, of which it has at least three.

04:04:47.260 --> 04:04:50.920
The more you hear about this utterly harmless
creature, the more that matching it up with

04:04:50.920 --> 04:04:56.880
the pure embodiment of absolute hatred known
as SCP – 682 feels downright cruel.

04:04:56.880 --> 04:05:02.130
In absolute contrast to the misanthropic attitudes
of the reptile, 999 loves humans.

04:05:02.130 --> 04:05:04.220
It has a playful, dog-like attitude.

04:05:04.220 --> 04:05:09.250
Much like an over-excited puppy, when approached,
999 will react with extreme joy and slither

04:05:09.250 --> 04:05:12.390
towards the nearest person in order to interact.

04:05:12.390 --> 04:05:17.120
It will leap onto them, using two of its three
prehensile pseudopods to hug the person, while

04:05:17.120 --> 04:05:22.460
the third nuzzles the person’s face – emitting
high-pitched cooing and gurgling noises throughout.

04:05:22.460 --> 04:05:26.680
The creature is apparently pleasant in every
conceivable fashion, as even its odor has

04:05:26.680 --> 04:05:31.010
been reported to smell just like the favourite
scent of whoever is smelling it.

04:05:31.010 --> 04:05:35.420
Examples have included chocolate, fresh laundry,
bacon, roses, and Play-Doh.

04:05:35.420 --> 04:05:39.920
It's almost impossible to oversell just how
beloved and benevolent this strange creature

04:05:39.920 --> 04:05:40.920
is.

04:05:40.920 --> 04:05:44.790
It’s one of the rare sapient SCPs to earn
the “Safe” class, and it’s allowed to

04:05:44.790 --> 04:05:49.500
roam freely around its facility at all times,
apart from a one hour bedtime period between

04:05:49.500 --> 04:05:51.010
8 and 9 PM.

04:05:51.010 --> 04:05:55.920
In the rare instances that 999 has caused
harm to a worker at the facility, it immediately

04:05:55.920 --> 04:06:01.180
began to back away and contract its body while
whimpering in a kind of dog-like apology.

04:06:01.180 --> 04:06:05.020
The closest the Foundation had ever come to
having a real incident with the creature was

04:06:05.020 --> 04:06:09.060
the time someone accidentally fed it a can
of caffeinated cola, causing it to become

04:06:09.060 --> 04:06:12.130
hyper for an hour before becoming visibly
queasy.

04:06:12.130 --> 04:06:15.630
You’ll be relieved to know that it’s since
made a full recovery.

04:06:15.630 --> 04:06:20.569
But what would happen when this whimsical
creature is forced to go toe-to-toe with the

04:06:20.569 --> 04:06:22.760
Foundation’s most ill-tempered monster?

04:06:22.760 --> 04:06:27.210
The employees observing the test watched in
suspense as 999 began to enthusiastically

04:06:27.210 --> 04:06:28.850
slither towards 682.

04:06:28.850 --> 04:06:33.229
It’s no surprise that after being tortured
and almost killed hundreds of times during

04:06:33.229 --> 04:06:37.739
testing, 682 had grown jaded to the cross-tests
it was regularly subjected to.

04:06:37.739 --> 04:06:42.779
When it saw this strange, orange blob squelching
across the ground towards it, it sighed and

04:06:42.779 --> 04:06:44.210
groaned, expecting the worst.

04:06:44.210 --> 04:06:45.890
“What is that?”

04:06:45.890 --> 04:06:48.430
the creature asked of its gelatinous guest.

04:06:48.430 --> 04:06:54.749
SCP – 999 began jumping up and down in front
of 682 like an excited puppy, creating a high-pitched

04:06:54.749 --> 04:06:56.479
squealing noise.

04:06:56.479 --> 04:07:00.770
Just as it regarded all living things, 682
thought the creature bouncing around before

04:07:00.770 --> 04:07:04.100
it was disgusting and hardly worth the effort
to destroy.

04:07:04.100 --> 04:07:06.119
Was the Foundation even trying anymore?

04:07:06.119 --> 04:07:11.340
With a single vicious stomp, 682 flattened
the friendly creature beneath one of its feet.

04:07:11.340 --> 04:07:16.510
Observers were prepared to charge in and liberate
999 from under 682’s claws, but then something

04:07:16.510 --> 04:07:18.479
truly unexpected happened.

04:07:18.479 --> 04:07:23.310
The expression on 682’s acid-eaten face
began to slowly change.

04:07:23.310 --> 04:07:25.990
It was beginning... to smile.

04:07:25.990 --> 04:07:28.921
Observers recorded a noise that they thought
could have been a chuckle, as the creature

04:07:28.921 --> 04:07:32.199
growled and said, “Hmmm?

04:07:32.199 --> 04:07:36.819
What is this…I feel… good…”

04:07:36.819 --> 04:07:42.189
While the observers looked on, stunned at
what was happening, 999 began to slither and

04:07:42.189 --> 04:07:44.670
crawl up from between 682’s toes.

04:07:44.670 --> 04:07:49.699
It reformed on its scaly leg and slithered
up along its side until it reached the neck.

04:07:49.699 --> 04:07:53.359
There, it began to nuzzle like it had never
nuzzled before.

04:07:53.359 --> 04:07:55.399
The results spoke for themselves.

04:07:55.399 --> 04:08:00.449
682 was grinning and chuckling, repeating
a phrase that the Foundation never would have

04:08:00.449 --> 04:08:07.960
even imagined coming from 682: “Feel…
so… happy.

04:08:07.960 --> 04:08:11.359
Happy…happy… happy…”

04:08:11.359 --> 04:08:16.040
Just when you thought SCP – 999 couldn’t
possibly be more adorable, you learn about

04:08:16.040 --> 04:08:18.899
its greatest power: Bringing joy.

04:08:18.899 --> 04:08:23.380
Anyone and anything that comes into contact
with the creature, even in passing, will experience

04:08:23.380 --> 04:08:25.200
a kind of mild euphoria.

04:08:25.200 --> 04:08:29.680
As one’s contact with the creature is prolonged,
this overwhelming sense of joy increases,

04:08:29.680 --> 04:08:32.649
and continues long after you’re separated
from it.

04:08:32.649 --> 04:08:37.609
Prolonged contact has completely cured depression,
anxiety, and PTSD, along with a number of

04:08:37.609 --> 04:08:42.069
other conditions, including rage and antisocial
personality disorders.

04:08:42.069 --> 04:08:46.779
Serial killers practically become saints after
coming into prolonged contact with 999, and

04:08:46.779 --> 04:08:50.489
in that moment, 682 was no exception.

04:08:50.489 --> 04:08:52.979
And there truly does appear to be no exceptions.

04:08:52.979 --> 04:08:58.290
While “causing happiness and joy” isn’t
a dangerous weapon, when it comes to SCP – 999,

04:08:58.290 --> 04:09:00.409
it is an extremely powerful one.

04:09:00.409 --> 04:09:05.310
And what’s more, SCP – 999 also appears
to have an innate sense for those who need

04:09:05.310 --> 04:09:10.030
its help most – with a particular affection
for the hurt and the unhappy.

04:09:10.030 --> 04:09:14.511
The creature appears to be a true altruist
on a fundamental level, even risking its own

04:09:14.511 --> 04:09:17.859
safety to help humans during dangerous containment
breaches.

04:09:17.859 --> 04:09:22.859
In one dramatic instance, 999 leaped into
the air to block a bullet from making contact

04:09:22.859 --> 04:09:24.790
with a member of staff.

04:09:24.790 --> 04:09:29.959
As a result, the creature is pretty much universally
loved by all members of Foundation staff.

04:09:29.959 --> 04:09:34.209
It’s the one SCP who never made trouble
for anyone.

04:09:34.209 --> 04:09:38.999
Back in SCP – 682’s containment cell,
the beast was still smiling and laughing as

04:09:38.999 --> 04:09:40.689
999 rubbed against its neck.

04:09:40.689 --> 04:09:45.890
It was an event so strange, so unprecedented
that the observers in attendance felt like

04:09:45.890 --> 04:09:47.249
they were hallucinating.

04:09:47.249 --> 04:09:52.439
For a few minutes, the monster kept dreamily
repeating the word “happy” but then, suddenly,

04:09:52.439 --> 04:09:56.340
the creature began to enter a fit of uncontrollable,
booming laughter.

04:09:56.340 --> 04:10:00.510
It rolled onto its back, slamming its huge
tail against the door.

04:10:00.510 --> 04:10:06.149
It’d just fallen victim to one of 999’s
favorite pastimes: Tickle Fights, hence how

04:10:06.149 --> 04:10:09.739
it earned its Tickle Monster nickname among
staff.

04:10:09.739 --> 04:10:14.680
The tickle fight continued until 682 appeared
to tire and fall asleep, with a smile still

04:10:14.680 --> 04:10:16.410
on its face.

04:10:16.410 --> 04:10:21.199
After fifteen minutes of inactivity, two D-Class
personnel were commanded to enter and retrieve

04:10:21.199 --> 04:10:23.520
SCP – 999 from the containment cell.

04:10:23.520 --> 04:10:29.410
They did so successfully, but as soon as 999
was removed, 682 roused from its slumber and

04:10:29.410 --> 04:10:33.700
released a powerful psychic attack from its
entire body while laughing maniacally.

04:10:33.700 --> 04:10:38.590
It rendered all personnel within a certain
distance incapacitated as they collapsed in

04:10:38.590 --> 04:10:43.380
fits of laughter, allowing 682 to escape and
go on a violent rampage.

04:10:43.380 --> 04:10:48.579
However, in spite of this, 999 showed no fear,
and helped save some of the bystanders as

04:10:48.579 --> 04:10:52.359
security officers subdued and recaptured 682.

04:10:52.359 --> 04:10:58.739
And even after all this, 999 showed no hard
feelings towards 682, and indicated a desire

04:10:58.739 --> 04:10:59.739
to play again.

04:10:59.739 --> 04:11:03.939
It’s a creature whose capacity for love
is so limitless that it’s practically immune

04:11:03.939 --> 04:11:05.250
to fear.

04:11:05.250 --> 04:11:10.670
Which is all well and good, because the true
enemy that 999 is destined to face is infinitely

04:11:10.670 --> 04:11:15.550
more powerful and terrifying than 682 could
ever hope to be.

04:11:15.550 --> 04:11:19.539
What is this monster, and why should 999 have
to face it someday?

04:11:19.539 --> 04:11:25.159
The answers to these questions all lie in
the true origins of SCP – 999, available

04:11:25.159 --> 04:11:27.590
only to those with level 5 clearance and beyond.

04:11:27.590 --> 04:11:32.609
It’s a perfect example of how something
good can come from the darkest places…

04:11:32.609 --> 04:11:37.239
There would be no SCP – 999 without SCP
– 231 – 7.

04:11:37.239 --> 04:11:42.899
SCP – 231 was a collection of seven girls,
all impregnated by horrific nightmares in

04:11:42.899 --> 04:11:47.770
a ritual performed by a cult known as the
Children of the Scarlet King.

04:11:47.770 --> 04:11:52.420
Each of these girls, over the years that followed,
gave birth to some of the most horrific monsters

04:11:52.420 --> 04:11:58.569
imaginable – one of which, according to
some, was SCP – 682.

04:11:58.569 --> 04:12:03.479
These beings were manifested by the Scarlet
King, a powerful interdimensional nightmare

04:12:03.479 --> 04:12:07.569
God, believed to be behind a great deal of
the darkness and horror present within our

04:12:07.569 --> 04:12:09.880
and many other dimensions.

04:12:09.880 --> 04:12:13.600
Foundation higher-ups have declared the Scarlet
King to be the greatest existing threat to

04:12:13.600 --> 04:12:21.340
the Multiverse at large, and SCP – 231 was
his latest direct interaction with our universe.

04:12:21.340 --> 04:12:27.960
The only surviving member of SCP – 231,
SCP – 231 – 7, gave birth in secret.

04:12:27.960 --> 04:12:33.920
But she didn’t give birth to a monster – she
gave birth to SCP – 999, a being of pure

04:12:33.920 --> 04:12:34.920
goodness.

04:12:34.920 --> 04:12:41.699
That’s right: The nicest, kindest, cuddliest
SCP of all is the direct descendent of a being

04:12:41.699 --> 04:12:44.750
that’s essentially the Dark God of all evil.

04:12:44.750 --> 04:12:47.670
Feel free to take a moment to absorb that.

04:12:47.670 --> 04:12:52.040
The creature even healed the girl who birthed
it, and allowed her to return to normal life

04:12:52.040 --> 04:12:53.939
with her family once more.

04:12:53.939 --> 04:12:59.569
From its first moments, SCP - 999 was making
positive changes to the world around it.

04:12:59.569 --> 04:13:03.680
And according to ancient texts from a Scarlet
King-aligned culture known as the Daevas,

04:13:03.680 --> 04:13:09.760
SCP – 999 is still very much in its infancy,
yet it already has the power to pacify its

04:13:09.760 --> 04:13:12.959
monstrous siblings like the aforementioned
682.

04:13:12.959 --> 04:13:17.680
It’s believed, according to some prophecies
and Foundation theories, that the power of

04:13:17.680 --> 04:13:22.569
SCP – 999 will grow exponentially as it
matures.

04:13:22.569 --> 04:13:23.600
Why does this matter?

04:13:23.600 --> 04:13:28.600
Well, it’s believed by some that one day
999 will grow powerful enough to overthrow

04:13:28.600 --> 04:13:35.069
not only its own monstrous siblings, but the
thought-to-be-unstoppable Scarlet King himself.

04:13:35.069 --> 04:13:39.490
Not through violence or hate, but through
the pure force of happiness and love burning

04:13:39.490 --> 04:13:43.010
out the darkness and purifying the corrupted.

04:13:43.010 --> 04:13:48.489
While the humble SCP – 999 rarely outshines
its frightening competitors, to those truly

04:13:48.489 --> 04:13:55.180
in the know, 999 is one of the most powerful
and valuable SCPs in existence, and may be

04:13:55.180 --> 04:14:00.949
the greatest asset in the Foundation’s arsenal
for the war against dangerous anomalous activity.

04:14:00.949 --> 04:14:05.109
After all, what could strike more fear into
their hearts than the knowledge that it might

04:14:05.109 --> 04:14:10.660
be love rather than firepower that finally
dethrones the Scarlet King?

04:14:10.660 --> 04:14:14.979
And for the knowledge that it may one day
save everything we know from a fate so much

04:14:14.979 --> 04:14:19.550
worse than death with nothing but affection
for everyone and everything, it’s worth

04:14:19.550 --> 04:14:24.949
offering thanks to the little orange blob,
or at least an extra pack of M&amp;Ms before bedtime.

